2026-08-17 09:52:56,886 989962 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/specs/setyagiaz-dashboard-fix.md (attached, kind=plan). Run under /afk — all five phases, no pausing.\n\n1. Investigate — done. Root cause is data/dashboard.html:454 calling send() with one object where it takes (action, args); the frame goes out as {"action":{...},"args":[]} and wsCmd (main.cpp:398-400) drops it silently. Firmware measured CORRECT. Persistence measured CORRECT across a reboot. qmcCali\'s wipe is correct behaviour; its ANNOUNCEMENT is the defect.\n\nCORRECTION made mid-task: an earlier note in this task said qmcCali gives "no mention" that the pointing was wiped. WRONG. src/main.cpp:120-123 has always broadcast "... Boresight reset — re-run @qmcOsStart/@qmcOsEnd." It is inadequate (fires ~20 s after the wipe, says "Boresight" which is not on the dashboard, and names the true-north procedure rather than the Set pointing control the user actually pressed) but it is not absent.\n\nSecond find: docs/specs/set-yagi-az.md:74 specified the broken call verbatim. The bug was SPECIFIED, then implemented faithfully. Fixing only the code would have left the spec to regenerate it.\n\n2. Document — done, spec written and attached.\n\n3. Implement —\n   a. data/dashboard.html:470 — send("setYagiAz", {az:v}).\n   b. data/dashboard.html:465-480 + 307-314 — toast confirms on the device\'s next status frame (tolerance 2 deg = 1 rounding + 1 QMC flutter; timeout 3000 ms = 120 status frames at 25 ms and one reconnect backoff), error toast when nothing arrives.\n   c. src/main.cpp:112-124 — clearedOffset captured; alert at the START names the loss and the right control; console line logged; only warns when there was something to lose.\n   d. src/main.cpp:136-138 — completion message names "Set pointing" / @setYagiAz instead of @qmcOsStart/@qmcOsEnd, and is silent when nothing was cleared.\n   e. docs/specs/set-yagi-az.md:74 — corrected so the spec stops carrying the bug.\n\n4. Observe — four checks, all on the live device 192.168.10.186.\n   STATIC: grep -n \'send({\' data/dashboard.html returns NOTHING. send("setYagiAz" at :470. _pendingYagiAz at 307/308/312/465/471/476/477. clearedOffset at 112/115/116/118/120/136.\n   FUNCTIONAL (real browser, button actually clicked): az 115 -> 200, offset 119 -> 204, toast "Pointing set — now reading 200°" class=success. Repeated at 150 and 250; toast sampled in-page every 100 ms, display=block from the first sample and for all 20 samples.\n   REGRESSION: Seek 210 -> az 212. send("seek2az",{az}) still reaches the device, so the shared send() is unharmed.\n   FALSIFICATION: reverted change (a) ALONE, regenerated, rebuilt, reflashed. Binary mtime 09:48:51 POST-DATES the header regen 09:48:38, so it genuinely recompiled rather than serving a warm cache. Pressed the same button with 300: az unchanged 211 -> 212, offset unchanged 204.0, toast "Set pointing: no answer from the device — bearing NOT set" class=error. Restored the fix, rebuilt, reflashed, re-ran: passes again. The check therefore distinguishes fixed from broken.\n\n   One unexplained observation, resolved: toast_visible read "none" on two early queries. Cause is showToast\'s own auto-hide timer (3000 ms success / 8000 ms error) firing before the Playwright round-trip completed, confirmed by the in-page 100 ms sampling which showed display=block throughout. Not a defect.\n\n5. Track — hashes updated in three specs (setyagiaz-dashboard-fix.md, set-yagi-az.md per-file dict, docs/modules/main.md), check_specs.py passes 2 of 2, commit.\n\nDEVICE LEFT AT: yagiOffset=119 (Peter\'s calibration, restored via setOffset after testing moved it to 204/143/243). Verified live.'}
