2026-08-17 09:58:28,136 989962 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': "seek2az-runaway-shortly-after-boot — UNVERIFIED (seen once, not reproduced, not diagnosed).\n\nWHAT WAS SEEN, 2026-08-17 09:56, device 41 s after an OTA reboot:\n  --- target=300 hold=5s mode=one-command ---\n    origin az         = 300.0\n    outbound done     = az 59  ok=False\n  status at that moment: az 60.0, abs -68815, rel -68815, calAz 241.9, uptime 41\n\nseek2az(300) was issued while the compass already read ~300, so the required arc was about\nZERO. The motor instead ran to 59 deg and the encoder counted -68815 pulses. At the recorded\npulsePerDeg 30.21 that is roughly 2278 degrees — over six full revolutions — for a move that\nshould not have turned the antenna at all.\n\n`abs` and `rel` being EQUAL and both large is itself informative: both counters start at 0 on\nboot, so this was one continuous run from power-on with no intervening reset of relCount.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS: this is a shared rotator on a mast. A command for a zero-degree move that\nproduces six revolutions is a mechanical risk, not just a pointing error.\n\nNOT KNOWN, and I am not guessing:\n - whether it is boot-related at all (the only evidence for that is uptime 41 and abs==rel)\n - whether the QMC has settled at that point — qmc.restore() runs in conInit() but nothing\n   establishes how many reads are needed before getAzimuth() is trustworthy\n - whether seek2az's missing already-on-target early exit contributes. move2az HAS one\n   (`if(fabsf(d0) <= tol) return true`); seek2az does NOT, and task retire-move2az's spec\n   already lists that as something seek2az must absorb. A near-zero d0 with a bad compass\n   read is exactly the case the early exit would have short-circuited.\n - whether this is the same fault node-dash characterised on 2026-08-04 (xsession\n   mt-radar--node-dash msg 0017: arcs >= 56 deg stopping 63-71 deg short). That one STOPPED\n   SHORT; this one OVERSHOT enormously. Different signature, possibly unrelated.\n\nNOT REPRODUCED: the immediately following runs, on the same firmware with the device 68 s up,\nboth PASSED cleanly (target 200 and 90, return error 1 deg). So it did not recur, and one\nsighting is not a characterisation.\n\nNEXT ACTION IF PICKED UP: issue seek2az within ~45 s of boot with the antenna already on\ntarget, several times, watching abs/rel and the @seek log lines. If it reproduces, the early\nexit in retire-move2az's spec is the cheapest guard.\n\nFound while paying the falsification debt on seek2az-hold-return. Out of scope of\nsetyagiaz-dashboard-fix."}
