2026-08-17 10:08:00,985 989962 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-17: "ws feeds need to carry a alert that yagi offset has not been re-done after a qmc cali. my gut feeling is that after a qmc cali is done, the offset ## MAY ## not be the same as before it."\n\nThe gut feeling is correct and stronger than "may". qmcCali() writes new hard-iron offsets and scales (qmcSave, src/main.cpp:88-96) which are applied inside compass.getAzimuth(). yagiOffset is a constant added to that reading (include/qmc.h:121). New constants therefore change the raw value for the same physical bearing, so the previous yagiOffset no longer maps raw to true. It is not merely stale, it is INVALID — which is why qmcCali clearing it is right, and why remembering and restoring it would be wrong.\n\nWhy a standing status field rather than the alerts added by 5a70bcc: those are one-shot WsEventAlert broadcasts. A client connecting after the calibration never sees them, a page reload loses them, and node-dash does not subscribe to alerts at all — it reads the status stream (node-dash/src/rotator.js). node-dash aims this antenna continuously (active-tracker.js:68), so with yagiOffset at 0 every bearing it commands is wrong by whatever the offset should have been (119 in the case that prompted this), with nothing in the feed saying so.\n\nShipped 324e62f. Spec docs/specs/yagi-pointing-stale-flag.md.'}
2026-08-17 10:08:21,998 989962 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'All five phases run under /afk, no pausing. Shipped 324e62f.\n\n3. Implement — qmc.h pointingStale; main.cpp raises it in qmcCali beside the offset clear, and ONE helper pointingSet() clears it, called from setYagiAz, setOffset and qmcSetOffsetNow so the three writers cannot drift; published as yagiStale in fillStatus; declared in /schema; dashboard banner.\n\nDERIVED DEFAULT, not a literal: con.INTinit("yagi_stale", qmc.yagiOffset == 0.0f ? 1 : 0). Every existing device lacks the key. Defaulting 1 would false-alarm on a correct rotator; defaulting 0 would stay silent on one never pointed. Must run AFTER qmc_offset loads (main.cpp:45).\n\nDESIGN FAULT CAUGHT BY LOOKING AT THE SCREENSHOT: the banner first went inside the Control panel, where it was invisible from the Config tab the user needs to fix it on. Moved above the tab bar. A DOM element that is display:block is not a visible one.\n\n4. Observe —\n  STATIC: yagiStale in /schema, pointingStale/pointingSet in main.cpp and qmc.h.\n  FUNCTIONAL: /schema serves the yagiStale declaration. Live device: yagiOffset=119.0, yagiStale=False, uptime 20 — the derived default correctly produced NO false alarm on Peter\'s correctly-pointed rotator. Banner verified rendering in a real browser above the tabs, amber on dark, readable from the Config tab.\n  Its first two screenshots came back with no banner. Cause was NOT a bug: the live feed carries yagiStale=false every 25 ms and re-hid it immediately after the client-side injection. That is the wiring working. Confirmed by patching applyStatus to force the flag on every incoming frame, then screenshotting.\n  REGRESSION: two consecutive builds left the tree clean, so 34f7166 still holds.\n\n  DEFERRED, needs Peter: qmcCali RAISING the flag is unverified. Running @qmcCali spins the motor ~20 s and destroys the pointing calibration, and by this task\'s own argument the old 119 cannot be correctly restored afterwards — only Peter can redo it, because it needs someone to observe where the antenna physically points. The test: note yagiOffset/yagiStale, run @qmcCali, confirm the flag goes true and survives a reboot, set the pointing, confirm it clears.\n\n  NO FALSIFICATION for the qmcCali path, for the same reason. The clearing path shares pointingSet() with setYagiAz, which was falsified in setyagiaz-dashboard-fix.\n\nSPEC CORRECTED MID-PHASE: acceptance item 3 as originally written ("setOffset 0 then reboot -> true") was WRONG. pointingSet() writes the key and INTinit only defaults when the key is ABSENT, so the derived default fires once per device and cannot be re-triggered by zeroing the offset.\n\nDECISION (AFK): docs/specs/set-yagi-az.md and docs/specs/setyagiaz-dashboard-fix.md carry source_hash values that this commit staled. NOT updated. A task spec\'s hash records the files as they were when that task shipped; refreshing every spec on every later commit is churn and destroys that meaning. Only docs/modules/*.md hashes are enforced by check_specs.py and those were updated. Reverse by recomputing and editing the frontmatter if the convention is meant to be the opposite.'}
