2026-08-17 12:49:52,005 1549720 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DONE. test-runs-pollute-the-audit-logs is CLOSED/commit — trial f20832f red, fix d28a50e green, tests/test_idiot_trial.py and tests/test_idiot_gate.py both changed between them. Register 20 closed of 23; the commit rung went 7 -> 8. Commits f20832f, d28a50e, 24afa25.\n\nTWO THINGS FOUND THAT ARE NOT MINE TO FIX HERE, both worth an entry:\n\n1. The hook deadlocks any already-fixed defect. `idiot_gate.py` could not be reverted because gate-after-exit-can-be-typed names it and reads untried, and an untried entry refuses every edit to its files. That is correct for the normal flow — the red comes before any edit — but for a defect that is ALREADY fixed, capturing the red REQUIRES an edit (the revert), and the entry is untried precisely because that red was never captured. There is no exit inside the tool except a withdrawal or Peter\'s ruling. `gate-after-exit-can-be-typed` and `run-json-duplicates-idiot-yaml` are both stuck behind it, and both name idiot_gate.py, so idiot_gate.py is currently unmaintainable.\n\n2. `amend` puts an entry back to untried, which locks its own files. If I had amended before making the revert edits instead of after, I could not have produced the red at all. The order that works is: edit -> amend -> try -> edit -> prove. That is worth writing down because it is not obvious and the AVOID rule as written ("amend before proving") does not distinguish it from "amend before editing", which deadlocks.\n\nAlso noted, out of scope: idiot.py\'s module docstring line 4 points at /root/.claude/docs/specs/idiot-trial-verdict.md, and the specs live in docs/specs/ in this repo. Stale path, same class as the eleven.'}
