2026-08-17 13:18:40,928 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'The charts must come from the code, or a hand-drawn chart is a defect count with no test behind it. Peter\'s ruling, 2026-08-17: the yaml is generated from the actual code by a script run in the repo, and `flow`\'s own seven charts are that script\'s first output rather than a hand-drawn exception.\n\n`flow.py` still never reads source — `onboard.py` does. Two programs, one direction of travel, and `docs/SPEC.md`\'s "no parsing of your source" stays literally true of the renderer.\n\nThe seam that makes generated and hand-written coexist: a node with `src: file:line` is derived and gets rewritten; a node without one is a human annotation and is preserved. `drift` compares structure only, so improved prose and hand-added holes survive regeneration.\n\nApproved area list for this repo (Peter, "list approved"): `load`, `check`, `render`, `wire`, `areas`, `cli`, plus `lifecycle` as the cross-area overview.\n\nDone when `onboard.py drift .` exits 0 on a clean tree and exits 2 naming a function added to `flow.py` — that is the proof the loop is closed — and `tests/test_flow.py` no longer needs the `idiot` repo to exist.'}
2026-08-17 13:18:51,384 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: `docs/specs/onboard-from-source.md` (attached). In scope: `onboard.py`, `tests/test_onboard.py`, `docs/flow/areas.yaml`, `docs/flow/*.yaml`, `tests/test_flow.py`, `README.md`. **Not `flow.py`** — it is gated by `the-index-never-says-unknown` and nothing here needs it.\n\nRegister: `no-generator-from-source`, type `new`, files `onboard.py`. Trial first (red because it does not exist), then build.\n\n1. Suite first, red: inventory count against `grep -c '^def '`, draw output passes `flow`'s own checker, draw twice is byte-identical, drift red when a function is added.\n2. `inventory` — ast walk: module-level defs, classes and constants, with kind, line, calls, branch count.\n3. `draw` — read `areas.yaml`, refuse a symbol in no area or two, ast → nodes/edges, 5-row bands per function, `src:` on every derived node, `--keep-layout` reuses `at` where `src` is unchanged.\n4. `drift` — structural compare, ignoring labels, notes and positions; exit 2 naming what appeared, vanished or changed area.\n5. Dogfood: `areas.yaml` for the seven approved areas, draw, render, and LOOK at the pngs in both themes at 1600 and 1024 (`/playwright`).\n6. Point `tests/test_flow.py` at this repo's own corpus; keep `FLOW_CORPUS` as the wider cross-check against idiot's 8 charts.\n\nDerived vs judgement, from the spec: node type and topology are ast-derived; area names, symbol assignment, prose and non-control-flow holes are the agent's and must never be invented by the script."}
