2026-08-17 15:05:09,239 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_project_set args={'name': 'mt-alarm-html', 'description': 'The alarm\'s browser host, standing up as its own pm2 service in mt-alarm-1.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-17: "remove DOES NOT MEAN DESTROY. the intention is it will run as it\'s own pm2 service".\n\nSibling components in the same superrepo, each its own git repo:\n- `bridge/` — live on :8790 under pm2, serves its own OpenAPI at `/schema`. The only route to the LoRa units.\n- `plugins/` — bridge feed plugins (dash, notify, probe). Data only; the bridge plugin contract refuses `res`, filesystem and transport, so it cannot serve HTML.\n- `device/` — RAK/ESP32 firmware.\n- `html/` — this project. Empty but for `docs/`.\n\nThe work is receiving 8 modules and 6 browser assets from `mt-radar/node-dash`. See `docs/HANDOVER.md` (a donor inventory written from the node-dash side, with corrections recorded 2026-08-17).\n\nMANDATORY READING: `mt-radar/node-dash/docs/ALARM_TRANSPORT_BOUNDARY.md` — Meshtastic is the alarm\'s TRANSPORT, never its application. The only contract between alarm and radar is arbitration of shared hardware: which radio transmits, and a rotator hold with a timeout.'}
