2026-08-17 15:08:26,220 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Give the four alarm modules that do NOT depend on node-dash\'s browser-host mechanisms a home in `mt-alarm-1/html`, so that half the move is done and proven before the A/B decision on the UI is taken.\n\n**The four, and why they are host-free** — measured 2026-08-17 in `mt-radar/node-dash`:\n\n| module | size | only core import outside the pure helpers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `alarm-host.js` | 49 KB | `served-time.js` (`scheduleTime`, line 24) — trivial |\n| `alarm-image-api.js` | 8.7 KB | none |\n| `pac-command-api.js` | 1.5 KB | none |\n| `coulomb.js` | 8.4 KB | none (imports `alarm-host.js`) |\n\nThe other four in the moving set are blocked on a browser host that does not exist yet:\n`alarm-ws.js` and `alarm-images.js` need `ws-relay.js`, `alarm-sections.js` needs\n`node-status.js`, `alarm-browser.js` needs `browser-plugins.js`.\n\n**MOVE, NOT DELETE.** Peter, 2026-08-17: *"remove DOES NOT MEAN DESTROY. the intention is\nit will run as it\'s own pm2 service"*. Nothing leaves node-dash until this side is running\nand proven — otherwise the Control page dies in the gap.\n\n**Settled during investigation, so it is not re-opened:**\n- The store question is closed. `stmts` is imported at `alarm-sections.js:26` and never\n  called (its only other mention, `:236`, is a comment). `obs_observation` / `obs_fact`\n  belong to node-dash\'s observatory. No moving module touches node-dash\'s SQLite.\n- `pac-align-api.js` is NOT in the moving set. `applyAlignModel` (`alarm-host.js:322`)\n  has no caller anywhere in `src/` and returns early on `!_sectionOk(\'align\')`. Dead code\n  is not carried across a boundary.\n\n**Not settled, and Peter\'s call:** whether the Control page UI moves here too (a full\nAlpine SPA host per `node-dash/docs/BROWSER_PLUGIN_SPEC.md`) or stays hosted by node-dash\nwith only data moving. This task is common to both answers.'}
2026-08-17 15:09:49,403 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': '## alarm-image-api-is-not-host-free — CONFIRMED, and it is my own Phase 1 error\n\n**Status:** CONFIRMED. Corrects a claim I made to Peter before this task was opened.\n\nI split the moving set into "host-free" and "blocked" using each module\'s **direct**\nimports only, and put `alarm-image-api.js` in the host-free half. It is not.\n\n```\nsrc/alarm-image-api.js:17  import { isStoredPid, isStoredId, isDevicePid, setDeviceImage }\n                             from \'./alarm-images.js\';\nsrc/alarm-images.js:13     import { registerWsWiring, registerConnectReplay } from \'./ws-relay.js\';\nsrc/alarm-images.js:353    registerWsWiring(({ broadcast }) => {      <- column 0, TOP LEVEL\nsrc/alarm-images.js:362    registerConnectReplay(() => [_message()]);  <- column 0, TOP LEVEL\n```\n\nBoth calls are at top level, so importing `alarm-image-api.js` executes `ws-relay.js`\nwiring as a side effect of module load. The four symbols it needs are not extractable\neither: `isStoredPid` `:50`, `isStoredId` `:55`, `isDevicePid` `:62` read `alarm-images`\nmodule state (`_stored`, `_storedIds`, `_device`), and `setDeviceImage` `:69` calls\n`_poll()`.\n\n**Effect:** the movable set is **three** modules, not four — `alarm-host.js`,\n`pac-command-api.js`, `coulomb.js`. `alarm-image-api.js` travels with `alarm-images.js`\nwhen the browser host exists.\n\n**Class of error:** I derived a transitive property from a one-level grep. The original\ngrep (`from \'./ws-relay.js\'` across the moving set) was correct and I read a conclusion\noff it that it did not support.\n\n---\n\n## node-dash-dead-stmts-import — NOT OURS, already raised\n\n`src/alarm-sections.js:26` imports `stmts` from `./db.js`; the only other mention of the\nsymbol in the file is a comment at `:236`. Never called.\n\nRaised with node-dash as seq **#49** on xsession channel `node-dash--plugins`. Their file,\ntheir fix. **Not to be worked around here** — it is why their `alarm-db-ownership` task\nis open, and a workaround would make it permanent and invisible.\n\n---\n\n## node-dash-stale-tmp-file — NOT OURS\n\n`src/observatory.js.tmp.57468.c85d89c9e43d` sits beside `src/observatory.js` and matches\n`grep -rln obs_observation src/`. It made the store question look like it had two writers.\nMentioned in #49.\n\n---\n\n## handover-asserts-tab-control-does-not-exist — CONFIRMED, ours\n\n`docs/HANDOVER.md:142` states *"**no `tab-control.html` exists**"*. It does:\n\n```\npublic/plugins/alarm/tab-control.html   48242 bytes\n```\n\nplus five more browser assets (`app-control.js` 17286, `plugin.js` 5763, `nav.html` 4177,\n`app-align.js` 2589, `header.html` 418) — 78 KB the handover never lists. The claim was\ntrue of node-dash\'s **core partials** (`public/partials/` holds no `tab-control.html`) and\nwas written as an absolute absence.\n\n**Effect:** anyone sizing the move from that document undercounts it by six files.\n\n---\n\n## handover-says-sockets-stall-every-90s — CONFIRMED, ours\n\n`docs/HANDOVER.md:154` says the bridge sockets stall *"roughly every 90 s"*. Every\n`/health STALLED` line in node-dash\'s pm2 log, as of 2026-08-17 15:01 BST:\n\n```\npm2 logs node-dash --lines 5000 --nostream | grep \'/health STALLED\'\n12:47:23.356   12:48:50.903   12:50:28.595   12:54:38.455   13:37:45.560\n```\n\nA four-event cluster, one straggler 43 minutes later, then nothing in the 84 minutes\nsince. Bursty, not periodic. The handover quoted two adjacent lines from inside the\ncluster.\n\n**NOT YET KNOWN:** the cause. Bridge, network, or node-dash\'s watchdog being too strict\n(`limit 30s = 3 ticks`) — I have not established which, and neither did the handover.\n\n---\n\n## mt-alarm-1-not-on-specboard — CONFIRMED, ours, TIDY\n\n`GET http://127.0.0.1:8420/p/mt-alarm-1/` -> **404**. The board is alive (`/` -> 200) and\ncarries `/p/device/` and `/p/specboard/` only. So findings for this repo have nowhere to\ngo but this task, while its sibling `device/` files to the board — the ledger is split\nacross two systems with nothing recording the split.\n\n`specboard.py subscribe` would fix it. **Not run — Peter\'s call.**'}
