2026-08-17 15:26:41,543 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Copy three modules and their four pure helpers into `html/src/` **byte-identically**, add the one original file that boots them, and prove the link to the live bridge — without touching a single file in node-dash.\n\nFull detail in the attached spec `docs/spec/move-host-free-alarm-modules.md`.\n\n1. **VERIFY the import surface** — done. Every relative import in `alarm-host.js`,\n   `pac-command-api.js` and `coulomb.js` resolves to a file we also vendor\n   (`log`, `format`, `served-time`, `utils`), so **no import is rewritten** and the\n   copies stay byte-identical. Byte-identity is the drift check that will later make\n   deleting node-dash's copies safe without re-reading them.\n2. **DISCUSS and write the spec** — done, attached, port derived to 8791.\n3. **TOOL stand up html/** — `package.json` (express ^5.2.1, ws ^8.21.0, no\n   better-sqlite3), `bin/httpd.js` (the only original code: `/health`, mount the\n   command router, `alarmHost.start()`), `.gitignore`.\n4. **VERIFY against the live bridge** — boot, and require `available: true` with a\n   non-null `servedAt`, then falsify by pointing `ALARM_HOST_URL` at a dead port and\n   requiring `available: false`. A health check that cannot report a dead bridge is\n   testing nothing.\n5. **AGREE with node-dash** — nothing is unwired on their side by this task. Their\n   `index.js:470 pacHost.start()` stays. Raising the finished state on xsession\n   `node-dash--plugins` is the last step, not the first.\n\n**Deliberately not in the plan:** pm2 registration (the service is proven by hand\nfirst), any route for `coulomb.js` (it is a library, not a surface), and any GET for\nqueue data (`pac-command-api.js:29-34` records that route as a real bug)."}
2026-08-17 15:26:56,908 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Give the alarm modules that do NOT depend on node-dash\'s browser-host mechanisms a home in `mt-alarm-1/html`, so half the move is done and proven before the A/B decision on the UI is taken.\n\n**CORRECTED 2026-08-17: it is THREE modules, not four.** The first version of this note\nlisted `alarm-image-api.js` as host-free. It is not — `:17` imports from\n`alarm-images.js`, which calls `registerWsWiring`/`registerConnectReplay` at top level\n(`:353`, `:362`), so loading the router executes `ws-relay` wiring. See the `bugs` task,\n`alarm-image-api-is-not-host-free`. The error was reading a transitive property off a\none-level grep.\n\n| module | bytes | host-mechanism imports |\n|---|---|---|\n| `alarm-host.js` | 49723 | `served-time.js` only (`scheduleTime`, `:24`) — trivial |\n| `pac-command-api.js` | 1544 | none |\n| `coulomb.js` | 8411 | none (imports `alarm-host.js`) |\n\nBlocked on a browser host that does not exist here: `alarm-ws.js` and `alarm-images.js`\n(`ws-relay.js`), `alarm-image-api.js` (via `alarm-images.js`), `alarm-sections.js`\n(`node-status.js`), `alarm-browser.js` (`browser-plugins.js`).\n\n**MOVE, NOT DELETE.** Peter, 2026-08-17: *"remove DOES NOT MEAN DESTROY. the intention is\nit will run as it\'s own pm2 service"*. Nothing leaves node-dash until this side is proven,\nor the Control page dies in the gap.\n\n**Settled, so it is not re-opened:**\n- The store question is closed. `stmts` is imported at `alarm-sections.js:26` and never\n  called (its only other mention, `:236`, is a comment). `obs_observation` / `obs_fact`\n  belong to node-dash\'s observatory. No moving module touches node-dash\'s SQLite.\n- `pac-align-api.js` is excluded as dead. `applyAlignModel` (`alarm-host.js:322`) has no\n  caller anywhere in node-dash\'s `src/` and returns early on `!_sectionOk(\'align\')`.\n\n**Not settled, and Peter\'s call:** whether the Control page UI