2026-08-17 15:45:40,679 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': "## bridge-sockets-stall-cause-unknown — EXPERIMENT RUNNING, NO RESULT YET\n\nRead as: set up, not answered. Do not quote a conclusion from this entry.\n\n**Status at 2026-08-17 14:45 UTC.**\n\n```\nnode-dash /health STALLED:  12:47:23  12:48:50  12:50:28  12:54:38  13:37:45  14:07:50\nhtml      STALLED|STALE:    0\nhtml connected since:       14:23 UTC (22 min); pm2-owned since 14:34 (10.4 min)\n```\n\n**No discriminating event has occurred.** Neither consumer has stalled since 14:07:50,\nwhich is 37 minutes ago — and node-dash's longest observed gap between bursts is 43\nminutes. So html's clean record proves nothing: the quiet window is shorter than the\nknown inter-event gap, and both services are quiet across the same period anyway.\n\n**What would settle it**, once a stall does occur:\n\n| observation | conclusion |\n|---|---|\n| the same instant in BOTH logs | the bridge stopped pushing. Ours. |\n| node-dash only | node-dash's socket or its watchdog. Theirs. |\n| html only | this service's environment, not the bridge |\n\n```bash\npm2 logs html      --lines 5000 --nostream | grep -E 'STALLED|STALE'\npm2 logs node-dash --lines 5000 --nostream | grep -E 'STALLED|STALE'\n```\n\nBoth log through the same `log.js` in UTC, so timestamps compare directly with no\nconversion. Wait for a window comfortably longer than 43 minutes containing at least one\nnode-dash stall before drawing anything.\n\n**Still unknown:** whether the fault is the bridge, the loopback, or node-dash's watchdog\nbeing strict at `limit 30s = 3 ticks` against `feedTickMs` 10000."}
