2026-08-17 15:55:04,415 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Five open items, all in `flow.py`, all of them claims the tool makes about itself that are not true:\n\n- **the-index-never-says-unknown** — `flow.py:6` and `:415` advertise UNKNOWN; `render_areas` is handed only the charts that loaded, so it cannot know which areas were expected.\n- **duplicate-node-ids-are-accepted** — `check()` validates cells but not ids; `seen[i] = n` overwrites, the page wires connectors by id, and `derive.py` hit this for real with two functions named `main`.\n- **the-footer-calls-every-chart-hand-written** — false for all 15 charts here; they are generated and drift-checked.\n- **no `-h`** — one usage line, no help, same class as the hook that printed an invocation which did not parse.\n- **`--areas` overwrites the render of a chart called `index`** — and `docs/HANDOVER.md` describes this wrongly, saying `index.yaml` itself is clobbered. It is not; the render is.\n\nRun under `/afk`, so decided rather than asked. The fork that mattered: **implement UNKNOWN rather than strip the claim.** Reasons — `areas.yaml` now exists and is a committed artefact, `dash.py` already proves the distinction is worth showing, and reading a declaration is not reading source, so `docs/SPEC.md`'s rule is untouched. Reversible by reverting the commit; the alternative was deleting two docstring lines.\n\nDone when all five have a test that was red first, `idiot`'s hand-drawn charts still render unchanged apart from the footer, `flow-derive drift` still reports 15 areas matching, and every entry reads CLOSED/commit."}
2026-08-17 15:55:24,060 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: `docs/specs/close-the-flow-py-defects.md` (attached). In scope: `flow.py`, `tests/test_flow.py`, `docs/flow/*.yaml` (regenerated), `docs/flow/areas.yaml`. Not `derive.py`, not `dash.py`.\n\nOrder is forced by the register: an untried entry naming `flow.py` gates every edit to it, so **all five are tried before any is fixed**.\n\n1. Tests for all five, observed red, each trialled → `guilty`.\n2. `declared_in(dir)` reads `areas.yaml`; `render_areas(docs, declared)` emits an UNKNOWN row per declared-but-uncharted area. No declaration → unchanged behaviour, because without one UNKNOWN is unanswerable rather than zero.\n3. `check()` refuses a repeated id.\n4. Footer by provenance: every node has `src` → derived and drift-checked; none → the existing sentence, which is then true; mixed → says so.\n5. `-h` / `--help` prints the docstring and exits **0**.\n6. `--areas` refuses when `index.yaml` is present rather than replacing its render.\n7. Reconcile the two older tasks against what `dash.py` already ships.\n\nEach fix: its own commit, its case red-before/green-after, and the guard removed to confirm that case alone fails. Then `idiot prove` on a clean tree.\n\nLedger: the board is alive (200) but `flow` is **not subscribed** (404), so findings go to this repo's own `idiot` register rather than an mcpp `bugs` task — the register is what gates the hook, and keeping half the findings elsewhere is the split the rule exists to prevent. `specboard.py subscribe` not run: that is Peter's call."}
