2026-08-17 16:16:23,783 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**Delivered by `dash.py`, not by a separate tool.** All three steps are satisfied by what shipped in commit `3cacbd8`:\n\n- `~/.flow/projects.yaml` holds a list of absolute paths and nothing else; the project name is derived from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` on every read, so a moved repo cannot carry a stale name (`name_of`, `dash.py`).\n- `flow-dash subscribe <charts dir>` / `unsubscribe <name|path>`, and `projects` to list.\n- A vanished path reads `MISSING` and is never dropped — verified by `test_a_vanished_path_reads_MISSING_not_absent`.\n\n**Decision taken under /afk:** the refusal rule changed while running it. Step 2 originally said subscribe should refuse a directory with no `areas.yaml`; that would have shut out `idiot`, whose eight hand-drawn charts are the corpus this tool was built against. Now only a directory with **no charts at all** is refused, and a directory with charts but no declaration is accepted while every surface prints `no areas.yaml` where it would otherwise print a number — because `0 UNKNOWN` with nothing declaring the areas is a lie, and it printed once before being caught. Undo by reverting `3cacbd8`.\n\nLeft for Peter: nothing. Closed as delivered elsewhere.'}
