2026-08-17 16:17:39,912 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "The three findings recorded out of scope on 2026-08-17 while proving the contract. **All three are now closed, two of them by later tasks:**\n\n1. **`--areas` overwrote a rendered `index.html`** — fixed in `943f76d`, register `the-index-clobbers-a-chart-called-index` CLOSED/commit. Note the correction this task's own title carries: `docs/HANDOVER.md` claims `index.yaml` itself is clobbered, which is wrong, and the test pins the real behaviour — the yaml survives, the render is lost.\n2. **No `-h`/`--help`** — fixed in `943f76d`, register `flow-cannot-explain-itself` CLOSED/commit. Prints the module docstring, exits 0.\n3. **`flow` had no charts of its own areas** — done by `flow-derive`: 15 areas drawn, `drift` reports them matching the code.\n4. **DECIDE, whether anything invokes the suite automatically** — see plan note."}
2026-08-17 16:17:56,846 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "**DECIDE, answered under /afk: nothing invokes the suite automatically, and I did not install anything that would.**\n\nThe facts, re-checked now: no `.github/`, no Makefile / tox.ini / justfile / pyproject, and `ls .git/hooks | grep -v sample` is empty. So `python3 -m pytest tests/ -q` and `python3 derive.py drift .` are run by hand or not at all, and `README.md` says so in those words.\n\n**Why I stopped short of installing a pre-commit hook**, which is the obvious fix:\n\n- A hook lives in `.git/hooks/`, which git does not track, so installing one changes Peter's local behaviour in a way that is invisible to the repo and cannot be reviewed in a diff. That is outside what /afk calls reversible-in-git.\n- The reversible half — a tracked `tools/pre-commit` plus a one-line installer — is a new file outside this task's attached spec, so it needs its own spec and register entry. Rule 3 says prefer finishing to starting, and there were six defects in flight.\n\n**What it would look like** if he wants it: `tools/pre-commit` runs `python3 -m pytest tests/ -q` then `python3 derive.py drift .`, refusing the commit on either failure; installed with `ln -s ../../tools/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit`; undone by deleting that symlink. Worth noting the loop it would close — three times today `drift` went red because I edited code without redrawing, and once I committed while it was red (`2121c9b`, corrected in `233f7a8`). A hook would have caught that one."}
