2026-08-17 18:19:08,625 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**`html/` is an HTTP server for the page. Nothing else.** Peter, 2026-08-17:\n*"effectively this is just an http server, with feeds from bridge and plugins"*,\n*"everything is served from either bridge, or it\'s plugins"*, and\n*"browsers cannot make decisions, they are a presentation layer ONLY"*.\n\nWhat I built in 5e05f44 / 0cfda68 / 4b81ad6 is wrong on three counts, each independently\ndisqualifying:\n\n1. **It relays data the bridge already emits.** Measured 2026-08-17 over a 70 s window:\n   `dash/live`\'s counters are 9/9 verbatim from `/stats`, its unit fields verbatim from\n   `/state[unit].link` and `.schedule`. The plugin originates nothing; the bridge emits\n   everything. A relay in `html/` is a second surface that can only drift — the reason\n   `/obs` and `/tx` were deleted rather than converted.\n2. **`GET /health` serves live data.** ~50 field paths, of which 9 groups are live —\n   `heardAt rssi snr beat servedAt missed nextWake`. The rule is quoted **verbatim in\n   the file I vendored**, `alarm-host.js:36-37`: *"GET/HTTP is FORBIDDEN FOR LIVE DATA.\n   NO EXCEPTIONS ... the ONLY data that can use POST/GET is for things like form\n   submission."* I read line 33 of that file and cited it; the rule was three lines below.\n3. **It serves raw values.** `heardAt` as ISO, `beat` as 60000. Rendering those means\n   computing in the browser, which is forbidden.\n\n**Nothing is lost by deleting the vendored copies** — node-dash\'s originals are untouched\nand byte-identical, verified by the hashes in `PROVENANCE.json`.\n\n**What this is NOT:** it is not a decision to abandon the view-model code. `alarm-sections.js`\nand the `fmtAgo`/`scheduleTime` string layer are the missing consolidation-and-presentation\nroute. By Peter\'s rule — *"plugins adds routes and consolidates data from other bridge\nfeeds"* — that is **a plugin in `plugins/`**, served on 8790, and it is a separate repo.\nRaised, not built here.'}
2026-08-17 18:19:46,883 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'docs/spec/html-is-a-static-server-only.md', 'kind': 'plan', 'label': 'Spec: unwind the relay, html serves static assets only', 'scope': 'task'}
2026-08-17 18:23:13,817 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': '## CONSTRAINT ADDED MID-TASK — Peter, 2026-08-17, verbatim\n\n> *"but that said, this is jsut one page. this will be a dashboard and pages will be\n> added. that might or might not need backend nodejs modules, so bear that in mind"*\n\n**What this does and does not change.**\n\nIt does **not** reopen the relay. Device data still comes from the bridge and from\nplugin routes; this server still originates and forwards none of it.\n\nIt **does** mean the guards must be read as what they actually are: a blunt proxy for\n*"this server relays no device data"*, not a ban on backend code. Concretely:\n\n- **`express.static` over `public/` already handles a multi-page dashboard** —\n  `extensions: [\'html\']` resolves `/foo` to `foo.html`, so pages are added as files\n  with no code change.\n- **Backend node modules are permitted** when they serve something that is not device\n  data — templating, asset assembly, a build step, an auth or session layer. Nothing in\n  the current guards blocks any of that.\n- **The two guards that could bite** a legitimate future need are\n  `this package declares no websocket dependency` and\n  `no source in bin/ opens a socket or fetches`. They are deliberately blunt. If a page\n  ever appears to need one of them relaxed, that is a **decision to be taken and written\n  down**, not a guard to delete quietly — and the first question is whether the need is\n  really a consolidation route, in which case it is a plugin.\n\n**The line to hold:** a backend module here may compose the *page*. It may not compose\nthe *data*. The moment something in `bin/` wants a device value, it is a plugin on the\nbridge, because that is where routes are added and data consolidated.'}
2026-08-17 18:24:50,772 1578042 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Per `docs/spec/html-is-a-static-server-only.md` (attached).\n\n1. Prove the deletion lossless **first** — all 7 node-dash originals still hash to\n   `PROVENANCE.json`. Then delete `src/` and the three tests.\n2. Rewrite `bin/httpd.js`: `express.static` over `public/`, no `ws`, no bridge client,\n   no JSON route, no body parser. Bind address becomes a decision (`--host`, default\n   `0.0.0.0`, IPv4-only like the bridge) instead of Node's dual-stack default.\n3. `public/index.html` — honestly static placeholder. `package.json` drops `ws`.\n4. `test/static.test.js` — byte-identical responses, live-field blacklist, GET/HEAD only,\n   no ws dependency, nothing in `bin/` or `public/` reaching for data.\n5. Falsify all four guards; raise the consolidation route with plugins.\n\n**Done — commits `edc4640` and `c066bf5`.** 8/8 green. All four falsifications produced\nthe expected failure and were restored. Service live on `0.0.0.0:8791`, `GET /` 200 from\nthe LAN, `/health` 404, and `ss` confirms the process holds **no connection to the\nbridge**. node-dash `/control` still 200; bridge and node-dash pids and restart counts\nunchanged.\n\n**Raised as #51 `control-surface-consolidation`** on `node-dash--plugins`.\n\n**The guard caught its own subject during implementation** — the placeholder's comment\ncontained the literals it was explaining were forbidden. The page was reworded, not the\nguard."}
