2026-08-18 07:55:53,926 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Fix the duplicate-reply defect in replay FIRST, then open the /events websocket to replay. In that\norder, because the second makes the first reachable from a browser.\n\nBoth found 2026-08-18 by the mt-alarm-html session reading bridge source, on the xsession channel\nbridge--mt-alarm-html, item `events-ws-cannot-ask-for-replay`. The GAP is what they raised; the BUG\nis what their correction to my arithmetic uncovered. Neither is urgent and nothing is waiting.'}
2026-08-18 07:56:04,414 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'note', 'text': "EVIDENCE for the BUG, measured 2026-08-18 against data/bridge.db, not reasoned about.\n\n  bin/bridged.js:34-35   EVENT_KINDS = 12 names + ...CLASSES\n  src/classify.js:131    CLASSES = ['reply','beat','alarm','chunk','unknown']\n                         -> 17 entries, 16 distinct. 'reply' appears in BOTH lists.\n  bin/bridged.js:232     kinds.flatMap((k) => db.get(k, {...}))\n                         no dedupe, so db.get('reply') runs TWICE and both results concatenate.\n                         The .sort((a,b) => a.id - b.id) and .slice(-limit) that follow remove\n                         neither copy.\n\nReplaying the real store by hand:\n\n  reply rows in whole store                    28\n  since=0 limit=500  -> 2387 rows pre-slice,   28 duplicate ids\n  since=now-24h limit=200 -> 200 rows,          0 duplicate ids\n\nWHY IT HAS SURVIVED. The default replay window is 24h (src/bridge.js:1178) and there are no reply\nrows in the last 24h, so the duplicate never appears at the default. Test fixtures carry a handful\nof rows and never reach back far enough either. It becomes visible exactly when a caller asks for a\nlong window -- which is what step 2 adds.\n\nBLAST RADIUS. Every plugin using replay double-counts replies. notify is the one to check first:\nre-acting on replayed events is the failure mode the src/bridge.js:1185 comment was written to\nprevent, and it prevented the restamp but not the duplicate.\n\nCANDIDATE FIX is [...new Set(kinds)] at bridged.js:232, one word. NOT to be applied before a test\nthat fails on the duplicate and passes without it -- a one-word fix I am certain about is the kind\nI have shipped wrong before by skipping the proof."}
2026-08-18 07:56:21,697 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': "STEP 2 SHAPE, agreed with mt-alarm-html on the board before any code exists.\n\n  ws://host/events?since=<ms>&limit=<n>&types=<a,b>&unit=<!id>\n\n  - no params -> live only, byte for byte what /events is today. No existing consumer changes.\n  - src/api.js:320 already has `req` in lexical scope and calls onEvents(ws) without it.\n    onEvents(ws, req) costs nothing; the query string is NOT lost, the pathname is merely the\n    routing key. (html's original report said the query was dropped -- it is not.)\n  - limit MUST be capped server side. store.read reads `limit` rows PER KIND before merging\n    (bin/bridged.js:232), so an uncapped browser asking limit=40000 pulls up to 16 x 40000 rows\n    through the process that is the only route to the units. src/bridge.js:1174 already says this\n    concern in its own words, about a caller more trustworthy than a browser.\n    DERIVE the cap, do not pick it, and publish it in /schema rather than truncate silently.\n  - types and unit are already parameters of store.read; forwarding them is the change that makes\n    the cap stop mattering. html confirmed their range widget is PER-CHART (their cards.js\n    rangeGroup carries a name per group, no shared range state), so every ask is one type for one\n    unit -- ?types=witness&unit=!987ab80f, wanting the last few hundred of ~20k rows.\n  - replayed:true and the ORIGINAL `at` are already on replayed events (src/bridge.js:1189-1191)\n    and html will use them to distinguish history from live. Do not restamp.\n\nAGREED SPLIT, and it bounds this task: raw replay serves 1H..DAY honestly. WEEK/MONTH/ALL over\n40001 witness rows is downsampling, which is a plugin's job, not the firehose's -- html raised that\nseparately with plugins as `control-surface-consolidation`. Do not grow this task into buckets.\n\nSOCKET COUNT is not a problem to pre-solve. html offered to hold one socket and demultiplex; told\nthem not to. If N sockets ever becomes a real number, measure it and go back to them."}
2026-08-18 08:02:50,322 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'NARROWED 2026-08-18 by Peter via the html session, and it makes step 2 smaller.\n\nPRIMITIVES ONLY on this side: since (absolute ms), limit (records), types. NO range vocabulary in\nthe bridge and none in a plugin -- nothing here ever learns what 1H or WEEK means. The browser owns\nthe names and converts a selection to a since. Peter, verbatim: "plugin/bridge only have since or\nrecords. the (NEW) browser plugin can determine the since based on what the user selects".\n\nThis does not change the plan note above -- it never contained range names -- it confirms it from\ntheir side and removes the downsampling-plugin variant from consideration for THIS task.\n\nTRAP I FLAGGED BACK TO THEM, and it is the one thing this narrowing walks into. They wrote that\ntheir ALL button (ms: null) would mean "simply no since parameter". On this side that is FALSE:\n\n  src/bridge.js:1178   const since = opt.since ?? (Date.now() - 24 * 3600e3);\n\nOmitting since yields the 24h DEFAULT, not everything -- so ALL would silently render as DAY and\nlook correct. Same shape as the asc/desc defect already documented in bin/bridged.js:222-227:\nbounded wrongly, looks fine, is stale. Told them to send since=0 explicitly.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THIS TASK: since=0 is the window that hits the derived cap hardest AND is exactly\nwhere step 1\'s duplicate-reply bug becomes visible. ALL is the button that exercises both unfixed\nthings, which is another reason step 1 precedes step 2.\n\nOWED TO HTML WHEN BUILT: publish the cap in /schema, and make a capped response SAY it was capped\nrather than just returning fewer rows. Their widget already marks a range DISABLED when its source\ncannot reach that far, so they can grey out ALL truthfully -- but only if told, not if left to\ninfer it by counting rows.'}
2026-08-18 08:03:42,407 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'STEP 2 SURFACE -- FINAL, set by Peter 2026-08-18 after discussing it with the html session.\n\n  ws://host/events?since=<ms>&limit=<n>\n\n  TWO PARAMETERS. No types, no unit, no range names. Peter: "we should accept since and limit args\n  only. it is not up to us or plugins to define time buckets". An earlier version of this note\n  offered types and unit to html; that offer is WITHDRAWN and they have been told.\n\n  - no params -> live only, byte for byte what /events is today. No existing consumer changes.\n  - src/api.js:320 already has `req` in lexical scope and calls onEvents(ws) without it.\n    onEvents(ws, req) costs nothing; the query string is NOT lost, the pathname is merely the\n    routing key. (html\'s original report said the query was dropped -- it is not.)\n  - since is ABSOLUTE ms. Omitting it yields the 24h default (src/bridge.js:1178), NOT everything.\n    html must send since=0 for their ALL button or it silently renders as DAY and looks right.\n    Told them. Same failure shape as the asc/desc defect at bin/bridged.js:222-227.\n  - limit MUST be capped server side. DERIVE the cap, do not pick it. Publish it in /schema AND\n    make a capped response say it was capped, so html can grey out ALL because they were told\n    rather than because they counted rows.\n  - replayed:true and the ORIGINAL `at` are already on replayed events (src/bridge.js:1189-1191).\n    Do not restamp.\n\nCOST OF DROPPING types, recorded so reversing it is one sentence rather than archaeology. Every\nbrowser ask is now the firehose: store.read merges all 16 kinds and slices the last `limit` off the\nmerged timeline (bin/bridged.js:232). A chart wanting witness competes with beat/alarm/queue/send/\nonair for the same limit, so html needs limit >> points-wanted and must filter by type in the\nbrowser. The ratio is a property of the mesh that day, not a guarantee. This makes the cap bind\nharder than the version I had accepted, which is the whole of the cost.\n\nNOT CHANGED: ctx.subscribe(fn, {replay}) keeps types and unit for PLUGINS. Peter\'s message was\nabout the browser query; removing a capability plugins have today on my reading of it would be\ntaking something away that nobody asked me to. If it is meant to go, it is a separate change.\n\nSTILL BOUNDED: raw replay only. No buckets, no downsampling here -- html raised that separately\nwith plugins as `control-surface-consolidation`. Do not grow this task into it.'}
2026-08-18 08:06:12,730 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'docs/spec/events-replay-window.md', 'kind': 'plan', 'label': 'Spec: fix duplicate reply in replay, then open /events to since/limit'}
