2026-08-18 08:16:27,774 1652794 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'replay-duplicates-and-ws-replay', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'SHIPPED AND DEPLOYED 2026-08-18. Commit 6798357, pm2 restart of `bridge` at 07:15:07Z.\n\nVERIFIED ON THE LIVE SERVICE, not in a test:\n\n  restart clean           2 units restored, 4 plugins loaded (pointer/dash/notify/probe),\n                          radio !2687afb1 ch2, pointer reconnected to rotator and re-armed\n  GET /schema             declares since + limit on /events\n  ws /events              no params -> live only: 1 tick in 2s, NO window frame, no history.\n                          node-dash unaffected.\n  ws /events?since=0&limit=40000\n                          {"type":"window","since":0,"limit":2000,"cap":2000,"capped":true}\n                          then 2000 events, all marked replayed, original `at` preserved\n                          (2026-08-17T18:15:26Z -> 2026-08-18T07:13:26Z)\n  duplicate gone          live store: 28 reply rows stored, 56 delivered before, 28 after\n\nnpm test 220 pass / 0 fail (was 205).\n\nTWO REAL NUMBERS THAT CAME OUT OF DEPLOYING IT, both consequences of `types` not being a parameter,\nand both told to html rather than left to be discovered:\n\n1. The 2000-event window contained witness 1296, beat 443, alarm 212, overdue 24, returned 24,\n   schedule 1 -- and reply 0, with 28 replies stored. A low-rate type falls entirely outside a\n   window a high-rate type fills. Callers must read a thin series as "outside the window", never\n   "nothing happened".\n\n2. AT THE CAP, since=0 reaches back about 13 HOURS, not the 4.5 days the store holds. So raw replay\n   realistically serves html\'s 1H..12H buttons; DAY and above are truncated and say so via\n   capped:true. That is smaller than either side was picturing. The answer if it matters is the\n   downsampling plugin already raised as `control-surface-consolidation`, NOT a bigger cap -- the\n   cap is 1% of the pre-empt deadline on the only route to the units.\n\nBOTH ITEMS LEFT OPEN ON THE BOARD DELIBERATELY. html\'s `events-ws-cannot-ask-for-replay` is theirs\nto resolve once their charts actually draw; plugins\' `replay-delivers-replies-twice` is open until\nthey say whether anything of theirs counted replies under the bug -- the fix stops it recurring, it\ndoes not correct what was already counted.'}
