2026-08-18 10:06:55,335 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, parked 2026-08-17, worked 2026-08-18 under /afk:\n\n> *"a new flow symbol test-point. these would be intended as markers and even hooks to test scripts that validate / prove that at specific points in the flow, the running code produces the correct pre-determined results / values."*\n\n**Delivered as an attribute, not a seventh widget** — `docs/SPEC.md` forbids a seventh, and it is also the wrong category: the six widgets are kinds of STEP and a proof is an assertion ABOUT a step. A terminal that is proved is still a terminal. `prove:` sits on a node exactly as `src:` does.\n\n**Three files, three authors** — `<area>.yaml` derived by `flow_derive`, `areas.yaml` declared by a human, `proof.yaml` **measured** by `flow_prove`. Keeping the measurement out of the chart is the design: written into it, a verdict would be indistinguishable from the derivation.\n\n**Four verdicts, one green:** `unproved` (no entry — nobody ran it), `proved`, `FAILED`, `stale`. Stale is what earns the feature — every entry stores the sha256 of the source file it was proved against, so a green tick over code that has moved is demoted rather than believed.\n\nClosed: `a-hand-written-note-is-lost-on-redraw`, `no-way-to-prove-a-point-in-the-flow`, both CLOSED/commit on `2210b53`.'}
2026-08-18 10:07:10,382 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: `docs/specs/test-points.md` (attached). Shipped in `2210b53`; register findings in `d6568d3`.\n\n1. **Investigate** — done: it is an attribute, and the prerequisite bug was found by testing my own spec\'s claim.\n2. **BUG, the prerequisite** — done. `draw` kept only nodes with no `src:`, so a `note` (or any `prove:`) on a derived node was silently dropped. Then the first fix proved insufficient in real use: matching on `src:` alone meant adding 87 lines to `flow.py` moved every node below and lost **two of three** real markers. Falls back to the node id; an annotation that still cannot be re-attached is **reported**, never dropped silently.\n3. **TOOL, prove.py** — done. `flow_prove <repo>` / `--list`, installed as `/usr/local/bin/flow_prove`, writes `docs/flow/proof.yaml` with `want`/`got`/`at`/`commit`/`source_sha256`. Exits 2 if any point failed.\n4. **TOOL, the badges** — done. Four states rendered from the widget palette (terminal-green, gate-amber, hole-red) rather than new tokens — the chart template defines no `--ok/--bad/--warn`, so inventing them would have rendered colourless, the same defect as the index\'s undeclared `--warn`. Index counts failures separately from holes.\n5. **DOGFOOD** — done. Three real points, two asserting a pre-determined value; `/flow_prove` skill written; `docs/SPEC.md` amended so `hole` is "the only red WIDGET" and a failed proof is a red BADGE.\n\n**The most useful thing here was my own falsification catching a worthless test.** Every page carries `.w .proof.stale{...}` in its stylesheet, so `"stale" in body` was true of every page ever rendered — and the case that earns this whole feature PASSED with the staleness check deleted. Assertions now match the rendered `<span class="proof …">` markup; shown failing without the check and passing with it.\n\n146 passed, drift 16 areas matching, 3 points 0 failed, all read before committing.'}
