2026-08-18 10:33:14,761 1664209 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'four-specs-stale-against-config-py-and-bridge-config-yaml — CONFIRMED, pre-existing, NOT mine\n\nFound 2026-08-18 during Phase 5 of session-passkey-refresh-not-holding. `python scripts/check_specs.py` reports 4 stale specs that were already stale before any edit in this session:\n\n  nordic_dfu_session        stored=419f110b034e… actual=a2625a2d80f9…\n  ota_config_yaml           stored=303608b94270… actual=bebd9fc3763c…\n  ota_state_decision_tree   stored=7112b681a73d… actual=138f04609702…\n  region_unset_bootstrap    stored=82ab0c60c58e… actual=72cc2d07e7ef…\n\nEstablished by recomputing every spec\'s hash with HEAD\'s core/ble_device.py substituted for the working-tree copy: 5 specs were stale before the edit (these 4, plus this session\'s own new spec, which appears only as an artefact of the substitution). 24 further specs were staled by the one-function edit to core/ble_device.py and have been resynced, plus stale_spec_hashes, whose source list is four of those spec files.\n\nAll four remaining share BOTH core/config.py and core/bridge_config.yaml in their `source:` lists, and none of them are stale on any file this session touched — so something changed in config.py or bridge_config.yaml and was never resynced. The last three commits on main are all "chore(specs): resync stale source_hash after …", so the convention is to resync promptly; these four were missed.\n\nNOT FIXED, deliberately. Only files named in the attached spec are in scope, and a hash resync asserts "unchanged since last set" — it cannot assert the prose is still accurate. Resyncing four specs whose backing config I have not read would make the validator green over prose nobody has checked, which is the exact failure the hash exists to catch. Whoever changed config.py/bridge_config.yaml should re-read these four and resync them.\n\nCONSEQUENCE WORTH KNOWING: `python scripts/check_specs.py` is the project\'s /idiot validation_cmd and is specified to print "All specs current." It cannot print that while these 4 are outstanding, so every /idiot run in this repo currently fails its own Phase 5 validation for reasons unrelated to the work being done.'}
