2026-08-18 10:33:50,748 1664209 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Bound the refresh write and make failure survivable and visible. Spec: docs/modules/passkey_refresh_loop_stall.md (attached).\n\n1. Add module constant _PASSKEY_SEND_TIMEOUT_S = 30 in core/ble_device.py. Derived: interval + timeout must stay under the device-side expiry — 240 (admin_passkey_refresh_s) + 30 = 270 < 300 (_PASSKEY_TTL_S), margin 30s. Looser than the 5s foreground bound in methods.py:_write_direct because a background renewal on a merely-slow link must not be reported as failed; observed healthy cycle today was 243-273s, i.e. 3-33s of latency on top of the 240s sleep.\n\n2. Wrap the send in _passkey_refresh_loop with asyncio.wait_for(..., timeout=_PASSKEY_SEND_TIMEOUT_S), catch TimeoutError and Exception, log a WARNING naming the address and reason, re-raise CancelledError so shutdown still works, and keep the sleep OUTSIDE the try so a failure still waits out the interval instead of spinning.\n\n3. Nothing else in core/ble_device.py is touched. _send_admin_get_owner stays unbounded on its own (its connect-time caller has separate failure handling), and _signal_poll_loop's identical shape is recorded in the bugs ledger as UNVERIFIED rather than fixed here.\n\nVERIFICATION PLAN — the falsification is the one that decides whether the rest means anything: remove the bound, hang the write, and show the loop pinning on iteration 1. If it does not pin, the check was testing something else. Live functional verification needs a restart of the running gateway (pid 1659964, started manually, logs to a socket), which is Peter's call, not mine."}
