2026-08-18 10:48:41,618 1664209 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Stop the session passkey expiring on a connected radio, by echoing it on the one admin message that omitted it.\n\nROOT CAUSE, measured 2026-08-18 from /var/log/mesh-gw.log at DEBUG (a logfile that did not exist before today — the process logged to a socket, and enabling file logging is what solved this):\n\n  10:34:54  get_owner_request sent -> 10:34:56 session_passkey refreshed    ANSWERED\n  10:38:55  get_owner_request sent -> nothing                               IGNORED\n\nsend_admin (core/ble_device.py:873-901) injects the session passkey when one is held. _send_admin_get_owner (:1249-1267), the refresh path, did not. Firmware >= 2.7.18 ignores admin traffic that omits it once a session exists, so the refresh request was the one admin message the radio dropped — and it is the one that renews the key. The first request is answered because no key is held yet and there is nothing to omit; every later one is dropped silently, the key expires, and every subsequent config SET / OTA / factory-reset carries a dead key.\n\nFIXED, verified live on the same running gateway:\n  10:47:46 sent -> 10:47:47 refreshed   ttl 297, new key   (!2687afb1, fw 2.8.0.793a749)\n  10:47:52 sent -> 10:47:53 refreshed   ttl 294, new key   (!fa39f7b4, fw 2.7.26.54e0d8d)\n\nSUPERSEDES the root cause in task session-passkey-refresh-not-holding / docs/modules/passkey_refresh_loop_stall.md, which was wrong. Two diagnoses were disproven: a dead task from an unhandled BleakError (a dead asyncio task cannot resume, and these did), and a stalled GATT write (the write completes in 79ms). Both reasoned about the sending side while the receiving side was invisible. That spec is amended in place rather than deleted, and the hardening it added (a 30s bound plus exception guard on the loop) is kept as correct-but-not-the-fix.'}
2026-08-18 10:48:48,753 1664209 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Two lines in core/ble_device.py:_send_admin_get_owner, mirroring send_admin:882-883:\n\n    if self._data.session_passkey:\n        admin.session_passkey = bytes.fromhex(self._data.session_passkey)\n\nDeliberately NOT rewritten to delegate to send_admin: _send_admin_get_owner takes an explicit client argument and runs inside the connect sequence, whereas send_admin resolves self._client via send_toradio and raises unless state == READY. Coupling them is a larger change with a different risk profile.\n\nAlso amend docs/modules/passkey_refresh_loop_stall.md in place with a superseded banner rather than deleting it — a wrong diagnosis that is quietly removed gets rediscovered.\n\nVERIFICATION: restart the gateway and watch past the 240s mark on both radios; a "session_passkey refreshed by AppRouter" line must follow the second "get_owner_request sent". The failing half of the falsification is already measured on this same system at 10:38:55/10:38:59 today, so the before/after is one live system in two states, not an assertion.\n\nDone and passing — see the goal note for the timestamps.'}
