2026-08-18 12:21:40,343 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Shipped in `a6c1176`, `58f38bc`, `2a3e04f`. All five steps done.\n\n`flow_derive` refuses a repo it cannot parse and names what it found, instead of answering `symbols: []` about 815 lines of C++. `stamp` records the sha256 of every file a chart cites; `drift` falls back to comparing them where there is no backend, and says which check ran. Proved end to end on a copy of `pio/mylibs/mt-chunk-push`: charted `PushServer::onFrame` by hand, added a `PUSH_CANCEL` case, and both `drift` (exit 2, names the file) and `flow_prove` (exit 2, "want \'4\', got \'5\'") caught it, with a red FAILED badge on the page.\n\nFound and fixed on the way: an authored chart claimed a generator produced it, because provenance was inferred from `src:` which an agent writes too. Charts now declare `derived_by:`.'}
