2026-08-18 12:22:42,161 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'flow-test-points-are-probe-points', 'title': 'GAP - a test point is a PCB probe pad: the expected value belongs on the chart, and a measurement needs tolerance', 'steps': ['TOOL - show the expected value ON the node, the way TP3 is silkscreened 3V3 next to the pad', 'TOOL - a measurement needs tolerance: near: for numbers, matches: for a pattern, beside the exact is:', 'VERIFY - look at a probed chart and check a reader can see what SHOULD be there without running anything']}
2026-08-18 12:22:56,096 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**Peter, 2026-08-18, verbatim:**\n\n> *"- you do know the purpose of test point dont you. this is like a test point on a circuit board. it is used to attache verifyable test/pass"*\n\n**My reading, kept separate from his words so the next reader can check one against the other:**\n\nA test point on a PCB is a pad the designer *deliberately exposes* so the circuit can be probed **in situ, while running**. Three properties, and I only built the third:\n\n1. **The expected value is printed next to it.** `TP3 · 3V3`. You can read what *should* be there without a meter in your hand. My chart shows only `proved` / `FAILED` — the pre-determined value is buried in the yaml, so the page tells you whether somebody measured it but never what it ought to be. **That is the gap.**\n2. **A measurement has tolerance.** 3.3V ±5%, not exactly the string "3.3". `is:` is exact-match only, which is the wrong instrument for anything numeric — and firmware, which is where this is heading, is all counts, timings and voltages.\n3. **You attach and get a verifiable pass/fail.** Built: `run:` plus `is:`/`exit:`, four verdicts, stale demotion.\n\nSo the interjection sharpens what was already shipped rather than starting something new: the analogy says a test point is **an exposed place with a documented expected value**, and I built the probing without the silkscreen.\n\nNot changed by this: `prove:` stays an attribute rather than a seventh widget. A pad is not a component either.'}
