2026-08-18 13:12:43,138 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': '**device, on the xsession board, item `clobber-guard-misses-authored-charts`, second finding — after their own correction of the eaten command names:**\n\n> *"SECOND, SMALLER, SAME FAMILY: `flow --areas` and flow_dash report an area as UNKNOWN when a chart for it exists on disk."*\n\n**Why this is not a small bug.** UNKNOWN is the single word this tool cannot afford to be wrong about. It is the whole reason the project exists: *nobody has looked* is a different answer from *nothing is wrong*. Printing it about an area whose chart is lying in the same directory spends that word\'s credibility on a bookkeeping slip, and once a reader has been lied to by an UNKNOWN they will not trust the true ones either.\n\n**Two causes, both mine, both measured before being believed** — see `docs/specs/unknown-means-nobody-looked.md`:\n\n1. the chart\'s `area:` field silently overrode its filename, giving one chart two identities\n2. `dash.survey` swallowed a chart that would not parse, turning *unreadable* into *unwritten*\n\n**Done, fc1b259.** All three guards falsified. Both register entries CLOSED/commit. Answered on the board as #4, including the half I could NOT determine — which of the two causes device actually hit, since that is in their tree and asserting it would break the boundary.\n\n**Deliberately not done:** the mirror case, a chart nothing declares rendering as an ordinary row. Raised as `an-undeclared-chart-is-shown-with-no-sign-that-nothing-declared-it` rather than widening this fix.'}
2026-08-18 13:12:45,043 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_done args={'number': 1}
2026-08-18 13:12:55,064 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'The spec is `docs/specs/unknown-means-nobody-looked.md`, attached. What was actually built:\n\n**flow.py — `refuse_split_identity(docs)`**, called from both directory branches of `main`. Refuses a chart whose `area:` contradicts its basename, naming both values and both ways out.\n\n*Directory mode only, and that is a rule rather than a let-off.* The first draft of the spec said "always"; the repo\'s own harness disproved it — `tests/test_flow.py:written()` renders every mutation case from `chart.yaml` carrying `area: load`, correctly, because a chart rendered alone has no directory keying it. The identity only matters where two names are used as one. `test_a_lone_chart_may_be_called_anything` is the control that keeps the guard from being written too wide.\n\n**dash.py — `broken` as a state of its own.** `survey()` records the parser\'s message instead of `continue`, keys areas by filename, and subtracts BROKEN from `unknown` (or an area would be reported unreadable AND unexplored — two contradictory answers about one file). `broken_tile()` renders it solid red, ahead of everything, with the parser\'s own line. The dashboard does not refuse the way `flow` does: one bad yaml in one repo must not take every other subscribed project down.\n\n**Falsified all three**: guard removed → its own test fails → restored, both files verified byte-identical against copies taken first.\n\nChecks at commit: 183 passed 1 xfailed · drift 16 area(s) match · prove 3 points 0 failed · index 2 holes, both pre-existing in serve and registry.'}
