2026-08-18 13:16:38,450 1710223 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "Stop any web page being able to queue commands to the units, and give the dashboard the preflight\nit needs to command them honestly.\n\nFound 2026-08-18 answering the mt-alarm-html session's `page-cannot-post-to-queue` on channel\nbridge--mt-alarm-html. They asked whether adding CORS would widen the exposure; it does not, because\nthe exposure was already there. src/api.js never read Content-Type, so a POST with text/plain — a\nCORS simple request, sent with no preflight — was parsed and queued from any origin on the internet.\nThe page could not read the reply, which looks like a refusal and is not one.\n\nAfter this change browsers are STRICTLY more restricted than before it. Non-browser callers are\nunchanged, and that is the honest limit rather than an oversight."}
2026-08-18 13:16:46,619 1710223 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "THE RULE, applied before routing and before any body is read.\n\n  Origin absent      any method   pass, no CORS headers      curl, CLI, mesh-gw, node-dash, plugins\n  Origin allowed     any method   pass, Allow-Origin echoed\n  Origin foreign     GET          pass, NO header            unchanged from today, deliberately\n  Origin foreign     write        403 before the body parse\n  any                OPTIONS      answered if allowed, else 403\n\nA WRITE is any method that is not GET/HEAD/OPTIONS — named as a complement, so a plugin declaring\nPATCH tomorrow is guarded without src/callers.js being edited.\n\nBY METHOD, NEVER BY PATH, because POST /pointer/aim is a plugin route that moves shared hardware.\n\nALLOWLIST DERIVED from os.networkInterfaces(): a page served by this host may command it, nothing\nelse may. --allow-origin adds an exact origin; --allow-subnet takes CIDRs and `null` switches it off.\n\nSpec: docs/spec/who-may-command.md. Proof required before done, and all of it obtained:\na test observed FAILING 202 on today's code, Origin: null refused, no-Origin still queued, the\npreflight answered and refused, a plugin write route guarded, and the live service re-checked."}
