2026-08-18 14:34:23,678 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: `docs/specs/test-points.md`. Built across `0a3471c`, `caff1e4`, `b5145b7`.\n\n**Step 1 — the silkscreen.** `expected_of(marker)` in flow.py turns a point\'s `is:` / `exit:` / `near:`+`within:` / `matches:` into one short string printed beside the verdict chip: `exit 0`, `100 ±5`, `~ ^ok-[0-9]+$`. Verified by LOOKING, at 1600x1000, both themes — and the looking is what found the real defect: the value rendered at 8.96px grey next to a filled chip, so the page shouted the verdict and whispered the expected value. Inverse of a PCB, where the printed value is the permanent part. Now 9.6px in `--ink` against the chip\'s 9.28px, measured in the browser rather than asserted off the CSS.\n\n**Step 2 — tolerance.** `prove.compare()` has four instruments, each exercised: `near:`+`within:` (103 inside 100±5 passes, 106 fails, "not a number" fails), `matches:` (regex), `is:` (exact — and `is: 3.3` failing against `3.30` is the demonstration of why `near:` had to exist), `exit:`.\n\n**Step 3 — verify by looking.** Done. Two findings the assertions could never have produced: the chip flipped to **stale** the instant flow.py was edited, because check.yaml\'s point cites `flow.py:83` and the proof was recorded against bytes that no longer existed — the stale demotion firing on a real edit for the first time, green again after `flow_prove` re-measured. And the page\'s only console error is a 404 for `/favicon.ico`, which belongs to the dashboard, not to a chart.\n\n**Recorded against myself:** `caff1e4` was committed with a failing test and 144 drift differences while its message claimed green. Third time today with the identical shape — checks and commit chained into one invocation, so the failure scrolls past above a commit that has already happened. Corrected in `b5145b7` rather than amended away.'}
