2026-08-18 14:37:31,420 1724304 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Stop reporting a post-dispatch BLE link teardown as a write failure. A config save that makes the radio reboot is a success, not a 500.\n\nRAISED BY node-dash: POST /{id}/admin with a set_module_config returned 500 (BleakGATTProtocolError UNLIKELY_ERROR) three times, and the value persisted every time. They could not tell a real failure from a successful save and refused to work around it.\n\nROOT CAUSE — a race, proven from /var/log/mesh-gw.log:\n  13:28:12,453  disconnected_callback fired      <- link gone FIRST\n  13:28:12,454  write_gatt_char -> UNLIKELY_ERROR -> HTTP 500\n  13:28:12,459  -> RECONNECTING\nand the same operation twice more with no error at all (13:37:55,095 and 13:40:42,478 logged "send_admin sent" before the disconnect). Whether the caller sees an error depends on whether the ATT response or the firmware reboot wins by a millisecond.\n\nTHE REFERENCE ANSWER (Peter\'s standing rule: the phone app is what we emulate). Meshtastic-Android CommandSenderImpl: `if (!accepted) throw PacketQueueRejectedException` — the ONLY failure is the queue refusing the packet. BleRadioTransport: "Delivery is confirmed later by the protocol, not by this result." AdminControllerImpl.editSettings: "A dispatched local commit is durable once a post-dispatch departure is observed."\n\nFIXED in 0235d57. send_toradio returns bool (True clean / False dispatched-then-torn-down), send_admin propagates it, admin and _write_direct report reboot_observed. No 500 for this case.\n\nTHE TRAP: checking state or _disconnect_event inside the except block is RACY — _on_disconnect uses call_soon_threadsafe, so neither is updated when the exception is caught. The signal must be waited for with a bound. Falsification: sampled version misclassified 20/20.\n\nTimeout 0.1s derived from 6 measured disconnects (callback -> RECONNECTING: min 0.0ms, median 0.5ms, max 1.0ms) = 100x worst observed, 2% of the 5s foreground write bound.'}
2026-08-18 14:37:41,479 1724304 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Classify the failure in send_toradio, the single primitive every write goes through (message_manager.py:106, ble_device.py send_admin, send_traceroute). That is where the phone app puts it, and it means no caller has to know.\n\n1. send_toradio -> bool. On BleakError/EOFError, wait up to _WRITE_TEARDOWN_WINDOW_S for _disconnect_event. Set = dispatched then torn down, log INFO, return False. Not set = genuine rejection, re-raise THE ORIGINAL exception (`raise e from None`, not a bare `raise` — see below).\n2. send_admin returns the same bool.\n3. methods.admin and _write_direct add reboot_observed; _write_direct\'s error path gains the exception type.\n4. AdminResponse gains reboot_observed; VerifiedResponse gains it with a default so existing callers are unaffected.\n5. API_REST.md documents it, including that reboot_observed:true still does not mean applied — re-read with ?fresh=1.\n\nNOT DONE, deliberately: the app\'s 3-attempt retryBleOperation. Retrying at a rebooting radio is pointless and would park an HTTP caller up to 30s. Recorded, not built.\n\nBUG THE FALSIFICATION CAUGHT IN MY OWN CODE: a bare `raise` inside the nested `except asyncio.TimeoutError` re-raises the TimeoutError, not the original BLE error — _write_direct would then report every genuine failure as "Write timed out — BLE too slow". Found by running the test, not by reading the diff.\n\nDone and verified — see the goal note.'}
