2026-08-18 16:32:47,578 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Register: `small-functions-waste-a-whole-band`, guilty since 2026-08-18 morning, encoded as `tests/test_derive.py::test_a_repo_of_small_functions_is_not_mostly_empty_rows` with `xfail(strict=True)` so nobody could fix it silently. The last open entry in the register.\n\n**The accusation, as written:** *"every function gets a fixed 5-row band, so a repo of small functions renders mostly as vertical whitespace: in the xsession trial `utc_now` uses 2 nodes and occupies the same height as a 12-node function."*\n\n**One correction to it, recorded rather than softened:** the board is `grid-template-rows: repeat(N, auto)`, so an empty row collapses to zero height. An empty row costs one row-gap — `clamp(.6rem, 2.2vw, 2.2rem)`, up to 35px — not a row. Real waste, ~500px across five small functions, but not the page-of-whitespace the entry claims.\n\nSpec: `docs/specs/a-band-as-tall-as-the-function-needs.md`.'}
2026-08-18 16:32:59,119 1549532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Shipped in `0b169be`. `derive.py` gains `compact()` and `GUTTER`; `draw_area` advances the base by what the function used rather than by `used * BAND`.\n\n**How.** `compact()` sorts the rows a function put something on and renumbers them consecutively. Sorting is what makes it safe — order is preserved exactly, so a gate above its spine stays above it; only the gaps close. Nothing moves sideways: columns and the boustrophedon wrap are `band_of`'s business and untouched.\n\n**GUTTER = 2** keeps exactly one blank row between functions. After compaction it is the only thing separating one function's terminal from the next function's gate, so it is a named constant with the reason attached rather than arithmetic left over.\n\n**Measured.**\n\n| | rows | empty |\n|---|---|---|\n| five two-node functions, before | 25 | 15 |\n| five two-node functions, after | 14 | 4 (the gutters) |\n| this repo's sixteen charts, before | 550 | 310 |\n| this repo's sixteen charts, after | 308 | 66 |\n\n**Verified**: 187 passed (was 186 + 1 xfail) · drift 16 areas match · prove 3/0 · draw twice byte-identical · every gate above its source and every terminal below, checked programmatically on `check.yaml` · looked at in the browser at 1600×1000, the chart is about a third shorter and the three flows still read as three.\n\n**Rejected**: deleting every empty row globally. It would take the between-function gutter with it, and would reshape charts whose blank rows may be load-bearing for a reason nobody wrote down. Compaction happens per function, where the reason for each row is known.\n\n**One slip**: the first edit dropped `nodes += n` / `edges += e` and drew a chart with zero nodes. Caught immediately because the measurement was run before anything else."}
