2026-08-19 09:28:15,617 1774009 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-19, verbatim:\n\n"analyse the db tables and the number of records and derive / decide what is a reasonable amout of\nrecords for each table, and adjust the retention policies."\n\nCONTEXT AT PARKING, so this is not started from nothing. Today\'s work already set the SIX ledger\nkinds (reply, queue, send, onair, giveup, cancel) to mode `keep` as a RULE — never purged, and\nretention() refuses a TTL on them. That part is settled and is NOT what this asks about.\n\nWhat this asks about is everything else, which has never been derived:\n\n  obs      log  24 h / 500 rows     the only kind with a considered bound\n  alarm    log  no limits           "the primary function, kept forever, on purpose"\n  devstate latest                   one row per subject\n  said     latest                   one row per subject\n  witness  NO POLICY ROW            41,863 rows in 6 days — the firehose, unbounded\n  beat     NO POLICY ROW            14,202 rows in 6 days — unbounded\n  overdue / returned / schedule / pointer.aim / orphan / probe.undefined\n                                    NO POLICY ROW — all unbounded by omission\n\nMeasured 2026-08-19 on data/bridge.db, 6.0 days old (08-13 08:04Z -> now), 64,142 rows total:\n  witness 41863, beat 14202, alarm 6740, overdue 428, returned 423, pointer.aim 416,\n  reply 40, orphan 26, send 15, queue 8, onair 8, schedule 2, probe.undefined 2, devstate 1\n\nSO THE REAL FINDING BEHIND THIS ASK: witness and beat are 87% of the store and neither has a policy.\nThey survive by the same omission that was just fixed for the ledger — retain() returns early with no\npolicy row. Nobody decided they were unbounded.\n\n/derive APPLIES. Every number must come from something measured, not picked: rows per day per kind,\nbytes per row, what each kind is actually USED for and by whom (devstate.js, schedule.js measured(),\nthe pointer plugin\'s history, /events replay depth), and the disk the deployment has. The replay cap\nof 2000 events was itself derived from 1% of preemptMs — the same discipline applies here.\n\nALSO IN SCOPE: `probe.undefined` is almost certainly a bug in a plugin\'s kind name, not a real kind.\n2 rows. Worth naming while counting.\n\nDO NOT start this without a spec — it changes what gets deleted from the only record of what the\nunits have ever said.'}
