2026-08-19 09:39:25,101 1774009 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'THE STANDING REGISTER OF OPEN BRIDGE WORK. Not a one-shot task and never completed as a whole.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-19: "this is more of a management / long term task rather than a one shot task."\n\nHOW TO USE IT\n  - One step per item. Pick ONE, run it through /idiot with its own spec, mark that step done.\n  - A step is closed only when the fix is deployed AND verified on the live service.\n  - New findings are APPENDED as steps here rather than opened as new tasks, so there is one place\n    to look. The exception is a finding big enough to need its own spec and history — then open a\n    task and leave a step here pointing at it.\n  - This task stays active. Do not call plan_task_complete on it.\n\nWHY IT EXISTS. Everything on it was found on 2026-08-18/19 while chasing one unanswered ping, and\nall of it was recorded on the task `schema-hash-blinded-the-bridge` as steps. That task\'s own work\nshipped, so the leftovers needed somewhere durable that is not "step 14 of a closed investigation".'}
2026-08-19 09:39:54,680 1774009 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'WHERE THE EVIDENCE FOR EACH STEP LIVES. Every item was measured on 2026-08-18/19; nothing here is\nreasoned from reading code alone. `origin` is the step number on task `schema-hash-blinded-the-bridge`,\nwhich holds the full measurement notes.\n\n 1  rxid never read          src/bridge.js:856 stores comms.lastRx, nothing acts on it.  origin 4\n                             Cost: GARG\'s 22:13Z ping resent twice while rxid already named it.\n 2  telemetry counts as beat src/classify.js:126 maps TELEMETRY_APP/POSITION_APP/NODEINFO_APP.  origin 5\n                             GARG read overdue:false, missed:0 while 56 obs frames failed to decode.\n 3  no command provenance    src/bridge.js:1080 logs QUEUE <unit> <text>; record is {type,at,unit,\n                             text,queued}. Three doors: POST /queue, the queue file, --send.  origin 6\n                             The 08-13 09:46Z `reboot` of the deployed unit cannot be attributed.\n 4  no alert on decode fail  Mismatch goes to the stored frame\'s decodeError and nowhere else.  origin 9\n                             device measured "no hash-mismatch line in bridge-out.log" and CORRECTLY\n                             concluded the wrong thing, because the bridge hid it. 56 refusals.\n 5  inFlight leaks           src/bridge.js:1237 counts pending; giveup at :956-980 dequeues but never\n                             clears pending.  origin 13.  GARG read inFlight:1 nine hours stale.\n 6  heardAt regresses        Restore at 07:30:03Z gave GARG heardAt 07:13:16Z while the store already\n                             held 07:28:25Z. contact.overdue computed off it -> false overdue on BOTH\n                             units.  origin 16.  Fix: never let heardAt go backwards; take the later\n                             of snapshot and store.\n 7  no azimuth at arrival    GET /pointer read az 141 against an aim of 121-123.  origin 17\n                             GARG answers at -118 dBm relayed, so 19 deg is not cosmetic.\n 8  restart discards queue   Found 08:26Z by doing it: a ping queued 08:15:07Z was gone after the\n                             restart, no cancel, no giveup. Contradicts the 202 contract this repo\n                             just wrote into /schema ("transmitted when the bridge next hears").\n 9  round-trip blind to      /health startedAt changing mid-run makes the run VOID. It is detectable\n    a restart                and undetected; the run sat toward a 46-minute backstop instead.\n10  round-trip reads little  4 of 16 event kinds; ignores measured.landing (in-window vs radiated),\n                             comms.lastRx, comms.answering, direct-vs-relayed, overdue/returned/\n                             schedule/pointer.aim.  origin 14 has the candidate hop list.\n11  wire-projection hash     device\'s canonical form ACCEPTED verbatim on channel device--bridge item\n                             hash-covers-comments (their #3, my #6). They change gen_frames.py, I\n                             match, both land together.  origin 1 and 2.\n                             ADDENDUM THAT MUST NOT BE LOST: the presence bitmap is ceil(n/8) and is\n                             NOT on the wire, so append-only is transparent only until the field count\n                             crosses a multiple of 8. obs is at 18 of 24.\n12  close the /schema item   Fixed and deployed 2026-08-19 (202/400/403/404/409, DELETE +404), told\n                             html as #25. Mine to resolve once they confirm.\n13  chase plugins            replay-delivers-replies-twice ACK since 2026-08-18. Fix deployed; open\n                             only until they say whether anything of theirs counted replies under it.\n14  BNCH beat                Set to 60000 ms at 07:23Z for testing, on Peter\'s instruction, and never\n                             restored. Duty cycle on a real unit. Its config frame confirms 60000.\n15  must did not re-clamp    MtCmd.cpp calls clampMustSend on a beat change, yet BNCH\'s config frame\n                             at 07:23:06Z still read must=21600000 at a 60 s beat. device\'s, unraised.\n16  no debug console         The dongle at ttyACM1 matches rak-dongle\'s marker but --capture produces\n                             NO FILE, so hop 4 is unobservable on BOTH units, not just the deployed\n                             one. Peter: do not assume BNCH has USB or the dongle connected.\n17  probe.undefined          2 rows in the store under that kind name. Almost certainly a plugins bug.\n                             Belongs to plugins if confirmed - raise, do not reach in.\n\nSEE ALSO, parked separately because it is a sizeable derivation of its own:\n  park-derive-retention-per-table - witness 41,863 and beat 14,202 rows are 87% of the store and\n  neither has a retention policy at all.'}
