2026-08-19 09:40:56,283 1748124 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "`npm test` must go red when a renderer in `public/app.js` throws.\n\nToday the suite is 42 static checks over the source text — it never executes\napp.js, so every runtime break this session reached Peter's screen instead of the\nsuite: `NO_STRING is not defined`, `paintCommand is not defined`, `selected is not\ndefined`, and a python slice that deleted the entire board section. All four were\n42/42 green.\n\nDone means: a test boots app.js against a shim DOM, feeds it a captured `/state`\nand a few captured events, renders the board and the Control page, and fails on a\nthrown error. Falsified by breaking a renderer on purpose and watching it go red."}
2026-08-19 09:42:31,207 1748124 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': "**clock-swallows-subscriber-errors** — CONFIRMED, out of scope for `smoke-test`.\n\n`public/clock.js:32-35`:\n\n```js\nsetInterval(() => {\n  const now = Date.now();\n  for (const fn of subs) { try { fn(now); } catch { /* a bad subscriber is not the clock's problem */ } }\n}, 1000);\n```\n\nThe catch is empty and silent. Every value on the page that moves without a data\npush — the elapsed times, the draining bars, the header clock — is patched inside\nthat subscriber, so **a throw anywhere in the tick path is discarded with no log,\nno console error and no visible effect except that the numbers stop moving.**\n\nFound while sizing the smoke test: the test cannot detect a broken tick handler by\nwatching for a thrown error, because nothing ever escapes. That is a property of\nthe page, not of the test.\n\nDeliberate as written, and the intent is right — one bad subscriber must not stop\nthe clock for the others. What is wrong is that it is silent. A `console.error(e)`\nin that catch would keep the isolation and end the invisibility.\n\nNOT FIXED HERE: `clock.js` is not in the `smoke-test` spec's scope. Recorded so\nthe next session does not rediscover it, and so the smoke test's own limits are\nstated: it proves the render paths do not throw, and proves nothing about the tick\npath until this catch speaks."}
