2026-08-19 09:43:05,589 1774009 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'TOOL onboard this repo to flow — authored charts, because flow_derive has no javascript backend', 'description': 'Investigated 2026-08-19, nothing created. `docs/flow/` does not exist, so this repo has never been\ncharted.\n\nMEASURED STATE\n\n  flow_derive inventory .   "36 javascript file(s) in ., and 0 python file(s) — flow_derive derives\n                             from python only"  -> the AUTHORED path\n  dashboard :8800            200, already running. Do NOT start a second one; it fails silently.\n  flow_dash projects         flow, idiot, device.  bridge is NOT subscribed, so it is invisible.\n  size                       5,768 lines over 14 modules; src/bridge.js alone is 1,295\n\nWHY IT MATTERS THAT WE ARE ABSENT RATHER THAN EMPTY. device is on the board with 7 charts and 4\nUNKNOWN. An absent row reads as "nothing wrong here", which for this repo is badly wrong while the\nregister above holds 17 items.\n\nTHE COST IS REAL AND MUST NOT BE UNDERSTATED. No javascript backend means the agent IS the parser:\nread the code, follow the calls, hand-write every node with `src: file:line`, then `flow_derive stamp .`\nso drift watches it. Charts must NOT be written from filenames — the skill is explicit that a chart\nnamed from structure is a guess dressed as an answer.\n\nCANDIDATE AREAS, from code actually read during the 2026-08-18/19 investigation rather than from\ndirectory names:\n\n  wire      decode a frame, refuse one whose bytes do not match the schema   frames.js, classify.js\n  queue     accept a command, spend it on a heard contact, settle or give up  bridge.js\n  contact   decide whether a unit is awake, overdue, or returned              devstate.js, schedule.js\n  callers   decide who may command the units                                 callers.js, api.js\n  store     what is kept, what is purged, what is never purged               db.js\n  surface   what the bridge publishes about itself                           surface.js, api.js\n  plugins   what a plugin may and may not reach                              plugins.js\n  aim       point the shared rotator, hold, release                          plugins/pointer\n\nSTART WITH `queue` ALONE. It is the area that has cost the most this week and one area is enough to\nget the repo subscribed and visible. Its real holes are already known and would draw red honestly:\nrxid unread (step 1), telemetry counted as a beat (step 2), heardAt regressing (step 6), the queue\ndiscarded on restart (step 8). Red must mean undetermined-or-unhandled, never merely unfinished — so\nthose four qualify and most of the rest of the module does not.\n\nDO NOT do all eight in one pass, and do not skip `flow_dash subscribe` — a repo charted but not\nsubscribed is invisible and nothing says so.'}
