2026-08-19 10:30:20,965 1787535 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': '**Peter, 2026-08-19, verbatim (/ij):**\n\n> *"this needs a favicon I cannot easily find it in my tabs."*\n\n**My reading:** every page this tool serves — chart pages and the dashboard — renders with no `<link rel="icon">`, so browsers show the default blank/globe and a row of flow tabs is indistinguishable from every other tab. I had already SEEN the evidence and filed it as somebody else\'s problem: the only console error on a chart page is a 404 for `/favicon.ico`, and I wrote it off as "the dashboard\'s to answer, not a chart\'s". It was a real defect and Peter felt it before I acted on it.\n\n**What done means now:** a chart page and the dashboard both carry an embedded icon — a data: URI, since a chart page must stay a standalone file you can send to somebody, and an external icon file would break that the moment the page travelled. Distinctive at 16px, and drawn from the existing palette rather than a new colour.\n\nApplied inside the test-point task rather than parked, because these are the same pages I am editing and the icon has to survive the template changes.'}
