2026-08-19 10:42:57,322 1774009 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "BUG round-trip's dirty-queue guard tested queued only, so a leaked POST did not stop a run", 'description': "FIXED 2026-08-19 alongside step 5, same spec. Recorded as its own step because I first marked step 9\ncomplete for this work and step 9 is a DIFFERENT gap (detecting a mid-run bridge restart via\n/health startedAt, still open).\n\nbin/round-trip.js tested `st.queued > 0` while PRINTING `st.pending` in its own refusal message. So a\nbridge holding leaked in-flight POSTs with an empty queue passed the guard, the run started, and hop 9\nthen failed for a state that predated the run — a finding about the previous hour reported as this\nrun's result.\n\nMeasured: /stats read `queued 0, pending 2` at 09:20Z and `queued 0, pending 3` at 09:38Z.\n\nFIXED by extracting the decision into `dirtyQueue(st)` and refusing on either counter, with the message\nnaming WHICH tripped — the two remedies differ: DELETE clears a queue, only a restart clears a POST\nthe bridge never released.\n\nAND CHECK 4 CAUGHT A BAD TEST HERE. My first test grepped round-trip.js for `st.pending > 0` and PASSED\nwith the fix reverted, because that string still appeared in the message body below the guard. A test\nthat cannot fail is not a test. The extraction into a function is what made a behaviour test possible;\nthe second version fails correctly with the fix removed.\n\nnpm test 282 pass / 0 fail."}
