2026-08-19 11:59:11,728 1797750 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Onboard this repo to flow so the charts become a check rather than decoration.\n\nPeter chose, 2026-08-19: archive the hand-drawn charts to .off, then derive. The eight existing charts carry 0 src: lines across 94 nodes, so stamp records nothing and drift can never watch them; and enforce.yaml\'s first decision is "an edit tool? no -> exit 0 permit", the exact branch shell_hook replaced today. No chart mentions the shell guard at all.\n\nThey could not be left in place: assignment() refuses unless all 58 symbols are assigned, any area holding a function makes draw attempt a write, and refuse_to_clobber then kills the run. Its own docstring names this repo as the ordinary case for that refusal.'}
2026-08-19 11:59:22,273 1797750 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Spec: docs/specs/onboard-idiot-to-flow.md\n\nNine areas, named from reading the code: locate, derive, closure, evidence, verbs, rulings, enforce, shell, lifecycle. `shell` is new — today's guard, charted for the first time, and the area that has misfired four times so the one most worth a picture. `lifecycle` is a cross-area overview with no symbols of its own, so it can never be derived: it STAYS in place declared symbols: [], which is what refuse_to_clobber recommends for an authored chart. Archiving it would turn a real overview into UNKNOWN. The other seven are archived to docs/flow/.off/.\n\nAll 58 module-level symbols assigned — 45 in idiot.py, 13 in idiot_gate.py. Seven names are defined in both files and must be written file:name because a bare name is refused rather than guessed: STATE_ROOT, hook, load, main, mtime, save, state_dir. Constants are assigned too; assignment is the decision, drawing is what happens to be possible.\n\nThe mv into .off needs IDIOT_ALLOW_SHELL_WRITE=1 because the destination is inside a registered repo and mv is a write verb. Announced out loud, which is the arrangement the override exists for.\n\nFalsify: drift must match BY HASH and must go red if a cited file changes afterwards — a drift check that cannot fail watches nothing. The red nodes on a rendered chart must be real holes, never a refusal the code makes correctly; if everything is red the derivation misread the code and that is reported, not shipped. Subscribe must make the repo appear with no restart."}
