2026-08-19 12:38:53,686 1797750 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '~/.claude/skills/since/SKILL.md, 91 lines. Spec at docs/specs/since-skill.md, committed fd74b12. Confirmed live in the skill listing as `since`.\n\nClosed verdict set, no adverbs: DONE PARTLY FAILED BLOCKED REFUSED. "mostly done" is PARTLY; a qualifier is always the true verdict hiding under a better-sounding one.\n\nTHE RULE IT EXISTS FOR: a self-reported success is exactly what this repo distrusts — /idiot was built because assertions were passing for evidence, and the register refuses to close on anybody\'s word. A summary is not exempt, so every DONE carries the thing Peter can re-run (a SHA, a count, a pasted line), and a verdict with nothing attachable is downgraded to UNVERIFIED rather than asserted.\n\nScope is since his LAST message, not the session. Two categories kept apart: what he asked for (the verdict is about this only) and what I did anyway (included only when it changes what he does next). Fifteen-line hard cap; when the verdict is not DONE the fault leads.\n\nFalsified against its own format: a dry run summarising this very turn came to 7 lines, inside the cap, defect last only because the verdict was DONE.'}
