2026-08-19 18:26:04,902 1797750 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Commit ded77e1. Spec docs/specs/idiot-refreshes-flow.md.\n\nPHASE 4 gains `flow_derive drift .` and `flow_prove .`. A red drift there is the EXPECTED answer when charted code changed — the picture saying it moved, with a diff naming what appeared and vanished. Drift red in an area the change did NOT touch is a finding. flow_prove red is a real failure that outranks the task.\n\nPHASE 5 step 4 refreshes before the commit and into it: draw, render, index, stamp, prove, drift. Charts go in the SAME commit as the code — split across two and everybody else pulls a tree whose drift is red through no fault of theirs, and a red that is somebody else\'s fault is a red nobody reads.\n\nCOST MEASURED, so nobody later invents a skip-if-busy rule: drift 228ms, draw 309, render 363, index 218, stamp 261, prove 844 — about 2.0s total, against suites in the same phase taking minutes.\n\nAnti-rubber-stamp rules: stamp is a JUDGEMENT ("I looked, the chart is still true"), not a step, and running it to silence a warning is forging evidence. A NEW hole is a finding and gets an entry; a hole count FALLING with nobody fixing anything means the derivation stopped seeing something and is worse. A red node must be real — a false one goes to the flow repo, never hand-edited out.\n\nNot-charted repos are reported and pointed at /flow_onboard, never silently skipped.\n\nWalked end to end on this repo: every command runs from the root, drift green after redraw, 8 points 0 failed, index 9 charts 3 holes.\n\nRAISED WITH FLOW while doing it, channel flow--idiot: #1 the while-True back-edge drawn as a hole, #3 proof.yaml counted as a chart so flow_prove\'s own output renders as an undeclared tenth area — flow --areas says 9, flow_dash says 10. Both inflate the one number on that page anybody acts on. Neither worked around.'}
