2026-08-19 18:36:32,503 1797750 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Commit d32bbe4. Spec docs/specs/handover-marks-what-was-used.md.\n\nClosed marker set on both sections: used (work went through it, if wrong the work is wrong) / checked (run only to write the handover, nothing rested on it) / unused (not run this session, carried forward on trust).\n\nunused is NOT a failing — most instruments are irrelevant on a given day — and marking it honestly is the only thing that makes `used` mean anything. NOTHING IS DROPPED FOR BEING UNUSED: the section exists to name instruments nobody remembers, so deleting untouched rows deletes exactly those. They sort to the bottom.\n\nTwo dependent rules updated so the column is not decoration:\n- the write-up check now says a row run only while writing the handover is `checked`, not `used`. Promoting it is the small lie the column exists to prevent.\n- READ MODE step 4 now walks the `unused` rows FIRST — never run by the last session, possibly not the one before, so most likely broken and least likely to be missed until it matters. A table with no unused rows is flagged as written from memory.\n\nPEERS also gains a wider inventory: xs.py inbox shows only where you are seated, so `ls ~/.xsession/` is the real list — 26 channels on this machine against 1 seated.\n\nFALSIFIED by producing both tables for this session, which corrected two things I would have written from memory:\n- flow--idiot has NO seen/ directory at all. flow has never read any of the 4 messages; "cursor 0" would have been the wrong derivation.\n- device--idiot: device is at 16 of 16 and has CAUGHT UP. This morning\'s /handover read reported it 3 behind — now stale, which is exactly why the skill says re-run inbox last.'}
