2026-08-19 19:06:19,432 1876987 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bridge-backlog', 'kind': 'note', 'text': '/ij Peter, 2026-08-19, VERBATIM:\n\n"well tyhe issue now is the unrelaiability of the command / response system. /investigate and refer to the meshtastic phone app code for how they do it. we have achieved 100% hit rate in the past. do NOT blame the devices, this is a bridge issue 100%."\n\n"I also suggest that you chat with mesh-gw tell them the problem and see if they can uncover anything helpful"\n\nMY READING (check it against the quotes above, not instead of them):\n- The investigation is scoped to the BRIDGE. The device and the RF path are not candidates.\n- "100% hit rate in the past" is a real prior measurement, not an aspiration - so look for what regressed, not for a reason it was always broken. Measured this session: 28 of 29 = 97% for first attempts that hit the air on the good phase.\n- The phone app is the reference for how send/ack SHOULD be done.\n- mesh-gw is to be told the problem and asked what they can see. This is an ASK, not a handoff - the defect stays ours.\n\nINVESTIGATION RESULT (read-only, no fix applied), two bridge defects, both required:\n1. devstate.js:246 treats every obs frame as opening a burst (one obs per 300s wake always clears the beat/2 test), so devstate.js:111-114 declares LISTENING off whatever frame arrived last. On alternate wakes the frame heard was the DRAIN frame, transmitted at wake+10001ms - after rxdone at +9960ms, i.e. after the RX window shut. The bridge then fires into a closed window and records sentInState "listening". Wrong on all ten failures. The code comment at devstate.js:684 already says win "cannot tell an announce from a drain frame"; a0ca4d7 fixed that for wake PREDICTION and never applied it to the send gate.\n2. Retransmissions reuse the packet id, so the radio suppresses them as duplicates: sends:1 gets sent->queued->relayed->no_ack, sends:2 and 3 get sent->no_ack with no queued and no relayed ever.\n\nDevice is exonerated by its own console: woke= values exactly 300000ms apart, zero drift, and device txgo spacing 291952/308048ms matches bridge arrival spacing 292.0/308.1s exactly.'}
