2026-08-19 19:49:11,961 1876987 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bridge-backlog', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'THE FOUR PHASES — command/response reliability, 2026-08-19\n\nPeter: "so create a few 3 or 4 phases. all will be done with /idiot."\n\nEvery item below is an /idiot accusation in idiot.yaml: spec, test red, fix, test green, prove. One at a time. A phase is done when every accusation in it is CLOSED, not when the code looks right.\n\nORDERED BY DEPENDENCY, not by size. The one-line reason: phases 2 and 3 can only be PROVED in the field through the instrument built in phase 1, because deploying either of them restarts the bridge and a restart currently empties the lifecycle.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 1 - SEE IT.  Nothing downstream can be verified until this holds.\n\n  the-lifecycle-ssot-is-memory-only-so-a-restart-empties-it   REGISTERED, UNTRIED\n      spec docs/spec/the-command-lifecycle-is-a-state-machine.md already attached.\n      GET /commands/{unit}?settled=1 -> [] while 340 rows sit on disk, retention \'keep\',\n      never purged. Rebuild commandsFor() from the ledger: stateOf() already DERIVES rather\n      than stores and every event is keyed by packet id, so it is the same function over rows\n      instead of over a Map.\n      Work was abandoned mid-Phase-3 here by the previous session - registered and red-tested,\n      fix not started. Check what its trial actually recorded before re-deriving it.\n\n  step 25 - keep the whole status ladder, not just the terminal state       NEEDS AN ACCUSATION\n      sent / queued / relayed / no_ack / queue_failed each mean something different and we\n      keep only the last. `sent` with no `queued` means the radio never accepted the packet -\n      that is the discriminator mesh-gw pointed out we already had and were reading past.\n\n  DONE WHEN: a command\'s full history survives a restart and is readable from ONE route, and\n  "how far did this packet get" is a query rather than an investigation. Peter asked for\n  delivery statistics repeatedly today and every answer needed ad-hoc SQL.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 2 - STOP DOING HARM.  Peter\'s standing ruling, said numerous times.\n\n  step 23 - rip out our retry loop entirely\n      "let mesh-gw and the radios do their job". Ours reused the packet id and was destroyed\n      by the mesh 100 percent of the time - sends:2 and 3 never reached queued or relayed.\n      maxSends is doing THREE jobs; only :1442 is the retry budget. :1426 is the post-receipt\n      patience budget and MUST SURVIVE with its own name. :1861 is round-trip\'s timeout\n      arithmetic and breaks when maxSends goes.\n\n  a-retransmission-never-enters-the-mesh-because-we-reuse-the-packet-id     UNTRIED\n      Now fully explained and largely superseded by the above. Decide whether it closes as\n      part of step 23 or stays as its own entry - do not leave it dangling.\n\n  DONE WHEN: a command is transmitted exactly once, no id is ever reused, and nothing in the\n  bridge schedules a retransmission.\n  SAY THIS PLAINLY WHEN REPORTING: this does not move the hit rate. It removes a mechanism\n  that never worked. Phase 3 is what moves the hit rate.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 3 - FIX DELIVERY.  This is the hit rate.\n\n  step 22 - the send gate fires on ANY frame heard        THE PRIMARY DEFECT\n      0 of 7 when we fired on the drain frame, 28 of 29 when we fired on the announce.\n      devstate.js:246 + :111-114. Gate LISTENING on phase against the PREDICTED wake, which\n      devstate already computes, not against the arrival of whatever frame came last.\n\n  step 24 - our own witness radio cancels the sending radio\'s 3 retransmissions\n      CONFIRM FIRST, do not fix on inference: WS /{node_id}/events, mesh-gw\'s per-device\n      stream, which we have never used. It separates the two radios and would show YAGI\n      rebroadcasting an OMNI packet id. The firmware logic and "never witnessed twice, 45 of\n      45" are measured; the YAGI attribution is not.\n      Peter, 2026-08-19: mesh-gw is the phone app\'s BLE layer and filters nothing - "only with\n      multiple radios". The extra radio is the one thing our setup has that the reference\n      implementation does not, so suspect it for anything that differs.\n\n  DONE WHEN: hit rate measured over a full day from the phase-1 instrument, not from SQL.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPHASE 4 - CONTRACT, LEDGER HYGIENE, TIDY.\n\n  step 26 - GET /commands is declared in /schema and 404s. Test it the way surface.test.js\n            already tests the queue codes: every declared path answers on its declared transport.\n  step 28 - retention declares kind \'received\' with zero rows ever written; device\'s cursor is\n            6 against our ask at seq 7 so it is UNREAD not unanswered; two peer items await Peter.\n  step 27 - no git remote. 29 commits exist only on this disk. PETER\'S CALL, do not invent one.\n\n  REGISTER HYGIENE, and this one matters because a false accusation is worse than none:\n  the-loss-is-on-the-return-path-not-the-command-path   UNTRIED - and TODAY\'S MEASUREMENT\n      DISPROVES IT. The loss was on the command path: the device received nothing at all, rx=0\n      on every window. This entry should be withdrawn with the evidence, not left open to\n      mislead the next session. It is already listed in the handover\'s GOT WRONG as a theory\n      stated before it was measured.\n\n  Also still open and untouched by any of the above, listed so they are not forgotten:\n      the-send-record-reports-the-default-radio-and-channel-not-the-ones-used\n      a-plugin-can-replace-the-resolved-channel-with-a-raw-index\n      the-psk-fingerprint-the-resolver-matches-on-is-a-hardcoded-default\n      the-command-and-device-state-machines-are-not-gated-against-each-other  (not-reproduced)\n      the-seam-test-is-load-sensitive-and-flaked-once                         (not-reproduced)\n  The two not-reproduced entries need Peter\'s ruling; reasons are already written to\n  ~/.claude/idiot-state/214793a468849830/acquit-*\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nIF PETER WANTS PHASE 2 FIRST it is a cheap swap - step 23 does not depend on phase 1 to be\nBUILT, only to be PROVED in the field. Say which was done first when reporting.'}
