2026-08-19 20:04:36,580 1876987 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bridge-backlog', 'title': 'BUG the send record names the radio and channel we did NOT transmit on', 'description': 'PHASE 1 of the four-phase reliability plan (note 2759), and it goes FIRST because the /idiot gate blocks on it: `the-send-record-reports-the-default-radio-and-channel-not-the-ones-used` is untried and names src/bridge.js, so no edit to that file is permitted until it is settled.\n\nRegister entry: the-send-record-reports-the-default-radio-and-channel-not-the-ones-used\nSpec: docs/spec/the-send-record-names-the-radio-it-did-not-use.md\n\nsrc/bridge.js:945-946 resolves useRadio/useChannel (a before:send hook may override either, src/plugins.js:410). :951 and :964 transmit on those. :1007 and :1008 then log and publish the CONSTRUCTOR DEFAULTS instead.\n\nA CONSUMER IS ALREADY MISLED: bin/round-trip.js:655 lifts radio: ev.radio off the send event and :661/:974 print "via ${ev.radio}". The tool that exists to audit the bridge prints a radio it cannot know.\n\nAND IT COST THIS SESSION A FALSE STEP. While investigating the delivery failure I read radio/channel out of ten send ledger records, saw they were identical across the failure boundary, and used that to rule out a radio or channel switch. They are the defaults and would read identically however the frames were sent - the check established nothing. The investigation\'s conclusion is unaffected (it rests on the 0-of-7 versus 28-of-29 phase split and the device\'s own console, both independent of this field) but the step was unsound.\n\nTHE CHANGE IS TWO IDENTIFIERS at :1007 and :1008 - radio -> useRadio, channel -> useChannel. Nothing about which radio is CHOSEN changes.\n\nNOT CHANGED, deliberately: src/plugins.js:410 (that is the separate raw-index accusation) and bin/round-trip.js (it reads the field correctly; once the field is true it is true, with no edit).'}
