2026-08-19 20:33:04,390 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Audit mesh-gw\'s BLE layer against the Meshtastic phone app\'s, which is the reference implementation this repo emulates (Peter\'s standing rule, 2026-08-19).\n\nRESULT: five deltas found, THREE WITHDRAWN on evidence, two shipped in 1a0e079. The main finding is that mesh-gw is closer to the reference than the first pass claimed, and that my own first pass contained the same error I had spent the day correcting in two peer sessions.\n\nWITHDRAWN:\n- an-offline-device-is-never-retried-again — FALSE. I claimed OFFLINE was terminal without following the caller. _do_reconnect() returning None sets session_done=\'idle\', breaks, and with auto_connect falls through to CONNECTING where connect retries forever. Disproof was already visible: 6 OFFLINE transitions in 27h and the gateway is up.\n- a-failed-ble-operation-is-never-retried — all 22 Bleak exceptions in 27h are UNLIKELY_ERROR teardowns, where retrying is wrong. Zero cases the app\'s retryBleOperation would have changed.\n- concurrent-writes-to-toradio-are-unserialised — ATT permits one outstanding request and BlueZ queues; no test could be stated that would be red for a real defect rather than for "no mutex exists".\n\nSHIPPED (1a0e079), one mechanism, two uses:\n- ToRadio(heartbeat nonce=0) after heartbeat_after_silence_s of no FROMRADIO. Our liveness check was client.is_connected — BlueZ\'s LOCAL opinion, blind to a radio wedged behind a live ACL. The firmware answers a heartbeat with a queueStatus, which is the only end-to-end evidence a BLE client can get.\n- POST /{node_id}/nodeinfo_ping -> nonce=1, the firmware\'s NodeInfo ping (PhoneAPI.cpp): rebroadcasts our public key on the 60s path instead of the 10-minute cooldown.\n\n120s derived from 62,756 measured FROMRADIO gaps over 27h: worst silence 60.2s, 2x that, fires on 0 of 62,756.\n\nSTILL OUTSTANDING at the time of writing:\n- scripts/check_specs.py reports 4 stale specs (nordic_dfu_session, ota_config_yaml, ota_state_decision_tree, region_unset_bootstrap), all pre-existing and all against core/config.py + core/bridge_config.yaml. NOT resynced: a hash resync asserts "unchanged since last set" and I have not read the config they describe.\n- the firmware-side effect of nonce=1 is being verified separately; the earlier 90s window was inconclusive against a 40/hour baseline.\n- repo is not charted (no docs/flow/areas.yaml) so flow_derive/flow_prove could not run in Phase 4.'}
2026-08-19 20:33:14,124 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Read the app's BLE layer from meshtastic/Meshtastic-Android main (BleRadioTransport.kt, BleExceptionClassifier.kt, BleRetry.kt, BleReconnectPolicy.kt, HeartbeatSender.kt, CommandSenderImpl.kt) and the firmware's PhoneAPI.cpp / ReliableRouter.cpp / NextHopRouter.cpp, compare behaviour by behaviour, and register every delta in idiot.yaml rather than in conversation.\n\nThen apply /derive to each: is it harmful to us, is it breaking for consumers. Withdraw anything evidence closes rather than carrying it. Build only what survives.\n\nOrder: red before fix, enforced by the register's hook. Falsify by removing the RULE with an unmutated control.\n\nDone: five registered, three withdrawn, two tried red / proved green / closed, committed 1a0e079 with idiot.yaml and .proofs."}
