2026-08-19 20:55:38,260 1876987 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bridge-backlog', 'title': 'AGREE mesh-gw resolves private/public - the bridge stops holding a channel index at all', 'description': 'PETER\'S RULING, 2026-08-19, VERBATIM:\n\n"I am fed up with the channel selection issue, it has come up half a dozen times today alone. mesh-gw will now accept a request using private or public instead of a channel index. so a send message would include the __ble_addr (or !macaddr ???) and private or public. mesh-gw will resolve. problem solved"\n\nAnd the design behind it, same day:\n\n"the reality is the caller should be isolated from channels and indexes completely. they should simply call xxx(__ble_addr|!macaddr, primary(public)/private)"\n\nMESH-GW IS IMPLEMENTING THIS NOW - Peter: "that change is in progress now, you can take my word for it." Do not raise it with them again and do not build resolution here.\n\nTHE ADDRESS HALF NEEDS NO CHANGE, measured 2026-08-19: mesh-gw\'s route is already /{node_id}/messages and /devices reports node_id \'!2687afb1\' with ble_addr None. The BLE MAC is a separate \'addr\' field (E9:B0:3F:17:27:91) and is not what the API takes. So we keep sending \'!2687afb1\' and only the channel field changes.\n\nWHAT THE BRIDGE DOES WHEN IT LANDS\n  - POST body sends channel: \'private\' instead of an integer (src/bridge.js:964).\n  - createBridge stops taking a `channel` at all (src/bridge.js:131, :244) - there is no index to hold.\n  - discover() stops resolving the channel (src/bridge.js:91-109). It may still be needed to list\n    READY radios, but the pskFp match, the multi-hit refusal and the assertPrivateChannel gate all\n    move to mesh-gw. Check before deleting: the >1-match refusal and the public-key hard gate are\n    real protections and must exist on THEIR side before they stop existing here.\n  - bin/bridged.js:68\'s hardcoded pskFp default \'cae97c03\' disappears with it, which closes\n    the-psk-fingerprint-the-resolver-matches-on-is-a-hardcoded-default.\n  - the before:send hook contract: a hook names a ROLE or nothing. Never an index, never a key.\n\nTWO OPEN ACCUSATIONS ARE SUPERSEDED BUT NOT YET FALSE - do not withdraw them until the switch lands,\nbecause both are live defects today:\n  a-plugin-can-replace-the-resolved-channel-with-a-raw-index\n  a-radio-redirect-keeps-the-channel-index-resolved-for-the-old-radio\nTheir fix is no longer "validate the index" - it is "there is no index". Whoever picks them up must\nread this step first or they will build the design Peter replaced.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT THAT MADE THE CASE, kept so it is not re-derived:\n  OMNI !2687afb1   index 2 = \'Private\'  psk VMJzIWRPo19v\n  YAGI !fa39f7b4   index 2 = \'Off\'      psk eM1YYHz9Bawi    (Private is index 1 here)\nThe bridge holds index 2 resolved for OMNI, so a hook changing ONLY the radio sends on \'Off\'.\n\nBLOCKED ON mesh-gw shipping. Until then src/bridge.js stays locked by the two accusations above.'}
