2026-08-20 04:37:20,012 1965319 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 34, 'text': 'PREMISE 4 OF THIS STEP IS NOT EVIDENCE AND MUST NOT BE REASONED FROM. Found 2026-08-20 03:55Z.\n\nThis step says: "The radio\'s own 3 retransmissions (NUM_RELIABLE_RETX, started on want_ack alone)\nnever happen: 45 of 45 witnessed transmissions were witnessed exactly once."\n\nPeter had already corrected the denominator (16 of 45 carry the field). The corrected number is\nequally worthless, and for a reason neither of us had: OUR WITNESS RADIO CANNOT HEAR A REPEAT OF AN\nID IT HAS ALREADY HEARD.\n\n  FloodingRouter::shouldFilterReceived()  -> TRUE for a packet already in PacketHistory\n  Router::handleReceivedFromRadio()       -> if (shouldFilterReceived(p)) { packetPool.release(p); return; }\n\nFiltered means handleReceived() is never called, so the packet never reaches the phone API, so\nmesh-gw never sees it, so the bridge never publishes `onair`. "Witnessed exactly once" is what the\ninstrument is BUILT to report whatever the air carried. Ledger agrees exactly: 45 onair rows, 45\ndistinct ids, none witnessed twice; of the 16 carrying `nth`, all 16 are nth=1.\n\nNOT a bookkeeping artefact - checked. `pending` is deleted only on `failed` (src/bridge.js:1224) and\nat give-up minutes later (:1627), so the witness path was live the whole time.\n\nWHAT REPLACES PREMISE 4: we do not know whether the radio retransmits, and no observer we own can\ntell us. The device console only sees its own 8000 ms window once per 300 s. Retransmissions are\ngenerated inside the radio and do not cross the phone API.\n\nAND THE HAZARD THAT MATTERS MORE, from mesh-gw seq 7: there is no broadcast ACK, so the firmware\nstops early on an IMPLICIT ack - perhapsGenerateImplicitAckForOwnOverheard - when it overhears ANY\nneighbour rebroadcast our packet. `relayed` in our ledger IS that implicit ack. It appears on 10 of\nthe 14 packet ids where we hold a status sequence. The relaying node is NO