2026-08-20 04:54:57,497 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "A traceroute can only be answered by nodes that can decrypt its channel, so a private-channel trace is answerable by our own two radios and nobody else — it comes back as anonymous placeholders. For a MESSAGE private is the safe answer; for a TRACEROUTE it is the useless one. Settle that inversion once, in the gateway, instead of making every caller know it.\n\nAdd a config option `ble.trace_force_public`. When set, mesh-gw ignores the caller's channel on /traceroute and sends on PRIMARY. It ignores the CHANNEL, never the request: it never refuses and never 400s. The override is reported back as `channel_forced` and logged, never applied silently."}
2026-08-20 04:55:03,473 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'core/config.py — add `trace_force_public: bool = False` to the BLE config block.\ncore/bridge_config.yaml — set it true for this deployment, with the reasoning beside it.\ncore/methods.py — in `traceroute()`, branch on the flag: when set, channel = primary_index(bridge.channels), never refuse, and compute `channel_forced` by resolving what the caller asked for and comparing. When unset, keep the existing "channel is required" refusal.\nmodule/models.py — declare `channel` and `channel_forced` on TracerouteResponse so pydantic does not strip them.\ntests/test_trace_force_public.py — six cases: forced+private, forced+nothing (must not 400), forced+0 (agreed, not forced), forced+renamed primary, unforced+private, unforced+nothing (must refuse).\ndocs/modules/trace_force_public.md — the spec.\n\nNOT changing: send_text. A message on a private channel is the correct and safe default there; only traceroute has the inversion.'}
