2026-08-20 06:12:31,682 1975532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/specs/idiot-skill-takes-verbs.md\n\nPeter, 2026-08-20, two refinements after seeing the candidate list:\n  "we dont need the -- do we ?"  -> no dashes. Bare verbs.\n  "can we have a help that shows the args available ?"  -> /idiot help.\n  "I do not plan to open seperated ssh session and call them directly from the command line."\n  -> the value is the register\'s OWN OUTPUT in the chat, not shell convenience. Every count I\n     report is a claim; a verb makes it evidence he did not have to trust me for.\n\nSIX VERBS, and the exclusions are half the design:\n  list [filter]      nine filters, from `idiot list -h`, never a hardcoded list\n  show <slug>        derived verdict, trial/fix commits, and WHICH RUNG closed it\n  proof <slug>       the captured red and green output from .proofs/ -- the anti-fabrication one\n  acquit <slug> "reason"   writes {"reason": ...} to the state dir and runs idiot acquit.\n                     Today I write that file for him: the party being ruled on transcribes the\n                     ruling. This is the only verb the tool\'s own model says is not the agent\'s.\n  withdraw <slug> "why"    he retracts his own wishes; I cannot clear the board by calling\n                     something a blocker.\n  help               prints the TOOL\'s real output, never a hardcoded list.\n\nNOT exposed, deliberately: try, prove, amend -- they produce verdicts, and a verdict must come\nfrom a test that ran, never from someone typing. add -- it needs --type/--spec/--file, so if he\nsupplies only the sentence then I choose all three and file it under his name.\nCannot exist yet: verify (re-run every recorded test at HEAD). idiot has no such verb.\n\nDISAMBIGUATION, since there are no dashes to key on. The first word is a register verb AND its\nargument resolves -> command. Otherwise -> problem description, workflow starts.\n  /idiot list open              -> `open` is a known filter -> command\n  /idiot show <existing-slug>   -> the slug is in the register -> command\n  /idiot show me why it fails   -> `me` is not a slug -> problem description\nA verb whose argument does not resolve SAYS SO and stops. It must not silently start a\nfive-phase cycle on a typo.\n  /idiot bare stays the workflow -- CLAUDE.md has it implied on every task.\n\nNO REGISTER ENTRY IS POSSIBLE. ~/.claude/skills/idiot/SKILL.md is in no git repo, and closure\nasks whether a named file changed in THIS repo, so an entry naming it could never close.\nPrecedent 7cf725a did the skill work as ordinary work and registered only the defect inside\nidiot.py. Phases still apply; there is just no accusation.\n\nHELP MUST NOT GO STALE. The last session\'s defect class was documentation that does not parse:\nidiot.py documented and PRINTED `acquit --id <slug>`, which argparse refuses. So `help` runs the\ntool and shows what it says, and the skill carries no second copy of the verb list.'}
