2026-08-20 06:40:26,622 1975532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/specs/idiot-mine.md\n\nTwo sources for "blocking on Peter":\n  1. verdict not-reproduced -- the tool\'s own definition, authoritative and derived. Zero today.\n  2. a pending ask-<slug> file in state_dir -- written by the agent when it hands a decision\n     over, removed when the decision is taken.\n\nstate_dir is derived, never hardcoded:\n  python3 -c "import idiot; print(idiot.state_dir(\'.\'))"  -> /root/.claude/idiot-state/99d6ba2d02a80688\nIt is sha256(abspath(repo))[:16] under STATE_ROOT, so `.` and the absolute path agree. Another\nrepo\'s directory already exists there holding a different project\'s ruling -- do not confuse them.\n\nACTIONS ARE DERIVED FROM THE VERDICT, because do_acquit refuses anything that is not\nnot-reproduced and exits 2. Offering acquit on an untried entry would be printing an invocation\nthat cannot run, which is the defect this repo already convicted.\n  not-reproduced -> acquit, withdraw, show evidence\n  otherwise open -> withdraw, show evidence\n  closed         -> show evidence only\n\nEvidence BEFORE the ruling: offer show and proof first, so he rules on the captured red and\ngreen rather than on my summary.\n\nHis words go in verbatim. do_acquit writes them to RULING_LOG and into ruling.why. A ruling\nparaphrased by the party being ruled on is not a ruling.\n\nAfter acquit or withdraw, REMOVE the ask- file. do_acquit removes its own acquit- file and\nknows nothing about ask-, so a stale one keeps an answered question on his list forever.\n\nRegistered, blocked behind the four untried entries that lock idiot.py:\n  nothing-records-that-an-entry-is-waiting-on-peter (new)\n  schema-omits-the-ruling-field-it-writes (bug)'}
