2026-08-20 10:18:27,297 1975532 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/specs/handover-priorities.md\n\nREMAINS lists what is left and is UNORDERED. Nothing says which one first, so the next session\neither picks by whatever caught its eye or re-derives the order -- work the previous session was\nbest placed to do.\n\nMeasured on this repo, 2026-08-20: gate-after-exit-can-be-typed appears in three consecutive\nhandovers. The skill already says three appearances is a different problem from one, and there\nwas no section where that observation changed anything.\n\nPRIORITIES: 3-7 items, ordered, each carrying the constraint that forces its position. Rules:\n  - item 1 must be actionable without anybody\'s permission, or the session stalls on line one\n  - a blocker outranks a task and is named with WHAT IT UNBLOCKS (cli-styling locked idiot.py)\n  - [carried N], counted by grep over docs/handover/*.md, and three means the priority was\n    wrong rather than the item hard\n  - split by who is blocked: ours / Peter\'s (belongs to /idiot mine) / a peer\'s (name channel\n    and slug)\n  - DERIVED from AUDIT, REMAINS and PEERS. An item that traces to none of them means one of\n    those sections is incomplete -- fix the source, do not carry an orphan\n  - written LAST, placed SECOND, directly after AUDIT, because a priority order built on\n    uncorrected beliefs is worse than none\n  - no "and then everything else"; do not order by effort\n\nFour edits to ~/.claude/skills/handover/SKILL.md: named-sections list, the section itself after\nAUDIT, one READ MODE step, one Before-finishing rule.\n\nNo register entry possible: the skill file is in no git repo. Precedent -- this repo already\nholds since-skill.md and one-idiot-skill-on-this-repo.md.'}
