2026-08-20 10:42:22,579 2028323 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'park-telemetry-onchange-with-obs-byte-flags', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-20, verbatim: "most importantly schema should not be rejected based on hash. appended elements and changes to the HR lables does not affect the integrity of the data sent, just means extra packets are not decoded. already told bridge that"\n\nCHECKED AGAINST THE CODE, both sides:\n- Bridge already complies. `bridge/src/frames.js:107-128` — "A HASH WE DO NOT RECOGNISE IS NO LONGER A REFUSAL"; changed 2026-08-19 after the 8 h / 56-refusal outage. A foreign hash now decodes and is marked `out.foreign` (`:171`). Validation is by exact byte consumption (`:158`), applied to our own frames too.\n- Device never rejects on hash at all — it only STAMPS it: `rak/lib/mt-reply/src/MtFrames.h:15` (SCHEMA_HASH 0x6911), `MtReply.cpp:90-91`. There is no firmware decode gate to remove.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE PROJECTION WORK (gen_frames.py hashing raw file bytes): it is no longer the fleet-breaking item the handover ranked first. Its remaining value is that a label/comment edit stops moving the hash, so `foreign` does not fire spuriously. Demoted, not dropped.\n\nONE PLACE PETER\'S RULE DOES NOT HOLD AS STATED — MEASURED, not inferred. An appended field that is PRESENT on the wire makes an un-updated decoder refuse the WHOLE frame, not ignore the extra:\n  cd bridge && node -e \'... decodeFrame(obs frame + 1 extra varint) ...\'\n  baseline:            {"type":"obs","ver":2,"rxid":"00000005"}\n  with appended field: THREW "obs frame did not consume exactly: 8 of 9 B"\nSo append is transparent ONLY while the new field\'s presence bit is clear. Once `flags` is actually sent, every decoder that has not reloaded the schema drops the whole obs frame.\nBitmap headroom (schema/frames.json, counted): obs n=18, 3 B bitmap, 6 appends before the width moves; config n=14, 2 B, 2 appends. So `flags` does not cross a bitmap boundary — the hazard is the presence bit, not ceil(n/8).\n\nThis belongs to bridge to confirm/answer — raise on device--bridge, do not work around.'}
2026-08-20 10:51:51,116 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG an appended field makes the bridge throw the whole frame away, so it goes blind to everything the unit declares', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-20: "appended elements should not mean the whole packet is rejected and only that new elements at the end were not decoded. THAT IS IMPORTANT" and "it simply means that extra elements are not decoded."\n\nRegister entry: appended-fields-reject-the-whole-frame-instead-of-the-tail\nSpec: docs/spec/appended-fields-are-not-decoded-not-refused.md\n\nThe throw is src/frames.js:159. It does NOT crash — decode() catches it at :227-229 and returns\njson: null, so shout-on-heard survives (devstate.heard runs on arrival, src/bridge.js:1442) but the\nwhole obs block at :1465 is skipped: rxid, ans, beat, win and 14 more are lost, SILENTLY.\n\nNot a one-line delete: trailing bytes are also what a wrong bitmap width looks like, and the width\nis ceil(n/8) from the loaded schema and is not on the wire (:118-120). The fix counts set bits\nBEYOND our field count in the bitmap — bits obs already sends and we never read — skips that many\nvarints, and keeps exact consumption after.\n\nBlocks nothing, but device is landing `flags` on obs (bridge--device #26/#27) and this is what makes\nthat append cheap rather than a coordinated flag day.'}
