2026-08-20 11:35:02,452 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG a frame is decoded, classified and stored by its portnum alone, so 68 percent of frames log a decode error and no alarm in the ledger is an alarm', 'description': "Register entry: a-frame-is-decoded-classified-and-stored-by-its-portnum-alone\nSpec: docs/spec/route-a-frame-by-what-it-is.md\n\nMERGE of three entries, agreed with Peter 2026-08-20. The three originals are withdrawn, not\nretracted — every measurement carried into the merged criterion.\n\nsrc/bridge.js:1363 calls decode(dec.payload) BEFORE classify(dec) on the next line, ungated,\nthough the portnum is read on the line above and classify() already knows which ports are ours.\n\n(a) 16,398 decodeError rows / 77,131 records, ~68% every day the store holds, all Meshtastic\n    protobufs read as our type byte. Never started: the store's first row already errors.\n    Git dates it to the codec, e0f1898 2026-08-10. No commit has ever gated it.\n(b) 7,310 obs rows filed under kind='alarm', and ZERO rows carry a real alarm shape.\n(c) 0 chunk rows ever written; 'chunk' absent from LEDGER_KINDS (src/db.js:91).\n\nBlocks bridge-backlog step 4 — a decode-failure alert cannot be built on a 68% false-positive\nfloor, which is what let the 08-18 outage run eight hours.\n\nTWO THINGS THAT ARE PETER'S, flagged in the spec not decided: chunk retention (db.js:292 forces\n'keep' for any LEDGER_KINDS member, and chunk payloads are image data), and whether the 7,310\nmis-filed alarm rows are migrated (spec says no, and records the cutover instead)."}
