2026-08-20 12:23:54,707 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG the published lifecycle machine is missing a state the bridge actually returns, and the test that should catch it compares two hand-written lists', 'description': "Register entry: a-reachable-state-is-missing-from-the-published-machine\nSpec: docs/spec/the-command-lifecycle-is-a-state-machine.md\n\nFOUND BY html (bridge--mt-alarm-html #40), not by us — they measured the route against what we\ntold them and we had told them wrong.\n\nstateOf() returns 'delivered-unanswered' (src/bridge.js:828). GET /commands/lifecycle publishes 8\nstates and ZERO transitions reaching it — verified live 2026-08-20 on the running service. A\nconsumer switching exhaustively on the route falls through on a state the bridge genuinely\nproduces.\n\nThe guard test cannot see it: test/lifecycle-publishes-its-machine.test.js:37 holds\nSTATES = [8 names] as a HAND-WRITTEN constant and compares the declaration against it. Two\nhand-maintained lists checked against each other — the exact drift its own comment says it\nreplaces. 418 tests green with the defect live.\n\nSo the criterion demands the expected set be DERIVED FROM SOURCE, not typed. A fix that leaves a\nhand-written list is the same test again.\n\nAlso unlocks src/bridge.js, which two other untried entries currently hold."}
