2026-08-20 13:46:17,515 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG /schema asserts two things that are no longer true, and withholds the verb argument table html needs', 'description': 'Register entry: x-unknown-asserts-two-things-that-are-no-longer-true\nSpec: docs/spec/x-unknown-must-be-true.md\nRaised by device, device--bridge #28, answered as #29.\n\nsrc/surface.js:825-830 publishes x-unknown saying (1) "verb arguments: names, units and ranges are\nnot extracted" and (2) "verb reply shapes: not extracted". Both false, measured against our OWN\nlive /schema: 41 reply types with 204 fields are published as x-deviceReplies, and device landed a\nverbargs: block (35 entries) in the device-api.yaml we ALREADY read at surface.js:125.\n\nx-unknown\'s own header: "A DOCUMENT THAT LOOKS COMPLETE AND IS NOT IS WORSE THAN ONE THAT SAYS\nSO." The key that exists to prevent stale completeness has gone stale — the sharpest possible\nversion of the defect it guards.\n\nDevice asked for x-deviceVerbArgs as its own key, not folded into x-deviceVerbs, on the reasoning\nWE gave THEM for x-deviceReplies. They deliberately did not nest it, having read our parser at\nsurface.js:39, because /^verbs:/ would hand us "- kind: set" as a verb name.\n\nDERIVED, not typed: 9 of 35 verbs take an argument and declare neither a setting (which joins to\nx-deviceConfig for ty/def/min/max) nor subs — echo, ltc, nodes, sch, simenv, simpir, site,\nsleepfor, txp. That is what genuinely remains unextracted and what x-unknown should say instead.\n\nhtml cannot use any of it until we publish; they read /schema, not device\'s repo.'}
