2026-08-20 15:08:45,853 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG round-trip judges delivery on evidence that cannot answer, so it reports a delivered command as unproven and a received frame as a failed transit', 'description': 'Registers: hop-4-reports-delivery-unproven-while-the-receipt-sits-in-the-reply-it-prints\n           hop-3-fails-a-frame-the-target-received-at-minus-54dbm-because-our-other-radio-only-relayed-it\nSpec: docs/spec/round-trip-judges-on-evidence-that-can-answer.md\n\nONE SEAM, TWO HOPS. Both judge delivery on a source structurally incapable of answering.\n\nHOP 4 consults ONLY the obs announce. That announce OPENS the wake, so it necessarily predates\nour transmission and can never name the packet we are about to send. Under --remote there is no\nconsole either, so hop 4 is UNPASSABLE on a deployed unit — it printed "----" on runs that were\ndemonstrably delivered, three times today.\n\nHOP 3 fails a frame when our SECOND radio heard it only relayed. That is a fact about YAGI\'s\nreception, not about whether the frame entered the mesh. Measured on !987ab80f id=0xc9950ca2:\nhop 3 FAIL "only RELAYED sightings, rssi -100" while the device\'s own console logged\n"RX: from=0x2687afb1 id=0xc9950ca2 rssi=-54" and obs.ans proved it EXECUTED the command.\nround-trip then declares LOGIC ERROR and says its own report cannot be trusted.\n\nTHE FIX IS NOW CHEAP because da55161 put the receipts on GET /state. Hop 4 can ask the bridge\nwhat the unit said instead of inspecting one frame type at the wrong moment.\n\nPROVEN CASE IT MUST NOW GET RIGHT — !8cee336b, 13:38 today, no debug cable:\n  we sent 0xd804fe5a; its next announce carried rxid=d804fe5a, ans=d804fe5a, txid=bffe98a7.\n  round-trip said "the device never answered". The unit\'s own words say otherwise.'}
2026-08-20 15:09:58,947 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'docs/spec/round-trip-judges-on-evidence-that-can-answer.md', 'kind': 'plan', 'label': 'Spec: round-trip hops 3 and 4 judge on evidence that cannot answer them'}
