2026-08-20 15:14:10,209 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG contact.dueAt keeps a pre-reboot anchor, so a power cycle reads as overdue and aim.nextWakeAt compounds it', 'description': 'Register: contact-dueat-keeps-a-pre-reboot-anchor-so-a-power-cycle-reads-as-overdue\nSpec: docs/spec/dueat-follows-a-boot.md\nRAISED BY HTML, bridge--mt-alarm-html #41, with measurements. Answered as #44.\n\nPeter power-cycled !18a01fc4 and said "it should have caught the bootup". The bridge heard the\nboot frame and ignored what it declared.\n\nAt 2026-08-20T10:09:26.088Z comms carried boot=1 upSince=1 lastRx=00000000 nextWakeMs=895471,\nso the unit\'s own next wake was 10:24:21.6Z. aim.declaredWakeAt matched that to 0.1s.\ncontact.dueAt read 10:17:21.066Z — an anchor from BEFORE the reboot — went overdue at 10:17:21,\nand aim.nextWakeAt then rolled a beat forward FROM THE STALE VALUE to 10:32:21, compounding it\nto eight minutes past what the unit declared, with the reason "that many wakes have gone by\nunheard" when none had.\n\ndeclare() at src/devstate.js:433 DOES re-anchor s.wakeAt on nextWakeAt and its comment says it\nmust be allowed to move BACKWARDS precisely because a reboot restarts the schedule. contact.dueAt\nis computed separately as `first` (src/devstate.js:715) — the first wake owed after the last frame\nheard — and never consults the declaration.\n\nhtml guessed "a fifth place, or one the consolidation missed". It is the second: consolidation\nunified how the grid is PROJECTED and left how dueAt is ANCHORED where it was.\n\nTwo of our own fields disagreed by 8 minutes and html rendered both faithfully.'}
