2026-08-20 15:40:05,616 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG the aim record claims a bearing before the rotator has reached it, and records what we asked for rather than what it achieved', 'description': 'Register: the-aim-is-fire-and-forget-against-a-rotator-that-reports-arrival\nSpec: docs/spec/the-aim-records-what-the-rotator-achieved.md\nPeter, 2026-08-20: "the rotator is not dumb it will tell you", and authorised the fix:\n"that is outside your scope but I give you auth to fix it if it is not behaving".\n\nMEASURED DIRECTLY against ws://192.168.10.186:81 with his permission:\n  commanded seek2az 160 from az=122\n  {"evt":"started","cmd":"seek2az","target":160}     immediately\n  {"evt":"done","cmd":"seek2az","az":158,"ok":true}  after 3.00s\n  settled 158 vs target 160 — inside his stated +/-5 degrees\n  36 degrees in 3.00s = 12 deg/s\n\nSo the rotator reports started, done, the ACHIEVED az, and an ok flag. plugins/pointer/index.js\nrecords `done` into lastOutcome at :101 under a comment quoting Peter — "it tells you when it has\nreached target" — and aimFor() then publishes ctx.publish(\'aim\', {az: target.az}) IMMEDIATELY\nafter send(), never waiting, and records the REQUESTED bearing.\n\nSCOPE HELD DELIBERATELY NARROW. Two further defects are registered and NOT fixed here because\nthey change shared-hardware behaviour and are Peter\'s call:\n  - the hold is sent during the slew, wasting ~3s of a 16000ms window, but it keeps the antenna\n    locked while moving. Moving it after arrival gains the window and opens a 3s gap where the\n    radar could take the dish.\n  - the hold is too short: derived need is p90 aim->announce lag 13153ms + max rtt 10711ms\n    = 24064ms against 16000ms configured.\nBoth are in the register entry with the derivation.'}
