2026-08-20 15:58:36,056 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'DECIDE the rotator hold is a plucked 16000ms, and Peter has ruled the alarm outranks the radar so it must be derived', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-20: "derive a value and add 20% for example. it is not critical, actually this takes a higher priority anyway the other use is mostly ad hoc and is NOT time / wall clock critical."\n\nThat is the ruling on the fork registered in `the-aim-is-fire-and-forget-against-a-rotator-that-reports-arrival`. The hold\'s cost was that it locks a SHARED dish away from mt-radar; he has priced that at zero. So the number stops being a trade and becomes an arithmetic problem.\n\nAlso: "don\'t hold for 1 minute, be reasonable" — 60000ms is the stated absurd ceiling and the derived value must be well under it.'}
