2026-08-21 10:29:54,188 2209008 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'TIDY — docs/HANDOVER.md must state what is true now, and every figure in it must carry the\ncommand that re-derives it.\n\nWHY THIS TASK EXISTS. The handover is the only document a new session is told to read first,\nand it is written at the moment of failure by a session whose context is tainted. A false\nnumber in it is not a documentation defect — it is a premise the next session builds on. This\nproject has lost a day to exactly that twice: once to the beat flooding, once to a port map\nthat named the rare path.\n\nWHAT "DONE" MEANS HERE. Not "the handover was rewritten". Every claim re-derived against the\nrepo and the live services rather than against its own marks, and each surviving figure\ncarrying the one command that settles it. A claim with no command attached is unusable and is\neither given one or deleted.\n\nMEASURED, 2026-08-21T09:21Z, by the reading session — the rewrite of ed3eba1 still carried six\nfalse claims two minutes after it was committed, and NO CHECK CAUGHT ANY OF THEM:\n\n  WRONG   garage silence "TWENTY-FIVE HOURS"     -> 17.2 h. The re-audit inflated its own 16 h\n  NEW     !8cee336b inFlight=0                   -> inFlight=1, queued=1; rssi -114 not -125\n  BROKEN  "spec attached"                        -> mcpp had it flagged, stray device/ prefix\n  WRONG   "A LISTENER IS RUNNING"                -> it was not; died with the session\n  WRONG   bridge 34 of 46, 12 behind             -> 34 of 47, 13 behind, and still 34\n  WRONG   checks "eight pass, two fail"          -> six pass, three fail, all on rak/v2/\n  MISSING rx.win 8s->12s, +17 points             -> in no priority group at all\n\nCORRECTED AND COMMITTED as b1711b2, in place at each section, with the re-deriving command\nbeside each figure and a CORRECTIONS table at the head of the document.\n\nTHE CLASS OF ERROR, which is the part worth keeping: five of the six were STALE-BY-MINUTES\nlive readings written from a note rather than re-queried, and the sixth was arithmetic on a\ntimestamp that nobody re-did. Both are cheap to catch and neither is caught by any test in\nthis repo.'}
