2026-08-21 10:30:11,873 2209008 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'HOW. Two steps, and the order matters: audit first, because the audit is what decides what the\nrewrite says. Writing first and checking after is how ed3eba1 shipped six false claims.\n\nSTEP 1 — VERIFY every claim, against the thing itself and never against its own marks.\n  live       curl -s localhost:8790/state          every unit: beat, win, rssi, heardAt,\n                                                   lastReplyAt, inFlight, queued\n  arithmetic recompute every stated DURATION from its two timestamps. Two handovers running\n             have now carried a wrong one (16 h -> inflated to 25 h; true 17.2 h)\n  code       open every file:line cited. h:271, cpp:557, MtWake.cpp:132/:138 were exact; the\n             spec\'s :133 is one line out\n  checks     run all ten BARE, never through a pipe -- $? after a pipe is tail\'s\n  peers      cat ~/.xsession/<ch>/seen/<party> against `ls msg/ | wc -l`, for EVERY party, not\n             just ours. A peer\'s cursor is the difference between "disagreed" and "never read"\n  process    ps aux for anything the handover claims is running. The listener was not\n  mcpp       plan_file_list -- an attachment can be flagged broken and still read as "attached"\n  register   derive the verdicts from trial.exit/failures; never trust a typed count\n\nSTEP 2 — TIDY correct in place, and leave the correction visible.\n  - amend at the section that carries the claim, not only in a header note, or the next reader\n    finds the false line and never reaches the correction\n  - strike the wrong figure rather than silently replacing it, so a reader who remembers the\n    old number knows it moved and why\n  - EVERY surviving figure gets the command that re-derives it, inline. A number with no query\n    cannot be challenged and gets quoted onward as settled -- this project has done that\n  - put a CORRECTIONS table at the head: what it said, what is true, which section\n  - archive the previous copy to docs/handover/ before overwriting\n\nDONE WHEN. Every figure in the document has a command beside it, and every claim that could be\nre-derived was, with the ones that moved struck rather than replaced.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE. Deciding anything the corrections reveal. The garage\'s inFlight=1 and bridge\'s\nunread cursor are findings this task RECORDS; acting on them belongs to the tasks that own\nthem.'}
