2026-08-21 11:55:57,933 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG a send with no packet id is recorded and counted as a transmission, and round-trip then contradicts itself about it', 'description': 'Two registered defects that are one story, fixed together because the second is a consequence of the first.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-20: 1 of 140 sends returned no packet id from mesh-gw. The bridge wrote it to the ledger as a completed send (`sends: 1`), spent the unit\'s wake on it, and gave up. And round-trip printed `hop 2 PASS "the BRIDGE sent id=undefined"` immediately above `hop 3 FAIL "the bridge never sent"` — two derivations of one truth, disagreeing, because one keys on the send record existing and the other on there being an id to correlate.\n\nA command with no packet id can never be correlated to a reply, so every downstream verdict about it is decided by construction rather than by evidence.\n\nPeter is AFK; both are self-contained, touch nothing device\'s live /xlead test depends on, and neither transmits.'}
