2026-08-21 12:03:09,029 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG the aim ceiling hardcodes a slew rate that config declares wrongly and nothing reads', 'description': 'Peter\'s rule, 2026-08-20: "Every key in your config is read, or it is not in the file."\n\nMEASURED: `/var/lib/mt-bridge/plugins.d/pointer.json` declares `slew_deg_per_s: 360`, and `grep -c slew_deg_per_s plugins/pointer/index.js` is **0**. Meanwhile `doneCeilingMs` hardcodes 12 — the rate measured directly against the rotator on 2026-08-20 (36° in 3.00 s).\n\nSo the number that is RIGHT cannot be changed without an edit, and the number that CAN be changed is wrong by 30x and inert.\n\nTHE ORDER IS THE TRAP: simply making the code read the config would take a 22° move\'s ceiling from 3250 ms to 592 ms, and every aim would report `arrived: false`. The fix must not trust the configured value blindly.\n\nSame file also has `beamwidth_deg: null` unread while `on_target_deg: 6` is read, so the file cannot be used to tell which keys are live.'}
