2026-08-21 12:11:59,727 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'GAP eight obs fields are decoded every beat and reach no consumer, including the trigger count and both health figures', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-20, setting the bridge\'s role: "collection and usage of the data it sends us, and predicting the health of the unit, as well as managing the yet to be implemented alarm triggers and actions." And twice before that, on the receipts: "you keep just discarding it."\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-21: of nine device-reported obs fields, only `boot` appears anywhere in `GET /state/{unit}`. trig, stak, heap, cam, env, upst, rxg, p8b5 are decoded, stored raw in the ledger, and reach no consumer without a hand-written sqlite query.\n\nDEVICE HAS NOW SUPPLIED THE SEMANTICS (device--bridge #41 and the shared schema), which is what was blocking this:\n  stak  Stack used (%)      — rising is bad\n  heap  Heap used (%)       — so heap:5 is 5% used, healthy, not the broken constant I reported\n  trig  PIR edges since last beat\n  cam   Camera alive        env  Environment sensor present    upst  Upload state\n  rxg   RX gain register 0x08AC (0x96 = boosted)               p8b5  RX sensitivity register 0x08B5\n\nSCOPE IS DELIBERATELY NARROW: surface them with their schema labels. NOT a health predictor and NOT alarm actions — Peter has said that design is his.'}
