2026-08-21 12:37:16,089 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'GAP a command reads sent for a whole beat after its fate stopped being decidable, and the machine has no name for the second phase', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-20: "the lifecycle send expiry is broken. since a mt message has a life of about 30 seconds, if it is not heard on the next wake it never will be."\n\nMEASURED from every give-up in the store, as the gap between send and give-up: 21.7, 28.9, 29.8, 29.8, 38.4, 38.9, 59.9 s at a 30 s beat; 299.9 s at 5 min; 891.7, 899.9, 899.9, 900.4 s at 15 min. Give-up fires ONE BEAT after the send, whatever the beat.\n\nThat beat-long wait is CORRECT and is not being changed - it is what catches obs.rxid and obs.ans on the next announce, which is the only way delivered-unanswered and executed-reply-lost are determined.\n\nWhat is wrong is that the outcome stops being decidable far sooner. We transmit into a declared window (win, 5000-8000 ms), a unit that heard it replies in 5-7 s (measured rtt 5232/5675/6944), and retransmissions after the window shuts reach a sleeping device. At a 900 s beat the command reads \'sent\' for ~860 s after nothing can change it.\n\nFIX: a non-terminal state `awaiting-receipt` between sent and every terminal, entered at sentAt + win + meshMessageLifeMs. win is the UNIT\'S OWN declaration read per unit, never a constant. meshMessageLifeMs defaults to Peter\'s 30 s and is an option, not a literal. Corroborated: two give-ups landed at 38.4/38.9 s = win 8000 + 30 s.\n\nNOT a retry, NOT giving up earlier, no timing moves. A unit with no declared win stays in \'sent\' rather than guessing.\n\nSpec: docs/spec/a-command-says-which-phase-it-is-in.md\nRegister: a-command-reads-sent-for-a-whole-beat-after-its-fate-was-already-decided'}
