2026-08-21 14:08:07,785 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'park-traceroute-plugin-and-yagi-pointing', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-21, verbatim:\n\n"next plugin will be traceroute. remember we have 2 antennas, so yagi needs pointing and we need 2 methods of point, 1) direct, 2) using last known traceroute\'s first hop."\n\nContext standing at the time of parking (NOT instructions — just what was true, so the next session does not re-derive it):\n\n- The traceroute stream is already retained: port 70, retain 500, max_age 30 days, and /streams now reports AGE as the binding policy at ~7/day.\n- Payloads decode. Two captured today from TA2m at the garage:\n    12:33:53  route []                snr_towards [-68]      -> -17.0 dB   DIRECT\n    12:36:58  route [47500548]        snr_towards [-13,-11]  -> -3.25/-2.75 dB\n  snr_towards is QUARTER-dB and both values matched the OMNI/YAGI receive SNR exactly.\n- First hop 47500548 = !02d4cd04 "Preston~Bowyer" (T4, RAK4631), 5.32 km at bearing 274.17 from the YAGI. That is a live worked example of method 2.\n- Bearings already exist: GET /plugins/nodes/{node}/bearing?frm={radio}, and they now carry position_uncertainty_m and bearing_uncertainty_deg.\n- THE TRAP FOR METHOD 1: most nodes broadcast a MASKED position. 36 of 81 mask 15 bits (365 m), 25 mask 18 bits (2918 m). At 3 km a 2.9 km uncertainty is +/-44 degrees, so a direct bearing can be useless at short range while looking authoritative. Method 2 may be the BETTER pointing source when the first hop has a good position, and that is worth measuring rather than assuming.\n- Rotator is at ws://192.168.10.186:81, yagiOffset 119.0.\n- Blocked/related register entries: aim-should-accept-a-node-id-or-a-bearing (plugins cannot reach each other), and the-message-board-shows-no-distance-or-node-detail.\n- plugins/traceroute/__init__.py already exists as an inert placeholder.'}
