2026-08-21 15:00:37,333 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "BUG a radio failure settles a command 15 minutes before the device's own receipt would have settled it better", 'description': 'We broadcast (address by @token to 0xFFFFFFFF) with want_ack:true. src/bridge.js:1666 treats mesh-gw\'s status=failed as terminal: stamps outcome=\'radio-failed\', settledAt, and dequeues, ~30 s after the send.\n\nMEASURED 2026-08-21 on !987ab80f: packet 365794378 sent 11:49:47Z, failed MAX_RETRANSMIT 11:50:17Z, terminated at 30 s. Packet 569296247 sent 12:19:48Z, failed 12:20:25Z, terminated at 37 s. Both MAX_RETRANSMIT rows in the entire ledger are from today.\n\nTHE REGISTERED ENTRY OVERSTATES THE CASE and the spec corrects it. MAX_RETRANSMIT is not information-free: on a broadcast the ack is IMPLICIT (a neighbour rebroadcasting), so it means "nobody relayed our frame". In both observed cases it did coincide with real non-delivery - obs.rxid stayed 00000000.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: it does not prove the TARGET failed to hear the frame directly, and settling on it forfeits obs.rxid/obs.ans on the next announce - strictly better evidence, one beat away. Every command in the ledger that reached give-up took 512-1792 s; these took 30 and 37.\n\nFIX, and it keeps radio-failed reachable rather than deleting a declared state: record the failure on the entry but do not settle or dequeue. At the next announce the receipt decides as it does for any command; if no receipt names it, the give-up path settles it as radio-failed instead of gave-up, so the outcome still says WHY.\n\nMUST LAND BEFORE THE STOREWARD CUT-OVER: storeward sends with retry off and gets no_ack_needed, so the symptom vanishes when the cause does and the bug would close by accident.\n\nRegister: max-retransmit-on-a-broadcast-ends-a-command-that-may-have-been-delivered'}
2026-08-21 15:01:13,027 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'bridge/docs/spec/a-radio-failure-is-not-the-last-word-on-a-command.md', 'kind': 'plan', 'label': 'spec: a radio failure is not the last word on a command'}
2026-08-21 15:01:47,689 1748124 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'bugs', 'kind': 'note', 'text': 'CONFIRMED — config-json-commands-table-is-now-a-second-copy\n\npublic/config.json carries a hand-maintained `commands` table (23 verbs classified set/query/act, with `sets` naming a settings id). Its own comment: "Raised with device as [verb-argument-table]; this stands until they declare it, and comes out the day they do."\n\nThat day has arrived. Measured 2026-08-21 against the live bridge, schemaHash 0x6911:\n\n  curl -s localhost:8790/schema | jq \'."x-deviceVerbArgs".verbs | length\'   -> 35\n\n`x-deviceVerbArgs` publishes kind (set|sub|plain), arg (required|optional|forbidden), the config `setting` ids a `set` writes, and the enumerated `subs` a `sub` accepts. Its description: "Generated from the dispatcher and gated by the firmware build."\n\nEFFECT: the page classifies 23 verbs from a local table while the bridge declares 35 from the firmware build. Twelve verbs the page cannot classify, and any reclassification in firmware is invisible here. Exactly the drift the comment predicted.\n\nFIX: delete the config.json `commands` table and read x-deviceVerbArgs. `aliases` and `scales` stay — they are display-only and the bridge has no reason to carry them.\n\nNOT YET KNOWN: whether kindOf()/boundsFor() map cleanly onto set|sub|plain, and what the form does with `subs` (an enumerated select, which it does not have today).\n\n---\n\nCONFIRMED — two published command states have no display word\n\nGET /commands/lifecycle now publishes 10 states and 18 transitions (measured 2026-08-21). The page was written against 8.\n\n  awaiting-receipt      not terminal — "the unit\'s listening window has closed and the radio\'s retry budget is spent... NOT finished"\n  delivered-unanswered  terminal — "the unit CONFIRMED receiving it - its own obs.rxid named our packet - and then did not answer... the strongest delivery evidence that exists without a cable"\n\nEFFECT: both render unworded. delivered-unanswered is the strongest positive delivery evidence the system produces and the page cannot say so.\n\nBoth recorded in the handover pack at mt-radar/mesh-gw/docs/mt-alarm/ as things the new plugin must get right rather than inherit.'}
