2026-08-21 15:17:30,006 2028104 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG rxid absence is treated as evidence of non-receipt, and it cost a false report to a peer today', 'description': 'obs.rxid names the LAST PACKET FROM ANY SOURCE, not a receipt for our command. Measured 2026-08-21 06:34Z against our own witness ledger: !8cee336b reported rxid values that were frames from !987ab80f; !987ab80f reported frames from !8cee336b and !18a01fc4; !18a01fc4 reported a mesh-gw outbox send. Our units hear each other, and any of it overwrites the receipt before the next obs.\n\nSo: rxid naming our packet is PROOF of receipt. rxid not naming it proves NOTHING. ans is different and IS reliable - the device only answers our commands.\n\nIT COST A FALSE REPORT TODAY. I read twelve beats of rxid=00000000 from !987ab80f and told Peter and device "the device transmits normally and receives nothing", as a firmware receiver fault. Ninety minutes later the same unit received a storeward command and answered it, and its next announce carried rxid=74da9947 ans=74da9947. Not deaf - at the edge, self-reporting rssi -128 snr -19.2.\n\nThe entry already said absence is not evidence and I leaned on it anyway, so the fix makes the DATA say so rather than only the register.\n\nCHANGES: hop4Verdict must not return FAIL from a non-matching rxid (no test guards that branch; step 16 records that no unit has a working debug console, so it is unreachable in practice too). receipts() must say `received` is positive-only when it holds a value that is not ours.\n\nNOT CHANGED: noteReceived and hasReceived are already positive-only.\n\nRegister: rxid-names-the-last-packet-from-anyone-so-its-absence-is-not-evidence\nSpec: docs/spec/rxid-is-positive-only-evidence.md'}
