2026-08-21 15:37:38,738 1822309 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-21, VERBATIM: "MARK is now in the microwave to emulate the remote GARG. /afk"\n\nMY READING (separate from his words, so the next reader can check one against the other):\nMARK (!18a01fc4) has been put in a microwave oven as a Faraday cage, to attenuate it down\nto the signal level of the real GARG (!987ab80f) on its roof/garage site. Baseline at the\nmoment he said it: MARK -50 dBm on YAGI, real GARG -115 dBm on YAGI — so ~65 dB of\nattenuation is what "emulate" would mean.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS TO WHAT IS IN FLIGHT: it gives a marginal-link test subject that is in the\nhouse rather than 3 m up a mast, so today\'s work — storeward firing on a wake, the reply\ninbox correlating a threaded pong, and traceroute\'s first-hop pointing when a path\ndegrades from direct to relayed — can be exercised at the edge instead of only at -30 dBm\nacross the bench. Those are exactly the conditions that produced every defect found today.\n\nNOT ASSUMED: that the microwave gives enough attenuation, or that MARK degrades the same\nway GARG does. Both are to be MEASURED against the real GARG baseline, not asserted.'}
