2026-08-21 17:41:47,968 2337678 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG the give-up sweep only runs when we decide to fire, so a command the unit never gets is unsettleable', 'description': 'THE GATE FOR THE WHOLE STOREWARD MIGRATION. Peter has ruled fireOnHeard goes away ("you no longer need to wait for on heard, that is the whole point of storeward"). The settle/give-up sweep lives INSIDE it — src/bridge.js:2053-2093, function fireOnHeard at :2011 (handover said :1995 and :2062; both had drifted, the containment is unchanged). Delete the function as it stands and nothing ever reaches gave-up, delivered-unanswered or radio-failed.\n\nSpec: docs/spec/call-storeward-instead-of-firing-ourselves.md, section "fireOnHeard GOES AWAY ENTIRELY — AND THE SWEEP MUST NOT GO WITH IT".\n\nTHE RED TO CAPTURE FIRST: queue a command, let the answer budget expire, deliver an announce WITHOUT anything calling fireOnHeard, assert the command never reaches a terminal state. If that test passes today the premise is wrong and the step stops.\n\nTHE CHANGE: extract the sweep to its own function called from BOTH the announce path and fireOnHeard. Behaviour-neutral by design — it only makes fireOnHeard deletable. The receipt wait (obs.rxid / obs.ans, one beat) is OURS and does not move; storeward\'s TTL is a different clock and conflating them deletes our best delivery evidence.\n\nPROOF: red-to-green on the new test, npm test (552 green now), then a live round-trip on !18a01fc4 — direct on both radios, median -53 over 3 h. NOT !987ab80f: -116 direct, and a failure there proves nothing about the code.'}
