2026-08-21 17:55:07,910 2337678 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 58, 'text': 'SHIPPED 3d7b1c3-ish (see git log, commit "the sweep has its own door, and a hung POST no longer strands a command"). npm test 555 pass 0 fail, was 552. Bridge restarted onto it at 16:58Z, restart 40, /commands checked empty in its own call first, device approved ("RESTART: GO, now is fine. Nothing of mine is measuring", device--bridge #68).\n\nTHE STEP AS WRITTEN WAS BUILT ON A FALSE PREMISE AND A PROBE CAUGHT IT. The title said the sweep only runs when we decide to fire, and that an announce alone settles nothing. False: the announce CALLS fireOnHeard (src/bridge.js:1996) and the sweep runs inside it. Register entry the-give-up-sweep-only-runs-when-we-decide-to-fire was WITHDRAWN the same hour, before any code rested on it, and re-filed as two accurate ones:\n\n  a-post-that-never-returns-strands-the-command-forever  GUILTY -> CLOSED, red and green both captured in .proofs/\n  the-sweep-has-no-seam-of-its-own                       not-reproduced -> PETER\'S RULING, ask- file written\n\nWHAT SHIPPED: settleOnContact() is the sweep\'s own entry point. It judges, never transmits, returns the head of the queue when that head is still live. fireOnHeard calls it and then decides separately whether to send, which is what makes fireOnHeard deletable for storeward without taking gave-up, delivered-unanswered and radio-failed with it. THE MIGRATION GATE IS OPEN.\n\nPlus: a POST outstanding longer than the unit\'s own declared beat ends the command as radio-failed, and a late gateway answer records `late-post` instead of reopening a settled command.\n\nTHRESHOLD GOT DERIVED WRONG FIRST AND THE SUITE CAUGHT IT, NOT ME. I counted contacts as a proxy for elapsed time; queue.test.js:91 failed because four contacts arrive within a millisecond on the bench. Now devstate.schedule(unit).beat, the same derivation bestRadioFor uses. A unit with no declared beat makes no claim.\n\nTWO OF MY OWN INSTRUMENT FAULTS, both found by running rather than reading: the test read bridge.commands() AFTER close() and close() discards the queue, so it reported a stranded command as settled; and it demanded a lifecycle row that lifecycle() refuses by design on a null packetId (:671).\n\nSTILL OPEN OFF THE BACK OF THIS: the queue flow chart does not draw the seam. anchors.yaml was tightened so reanchor stays green, but a /flow_derive pass is owed. And a command that never gets a packet id has no replayable ending at all, whatever kills it - the no-id branch (:1522) has the same hole. Not filed, not mine to file inside this step.'}
