2026-08-21 18:52:31,844 2337678 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'GAP the bridge cannot hand a command to storeward, so the migration cannot begin', 'description': 'STEP ONE OF TWO. Peter, 2026-08-21: "we need to push forward with migration. we should not delete our code but disconnect it and keep as a reference."\n\nSTOREWARD IS RE-PROVEN ON THE LIVE FLEET, 17:45:11Z queue -> both units fired on their own wakes:\n  !18a01fc4  held 180 s  fired 17:48:11.7Z  packet_id 2050101549  1 reply\n  !987ab80f  held 275 s  fired 17:49:46.6Z  packet_id 2368837448  1 reply\nBoth within 0.2 s of the wake OUR aim predicted independently (17:48:11.514Z / 17:49:46.606Z).\nProduction-derived TTLs (must x 1.2). !8cee336b powered off: still held, not vanished.\n\nWHAT THIS STEP BUILDS: a per-command transport. send() marks the entry, the storeward route POSTs\nonce to /plugins/storeward/queue and records the entry_id, and fireOnHeard NEVER transmits a\nstoreward entry. Default stays \'own\' - at no point may the bridge be unable to send.\n\nEXCLUSIVITY IS THE POINT, NOT AN EXTRA. "We send to the radio ONCE, full stop" is standing. A\ncommand that goes down both routes is two packets the device would execute twice, so the test\nthat proves a storeward command never reaches a radio POST is the deliverable, not a nicety.\n\nTHE TWO CLOCKS MUST NOT BE CONFLATED. Our give-up budget is ONE heard contact; storeward\'s hold is\nup to must x 1.2 = SIX HOURS on the deployed units. So settleOnContact must not judge a storeward\nentry that has not fired yet, or we would report gave-up on a command storeward is still\nlegitimately holding. The receipt half (obs.rxid / ans) stays ours and does not move.\n\nDECIDED, NOT ASKED - THE HELD ROW NEEDS A KEY. A storeward entry carries packet_id: null until it\nfires; lifecycle() returns early on a null packetId by design (:671), so a held command would be\ninvisible in the replayable record for up to six hours. Key the held row on storeward\'s entry_id\n(exists at queue time, e.g. 18a01fc4-1787334311686-1, stable), switch to packetId once it fires.\nNothing that works today breaks: a consumer grepping by packet id still finds every post-fire row.\nhtml must be told BEFORE it lands.\n\nSTEP TWO, NOT THIS ONE: flip the default and move the own-transport path (per-radio POST,\nbestRadioFor, want_ack, hold-until-heard) intact into a reference module with a header naming the\nlast SHA it ran live under. Disconnected, not deleted.'}
