2026-08-21 19:26:18,508 2360378 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/modules/received_packet_store.md (attached).\nCore builds one complete record per frame off the air and emits it as data.frame on the packet event; plugins/packets retains it; module/server.py\'s route delegates to whichever plugin declares SERVES_PACKET_RETENTION and 503s when none does.\nRed at HEAD: check_packet_store_owner.py exit 1, 3 markers in core. Green: 0 markers, served by [\'packets\'].\nLIVE REGRESSION I CAUSED AND FIXED: a helper named _own_node_num collided with an existing int attribute of that name, so every received frame raised "\'int\' object is not callable" and tore the BLE link down — both radios reconnect-looped ~19:14-19:22 BST. Renamed to _own_number(); 0 occurrences since restart, both READY, rows landing (OMNI 9, YAGI 22 within a minute).\nCarried unchanged and still on the register: durability, the 37-minute window, the echo eviction, row node_id being the sender, and data.packet\'s dropped defaults.'}
