2026-08-21 19:41:54,105 2360378 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'DONE in 4d294f9: aim enabled and configured (core/bridge_config.yaml, gitignored — targets v4/v5, active v4); ctx.spawn(driver.run()) added so the plugin opens the socket itself; status gained `connected`.\nEvidence: red check_aim_connects.py -> green; live connected true, az 172.0, variant v4, matching an independent read-only probe of ws://192.168.10.186:81 taken before enabling. v5 (192.168.10.195) is UNREACHABLE, Errno 113 — configured and not live, as the contributed spec said.\nSTILL BLOCKING BRIDGE: aim has no write route. GET /status and /ledger only; aim-should-accept-a-node-id-or-a-bearing is untried. Until that lands bridge keeps its own pointing — told them so in #102.\nAlso owed to bridge: the arbitration contract — what a caller sees when pre-empted mid-slew, and "hold briefly, release, yield rather than queue" in numbers. bridge has run this hardware and we have not; their yield behaviour is the input we asked for.'}
2026-08-21 19:42:17,838 2337678 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'MEASURE what mesh-gw offers now, and what of ours it replaces', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-21: "i think a better approach is to see what mesh-gw offers now and what we can use / replace from our code."\n\nAhead of migration step two, so the disconnect list is derived from their published surface rather than from what I happen to remember. 74 paths, 6 loaded plugins, each with a self-describing index route.\n\nTHE ARGUMENT FOR WRITING IT DOWN: I made TWO false-absence claims today from not knowing their surface - "no service publishes a node\'s role" (it is GET /{node_id}/config) and "the aim plugin is not loaded" (it answers 200; their /plugins listing is what lies). Both were reported to peers before being checked. A written map is the fix for that class.\n\nDeliverable: docs/surveys/what-mesh-gw-offers-and-what-it-replaces.md - capability, their invocation, our code, verdict (USE / REPLACE / KEEP OURS), with the command that produced each row.'}
