2026-08-22 10:34:49,648 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_project_set args={'name': 'test', 'description': 'Test harness repo. Holds no product code of its own — it exists only to test the other repos under `/usr/share/pac/dev`.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-22: *"this repo / project only exists to test other repos under the /usr/share/pac/dev folder"*.\n\nConsequences that follow from that and are easy to get wrong:\n\n- **A finding here belongs to the repo under test, not to this one.** Report it to that repo\'s session over `xsession` and let them fix it. Never edit a peer repo\'s files and never build a workaround for their bug — a workaround makes the defect permanent and invisible.\n- Test harnesses live in the session scratchpad while they are being written; anything worth keeping gets a task here with the harness path recorded on it, because a scratchpad does not survive the session.\n- Tasks in this project are named for the repo under test, so `plan_task_list` reads as a list of what has been tested and what has not.\n\nCurrently under test: `mt-radar/rotator/v4` (party `v4` on xsession channel `test--v4`), WS API at `ws://192.168.10.186:81`, contract published at `http://192.168.10.186/schema`.'}
2026-08-22 10:34:55,546 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'v4-ws-passive-conformance', 'title': 'VERIFY rotator v4 WS API against its published schema — passive conformance', 'steps': ['VERIFY device sends a full status frame on connect', 'VERIFY status field coverage in both directions against schema.status.fields', 'VERIFY declared types, const and enum are honoured', 'MEASURE the status tick against schema.status.interval_ms', 'VERIFY subscription ops sub, unsub and set are acked with a subs mask', 'VERIFY the documented subscription traps are real', 'VERIFY error paths report themselves rather than failing silently', 'VERIFY read-only diagnostic verbs respond', 'VERIFY hold token is private to the requesting client', 'VERIFY HTTP route set matches what the schema declares']}
2026-08-22 10:35:05,513 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Establish whether `mt-radar/rotator/v4` behaves as the contract it publishes at `http://192.168.10.186/schema` says it does — without moving the antenna.\n\nThe device is unusual in publishing its own machine-readable contract (AsyncAPI, generated from `SCHEMA_JSON` in `include/httpserver.h`), so the test is not "does it work" but "is the published document true". A contract that is wrong is worse than no contract, because a client author trusts it and cannot see the device.\n\nScope is deliberately everything that does NOT swing the beam. It is a masted yagi in service.'}
2026-08-22 10:35:11,490 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Black-box only. Fetch the live `/schema`, drive `ws://192.168.10.186:81` from a Python harness, assert against the schema rather than against expectations.\n\n**Harness** (session scratchpad — copy somewhere durable if this needs to outlive the session):\n- `wslib.py` — one connection, timestamped frame log, `wait_for(pred)` so tests wait on the completion event, never on a clock\n- `t1_passive.py` — this task\n- `t2_semantics.py`, `t3_probe.py` — sibling tasks\n\n**Rules the harness follows:**\n1. Never assert a duration; wait for the frame that proves the thing happened.\n2. Exercise setters against the value the device ALREADY holds, so device state is unchanged.\n3. Any motion command targets the CURRENT bearing, so a failed guard cannot swing the beam.\n4. Snapshot and restore anything that does get written.\n5. Finish by asserting the device is as it was found.\n\nFindings go to the `v4` session over xsession channel `test--v4`. This repo never fixes them.'}
2026-08-22 10:35:21,173 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 4, 'text': '**MEASURED: median 250 ms**, min 243, max 257, over 11 consecutive gaps (12 status frames in 3.0 s).\n\nMatches `schema.status.interval_ms: 250`. But it does NOT match the prose in the same document — `events.status.description` says *"broadcast every 25 ms"*. The contract contradicts itself and the measurement settles which half is wrong: the prose, by 10×.\n\nRaised with `v4` as `schema-tick-25-vs-250`. Source is `include/httpserver.h:79`; `:24` and `:41` carry the correct 250 from today\'s 25→250 change, `:79` was missed. It has propagated into `docs/api/asyncapi.json` (2 occurrences).\n\nWhy nothing caught it: `api_audit.py` reads `schema.status.interval_ms` — the field that is right. The prose that is wrong is checked by nothing.'}
2026-08-22 10:35:23,821 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 10, 'text': "**MISMATCH.** Schema and `docs/specs/api-contract-published.md` both state the device serves only `GET /`, `GET /index.html`, `GET /schema`.\n\nLive:\n- `/`, `/index.html`, `/schema` → 200 ✓\n- `/nope` → **200**, 8381 bytes, byte-identical to `/index.html`\n\nEvery path is answered with the dashboard, so a client cannot use a 404 to discover whether a route exists.\n\nRaised with `v4` as `http-catch-all-200`, phrased as DISCUSS not BUG — it may be an intentional SPA fallback, in which case the schema should say so. Not this repo's call."}
2026-08-22 10:36:08,873 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_project_set args={'description': 'Test harness repo. Holds no product code of its own — it exists only to test the other repos under `/usr/share/pac/dev`.\n\n## The goal\n\nPeter, 2026-08-22: *"each session will effectively be 1 repo test, iteratively with the session who owns it, with the goal of identifying bugs and getting the repo owner to fix it."*\n\nSo the shape of the work is fixed:\n\n- **One session tests one repo.** Not a sweep across many. Pick the repo, go deep.\n- **The loop is iterative and two-sided.** Test → report to the owning session over `xsession` → they fix and flash → re-test against the new build → repeat. A session that reports once and stops has done half the job.\n- **The deliverable is a FIXED bug, not a filed one.** Success is the owner shipping the fix. Reports are therefore written to be actionable *by them*: measured frames rather than adjectives, and what was NOT tested stated explicitly so a pass count is never misread as coverage.\n- **This repo never fixes anything.** The defect belongs to the repo under test. No edits to their files, and never a workaround — a workaround makes the defect permanent and invisible.\n\n## Practical rules, learned the hard way\n\n- Seat the `xsession` channel yourself. A peer that has never been written to has no cursor and will never see the items; confirm they show as *"Waiting on you"* from the peer\'s side before believing they were delivered.\n- **A peer session\'s claim about physical hardware is not evidence.** On 2026-08-22 the `v4` session supplied a "safe sweep range 90-210 deg" for a masted antenna and retracted it minutes later as invented. Physical facts come from the operator only. Label OBSERVED / DOCUMENTED / UNCONFIRMED separately in every report.\n- Harnesses live in the session scratchpad while being written; anything worth keeping gets a task here with the harness path recorded, because a scratchpad does not survive the session.\n- Tasks are named for the repo under test, so `plan_task_list` reads as a list of what has been tested and what has not.\n\n## Currently under test\n\n`mt-radar/rotator/v4` — party `v4` on xsession channel `test--v4`. WS API at `ws://192.168.10.186:81`, contract published at `http://192.168.10.186/schema`.'}
