2026-08-22 10:37:07,706 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_project_set args={'description': '# test — the harness repo\n\nHolds no product code. It exists only to test the **other** repos under `/usr/share/pac/dev`.\n\nEverything below is standing instruction from Peter. **It does not need to be repeated to a session — read it here.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. The goal\n\n> *"each session will effectively be 1 repo test, iteratively with the session who owns it, with the goal of identifying bugs and getting the repo owner to fix it."* — Peter, 2026-08-22\n\n- **One session tests one repo.** Not a sweep across many. Pick the repo, go deep.\n- **The loop is iterative and two-sided.** Test → report to the owning session over `xsession` → they fix and flash → **re-test against the new build** → repeat. A session that reports once and stops has done half the job.\n- **The deliverable is a FIXED bug, not a filed one.** Success is the owner shipping the fix.\n- **This repo never fixes anything.** The defect belongs to the repo under test. No edits to their files, and never a workaround — a workaround makes the defect permanent and invisible.\n\n## 2. There is an mcpp task for every test\n\n> *"there should be a mcpp task for each test."* — Peter, 2026-08-22\n\nOne task per test suite, one **step per test**, named for the repo under test so `plan_task_list` reads as a list of what has been tested and what has not. Steps carry the evidence: measured values, actual frames, and the xsession slug the finding was raised under. A finding that is not on a step did not happen.\n\nA task stays **open** until the owner\'s fix has been re-tested. Closing it at "reported" would record the wrong outcome — see the goal above.\n\n## 3. Test scripts are reusable, not ad-hoc\n\n> *"you might need to write test scripts that you can reuse rather than creating adhoc temp scripts."* — Peter, 2026-08-22\n\nScratchpad scripts die with the session, and the iterative loop in §1 means every suite gets run **again** against the fixed build. So harnesses live in this repo:\n\n- `rig/` — repo-agnostic machinery (transport, frame log, assertions, reporting)\n- `suites/<repo>/` — the suite for one repo under test\n- `run.py` — the runner\n\nPrototyping in the scratchpad is fine. Anything that found a bug, or that will be re-run, gets promoted into `rig/` + `suites/` before the session ends.\n\n## 4. How findings are written\n\nWritten to be actionable *by the owner*, who cannot see your terminal:\n\n- Measured frames and numbers, never adjectives.\n- **State what was NOT tested**, explicitly, so a pass count is never misread as coverage.\n- Label **OBSERVED** / **DOCUMENTED** / **UNCONFIRMED** separately. "Nothing broke" is not "nothing can break".\n- Lead with the defect.\n\n## 5. Hard-won rules\n\n- **Seat the `xsession` channel yourself.** A peer that has never been written to has no cursor and will never see the items. Confirm they show as *"Waiting on you"* from the peer\'s side before believing they were delivered.\n- **A peer session\'s claim about physical hardware is not evidence.** On 2026-08-22 the `v4` session supplied a "safe sweep range is 90-210 deg true" for a masted antenna in service, then retracted it: *"I MADE THAT UP."* Physical facts come from the **operator** only. Before any irreversible or physical action, ask where the number came from — repo, measurement, or Peter. A peer\'s say-so leaves the action unauthorised.\n- **Test without moving anything first.** Exercise setters against the value the device already holds; point any motion command at the position it is already in; snapshot and restore whatever does get written; finish by asserting the device is as it was found.\n- **Wait on the completion event, never on a clock.**\n\n## 6. Currently under test\n\n`mt-radar/rotator/v4` — party `v4`, xsession channel `test--v4`. WS API `ws://192.168.10.186:81`, contract published at `http://192.168.10.186/schema` (AsyncAPI, not OpenAPI).\n\nOpen with `v4`: `hold-acks-nothing` (confirmed theirs, fix in `armHold`), `schema-tick-25-vs-250`, `http-catch-all-200`.\n**Beam motion is UNAUTHORISED** — the safe arc is unknown and only Peter can supply it.'}
