2026-08-22 10:58:28,200 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 5, 'text': '`rig/safety.py`. Requires `authority/<target>.json` granted by the **operator**, carrying his words verbatim, before any `NEEDS_MOTION` suite runs.\n\nRefuses on: no record; granted by anyone but the operator; no verbatim quote; expired; action not in the record\'s `actions` list. `grant()` takes no `granted_by` parameter at all, so a peer\'s assurance cannot be laundered into an authority record by passing a different name.\n\nWritten because of the incident it names in its own docstring — the `v4` session inventing a safe sweep arc for a live masted antenna and retracting it an hour later. The point is that nothing about the fabricated message was distinguishable from a true one.\n\n**Exercised for real:** it refused `s04` all afternoon, then accepted Peter\'s grant at 2026-08-22 — quote *"you can command any angle you like. no restrictions"* — recorded in `authority/v4.json`.\n\nA refusal prints as `INFO REFUSED`, never as a failed check: the gate working is not a test failing, and scoring it as one would train the next reader to make it go away.'}
2026-08-22 10:58:31,471 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 4, 'text': '`rig/schema.py` — fetch, cache, diff, plus generic conformance helpers (`field_coverage` both directions, `type_violations` honouring const/enum and catching bool-as-integer).\n\nThe cache is **not** for speed. "What changed in the contract since the last run" is itself a finding, and it earned its place the same day: the diff caught v4\'s fix landing without being told about it —\n\n```\n+ commands.hold.args range "1 to 86400000"\n+ events.denied.fields.reason.enum gains "not a valid hold duration"\n~ events.denied.description now covers hold as well as release\n```\n\nThat is how s03 knew what to assert against the new build.'}
