2026-08-22 11:00:49,522 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'v4-motion-closed-loop', 'title': 'VERIFY rotator v4 closed-loop motion — accuracy, slewed, hold-and-return, aimIn', 'steps': ["DECIDE whether the beam may be moved, and record the operator's authority", 'MEASURE move2az landing error across the full circle', "MEASURE the rate of v4's reported intermittent 7 deg miss", 'VERIFY seek2az emits slewed with a signed err, and move2az does not', 'VERIFY no status frames are emitted during a move', 'VERIFY done carries a holdToken and the lock is in force before done arrives', 'VERIFY seek2az hold-then-return: retArmed, retAz, no done on the return leg', 'VERIFY release during a move-armed hold reports willReturn and runs the return', 'VERIFY brake stops a move in progress and leaves nothing armed', 'VERIFY a scheduled aimIn fires on its own and lands on target', 'VERIFY jog2az reaches its target, and home zeroes the encoder without moving', 'BUG move2az emitted started and never done - reproduce and report']}
2026-08-22 11:01:05,641 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Test the half of the rotator API that actually moves the antenna — the closed-loop handshake, the hold-and-return semantics, and the accuracy the whole thing exists to deliver.\n\nThis was deliberately left untested for most of the engagement. It is a masted yagi in service, the safe arc was unknown, and the owning session\'s answer to "what arc is safe" turned out to be invented. Held until the operator himself authorised it:\n\n> *"you can command any angle you like. no restrictions"* — Peter, 2026-08-22\n\nSecondary goal, asked for by `v4`: give their reported intermittent ~7° miss a **rate** rather than another anecdote.'}
2026-08-22 11:01:10,144 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '`suites/v4/s04_motion.py`, run with `python3 run.py v4 s04 --motion`. Gated by `rig.safety` — it refuses without an operator-granted authority record, and refused for the whole of the earlier session.\n\nAccuracy is sampled over 8 bearings spread around the full circle, including a long haul and a short nudge, because the reported miss is not known to be size-independent. Error is measured as signed shortest arc after a settle, so 359 vs 1 is 2° and not 358°.\n\nThe suite parks the beam back where it found it. "No restrictions" is permission to move it, not permission to leave it somewhere it did not start.\n\n**Excluded even under unrestricted authority**, because each is destructive rather than merely mobile and none is needed to test the API: `calMotor` (multi-revolution, rewrites ppd and backlash), `qmcCali` (spins the motor and resets the boresight, raising yagiStale), raw `fwd`/`rev` (no closed loop), `restart`.'}
2026-08-22 11:02:34,684 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 2, 'text': "**move2az, 8 bearings around the full circle.** Error is signed shortest arc, measured after a settle.\n\n| asked | settled | err | took |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 180 | 180 | +0.0 | 2.85 s |\n| 90 | — | **no done** | see step 12 |\n| 270 | 268 | −2.0 | 2.73 s |\n| 120 | 120 | +0.0 | 5.37 s |\n| 300 | 302 | +2.0 | 3.51 s |\n| 60 | 59 | −1.0 | 4.38 s |\n| 240 | 241 | +1.0 | 4.19 s |\n| 150 | 151 | +1.0 | 2.99 s |\n\n**n=7, median |err| 1.0°, max 2.0°** — inside v4's own 2.0° tolerance on every completed move, and the compass flutters ~1° at rest, so most of this is noise rather than error."}
2026-08-22 11:02:37,981 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 3, 'text': '**Zero misses ≥ 7° in 7 completed moves.**\n\nReported to `v4` with the caveat stated plainly rather than buried: **this is not evidence the fault is gone.** n=7 is a small sample for an intermittent fault, and the honest claim is only "it did not appear in this sample". Tens of moves across a session would be needed before saying anything about its rate.\n\nWorth revisiting: the one anomaly that DID appear (step 12) was a hang rather than a miss. Whether that is the same underlying fault wearing a different hat is unknown, and was explicitly not asserted to v4 — there is no evidence either way.'}
2026-08-22 11:02:51,513 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 12, 'text': '**OPEN — observed once, not reproduced, mechanism unknown.**\n\n`move2az 90` (from 180) emitted `{"evt":"started","cmd":"move2az","target":90}` and then **no `done` within 60 s**. The suite continued; the next move behaved normally.\n\nReproduction attempt — the identical leg, 180 → 90, six times:\n\n| run | result |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | OK 4.78 s |\n| 2 | OK 4.32 s |\n| 3 | OK 4.29 s |\n| 4 | OK 5.12 s |\n| 5 | OK 5.42 s |\n| 6 | OK 4.34 s |\n\n6/6 completed, `stall=False` throughout, uptime rising normally so no reboot. **One occurrence in fourteen attempts.**\n\n**Why it matters:** a caller blocking on `done` has nothing to fall back on. Unlike the hold defect there is no `busy` or `denied` frame — the command simply never reports finishing, and the caller waits out its whole timeout.\n\n**Honest limits, stated to v4 rather than buried:** OBSERVED that it happened, that it did not reproduce, and that the connection did not drop (so not a reboot at that moment). UNCONFIRMED — everything about the cause. Not speculated at them.\n\n**My harness was at fault too**, and that is fixed: only the verdict was recorded, not the frames, so the one occurrence could not be diagnosed after the fact. `_move_and_measure` now dumps every frame of a failed attempt plus `dir`/`stall`/`abs`/`uptime`. An intermittent fault you cannot reproduce is only ever as useful as the log you kept the first time.\n\nStays open until it recurs with a frame log, or until a longer sweep gives it a rate.'}
