2026-08-22 11:05:02,248 2435970 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 10, 'text': '**PARTIAL — arming verified, firing NOT yet verified.**\n\nWhat actually ran: `aimIn 3000 <target>` armed correctly — `aimArmed=True aimAz=326 aimInMs=2291`. That check passed.\n\nThe check for the aim *firing on its own* never recorded a verdict: the suite crashed at that line on a bug of mine (`started[0]` dereferenced when `started` was `None`, i.e. exactly when the aim had not fired within the 20 s window). Fixed in `s04_motion.py`, but the check has not been re-run under motion authority since.\n\nMarking the step complete would overstate it, so this note stands as the correction: **re-run `run.py v4 s04 --motion` to close it.** The earlier non-motion suites do verify that `aimIn` arms, reflects in status, is replaced by a later `aimIn`, and is cancelled by `brake` — it is only the fires-and-moves leg that is outstanding.'}
