2026-08-22 11:06:39,475 2471134 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': "Root cause is module/main.py:44 — uvicorn.Config without timeout_graceful_shutdown, which defaults to None, so uvicorn/server.py:277 awaits _wait_tasks_to_complete() forever and lifespan.shutdown() at :292 is never reached. Secondary: module/server.py had no try/finally around the yield, so an exception at :264/:271/:273 also skipped dm.stop_all(), and dm.stop_all()'s own 15.0s equalled the whole of TimeoutStopSec.\n\nFix: name three budgets derived from 89 stops in the journal (GRACEFUL_SHUTDOWN_S 3.0, TEARDOWN_STAGE_S 3.0, DEVICE_STOP_S 7.0, sum 13.0 < TimeoutStopSec 15), bound uvicorn's wait, collect the six pre-stop_all awaits into one bounded _stop_services(), and run the whole teardown in a finally. Prove with tests/check_shutdown_is_bounded.py — source-only, so it never needs a restart, which matters because a restart is what costs the radios. Spec: docs/modules/shutdown_budget.md. Register entry: the-shutdown-is-unbounded-so-a-stuck-task-costs-a-sigkill-with-the-radios-still-open.\n\nScope: core only. No plugin file is edited — plugin teardown is merely bounded from the call site."}
