2026-08-22 11:31:06,178 2471134 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': "A consumer reading data.packet off WS /events must not see an absence where the wire carried a zero, and must be able to filter by portnum without string-matching an enum name.\n\nMeasured live 2026-08-22 10:31Z over ws://127.0.0.1:8001/events?subscribe=packet, 4 packets: `channel` ABSENT on 4 of 4 (it is 0 on all of them, i.e. the public channel), decoded.portnum a str on 4 of 4 ('PRIVATE_APP', 'POSITION_APP'). On own frames hop_start/rx_rssi/rx_snr were also absent."}
2026-08-22 11:31:15,144 2471134 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'core/ble_device.py:2725 builds the event\'s data.packet with _proto_to_dict, i.e. MessageToDict(preserving_proto_field_name=True) and nothing else. protobuf 6.33.6 defaults always_print_fields_with_no_presence=False and use_integers_for_enums=False.\n\nCHECKED, NOT ASSUMED: none of channel, hop_start, hop_limit, rx_rssi, rx_snr, rx_time, id, from, to has proto presence (f.has_presence False for all). They are plain proto3 scalars, so the protobuf itself cannot distinguish "measured zero" from "never set" — MessageToDict is faithfully reproducing the wire format\'s own ambiguity. No rendering of data.packet can invent that distinction.\n\nSo the fix is narrow and the ambiguity is resolved elsewhere:\n - add _packet_to_dict() used ONLY at the packet-event site, with always_print_fields_with_no_presence=True and use_integers_for_enums=True. Zeros stop vanishing; portnum becomes the integer.\n - keep the enum NAME as decoded.portnum_name so consumers are not left blind by the type change.\n - do NOT touch _proto_to_dict itself. It also renders config sections, nodeinfo, channels and metadata; printing every default there would add dozens of zero fields to GET /{node}/config and break consumers for no gain.\n\nJUDGEMENT CALL TO FLAG: with defaults printed, a frame this radio generated itself will now carry rx_rssi 0 / rx_snr 0 / hop_start 0, which are structural zeros and not measurements. That is not made worse by this change (the proto has no presence either way) but it does become visible. data.frame remains the honest record — it uses `or None` and is absent entirely for own frames — and the docs must say plainly that data.frame is the field to trust and data.packet is the raw protobuf rendering.\n\nBREAKING for any consumer matching decoded.portnum == \'TEXT_MESSAGE_APP\'. Announce on bridge--mesh-gw, mesh-gw--node-dash, mesh-gw--services.'}
