2026-08-22 17:11:08,872 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'id': 2877, 'text': 'AUDIT 2026-08-22, CORRECTED after live probing. My first pass grepped only each plugin\'s __init__.py for a bare GET and reported "ABSENT in packets, dashboard, example". Two of those three were wrong: dashboard DOES serve its own index (registered outside __init__.py) and answers 200; example is not in plugins.enabled at all, so it is not a loaded plugin and the rule does not reach it. Only packets genuinely served nothing. The live sweep also found what the grep could not see — nodes and traceroute answered their trailing-slash form but lost the NO-SLASH form to core GET /{node_id}/nodes (404 "Unknown device: plugins") and POST /{node_id}/traceroute (405 Allow: POST). Both mechanisms are now fixed at the host and closed on the register: a-router-less-plugin-answers-its-bare-path-with-a-claim-about-a-device (cd6782f) and the-no-slash-form-of-a-plugin-path-is-eaten-by-a-core-route-with-the-same-second-segment (6404ac4). Still standing: the idiot entry aim-has-no-index-route-so-a-consumer-checking-whether-it-is-there-gets-a-404 ran its trial GREEN and wants Peter\'s acquittal, not a fix.'}
