2026-08-22 17:23:45,658 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'signal-quality-carries-its-antenna-and-its-geometry', 'title': 'GAP: a signal-quality answer must name the antenna, and for a directional one give actual vs target bearing'}
2026-08-22 17:23:48,869 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_set_area args={'name': 'signal-quality-carries-its-antenna-and-its-geometry', 'area': 'aim'}
2026-08-22 17:23:51,441 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'name': 'signal-quality-carries-its-antenna-and-its-geometry', 'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'PETER, 2026-08-22, VERBATIM:\n\n"my point is that when we show stats like that, there are affecting factors such as the aimed angle and the target node bearing."\n\n"so if I ask (or display on a dashboar) a devices signal quality, I would also like to know what antenna that was, and as I said if it was directional it\'s actual vs target position"\n\nA reading from a directional aerial is not a scalar. It is a scalar plus the geometry that produced it, and shown without that geometry it invites a wrong attribution — which has now happened twice.'}
2026-08-22 17:30:01,276 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_show args={'name': 'signal-quality-carries-its-antenna-and-its-geometry', 'titles_only': True}
2026-08-22 17:31:07,853 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'SHAPE: aim owns WHERE THE DISH WAS, durably, in its own persist namespace. utils/link joins a reading to it BY TIMESTAMP at read time. Nothing is stamped onto heard_by on the packet hot path.\n\nWHY NOT STAMP AT RECEPTION:\n- a plugin cannot reach another plugin\'s state, and nodes would need aim\'s live az per frame\n- it would hold the same fact in two places\n- a stamped field only ever helps frames arriving AFTER the change; a timestamped series can be joined to any reading whose time falls inside a covered interval\n\nTHE SEAM IS LEGITIMATE, not a state reach-in: core/persist.py collection() is one sqlite file with ONE TABLE PER NAMESPACE, so a second plugin opening the namespace read-only is the shared-store seam, not ctx.state access. One writer (aim), many readers.\n\nIT MUST STATE WHERE IT IS WRONG. aim is not the only thing that moves the mast while node-dash still drives it directly (open: rotator-logic-is-aim-only-yours-is-a-third-copy). So "az at time T" means "where aim last put it, and aim is not the only mover" until that is closed. Published as a caveat in the same shape utils/link already uses for excluded_from_direct — never as a bare number.\n\nSPEC BOUNDARIES, so each cycle stays in scope:\n  docs/modules/aim_plugin.md -> plugins/aim/__init__.py      (the durable record)\n  docs/modules/utils.md      -> plugins/utils/__init__.py    (the geometry fields)\n  docs/modules/traceroute.md -> plugins/traceroute/__init__.py (antenna selection)\n\nNOTHING BACKFILLS BEFORE THE FIRST ROW. Everything recorded up to now stays uninterpretable. Peter knows; do not re-raise it.'}
2026-08-22 17:31:11,274 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_retitle args={'number': 1, 'title': "VERIFY: red check — aim's pointing record dies with the process, so no reading can be joined to a dish position"}
2026-08-22 17:31:15,311 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG: aim writes a durable pointing record, and publishes where it is wrong'}
2026-08-22 17:31:16,008 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'TRACK: hashes, check_specs, commit, register verdict'}
