2026-08-22 17:41:34,927 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'airtime-cannot-say-when-it-started-counting', 'title': 'BUG: a 22s window and a 600s window look like the same kind of answer — airtime never says when its buffer started'}
2026-08-22 17:41:38,519 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_set_area args={'name': 'airtime-cannot-say-when-it-started-counting', 'area': 'airtime'}
2026-08-22 17:41:45,313 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'A caller must be able to tell "the mesh was quiet" from "I have only just started counting".\n\nRAISED BY bridge, 2026-08-22, VERBATIM: "say in the response itself when the buffer last reset. A window_covered_s of 600 and a window_covered_s of 22 currently look like the same kind of answer, and only one of them is. Something like buffer_started_at would let a caller tell \'the mesh was quiet\' from \'I have only just started counting\'."\n\nTHEIR MEASUREMENT, sampling OMNI !2687afb1 every 120s:\n  16:35Z  cov=600s  occ=4.02%  pkts=36  senders=20\n  16:37Z  cov=22s   occ=7.21%  pkts=2   senders=2\n  16:39Z  cov=142s  occ=2.12%  pkts=4   senders=4\n\nThe collapse at 16:37Z was MY restart of mesh-gw to verify an unrelated plugin-host fix, done mid-measurement without announcing it. Note the occupancy went UP to 7.21% on 2 packets — a short denominator makes a percentage that reads like a measurement.\n\nNEARLY FREE. AirtimeWindow._started already exists, is set on the FIRST packet rather than at construction, and is already what the covered-window denominator is computed from. It is simply never published. This is not new bookkeeping; it is publishing a field already relied on.\n\n`truncated: true` is already in those responses and does mean "the window asked for is not the window covered" — it is not as clear as a timestamp and is not a substitute.'}
2026-08-22 17:41:45,382 2595151 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_show args={}
2026-08-22 17:41:52,509 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Publish AirtimeWindow._started as `buffer_started_at`, and alongside it `buffer_age_s` so a caller does not have to do clock arithmetic against our clock to use it.\n\nSCOPE: docs/modules/airtime_endpoint.md governs core/airtime.py, core/app_router.py, module/server.py, module/models.py, cli/airtime.py, docs/API_REST.md — all in scope. The response model in module/models.py must carry the field or FastAPI will filter it out of the response, which is the trap that would make this look done and ship nothing.\n\nNOT IN THIS CYCLE: making the accumulator durable so airtime can be asked retrospectively. bridge asked for the honest label, not the durable store, and said so explicitly. The ring is in-memory, bounded at DEFAULT_CAPACITY=4000, and a restart empties it. That is a real piece of work and is registered separately rather than smuggled in here.'}
2026-08-22 17:41:53,441 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_file_attach args={'file_path': 'docs/modules/airtime_endpoint.md', 'kind': 'ref', 'label': 'governs core/airtime.py, module/models.py, module/server.py, docs/API_REST.md'}
