2026-08-22 18:50:50,973 2602540 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Three pre: gates listed in rak/v3/platformio.ini (check_wake_contract, check_verb_count_comment, check_rxms) carried `if __name__ == "__main__"` guards. SCons exec()s a pre: script, so __name__ is never "__main__" — all three were silent no-ops in every build since 39c6201, and two commit messages claimed otherwise. One of them (check_wake_contract) was additionally RED by hand against correct firmware, because it tested whether "handleCommand" sat on the SAME LINE as the rxid stamp and 47ad1db had reformatted that guard into a block.\n\nDONE when each of the three is shown to FAIL A BUILD when the rule it guards is broken. A print is not proof — the failure mode being fixed is exactly a check that runs, prints, and is ignored.'}
