2026-08-22 18:50:57,987 2602540 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': '1. Drop the __main__ guards; work at module level; `raise SystemExit(1)` on failure so a red gate FAILS the build rather than printing into a log. — landed c2f782f\n2. Port check_rxms\' brace-matched `body_of("if (handleCommand(rx))")` into check_wake_contract, replacing the line-based test. — landed c2f782f\n3. Prove each gate is REACHED: mutate a throwaway copy of the tree, point MT_SRC_ROOT at it, run `pio run` in the real rak/v3, and confirm the BUILD stops. The real tree is never broken. Restore, confirm green.\n\nHarness (all under scratchpad, never the repo):\n  cp -a rak/lib rak/transport rak/tools $S/device/rak/ ; cp -a rak/v3/src rak/v3/docs $S/device/rak/v3/\n  cp -a ../schema/frames.json $S/schema/          # check_rxms reads dirname(ROOT)/schema\n  cd rak/v3 && MT_SRC_ROOT=$S/device pio run'}
2026-08-22 18:51:10,811 2602540 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 3, 'text': 'PROVEN. Three separate `pio run` invocations in the real rak/v3, each with MT_SRC_ROOT pointed at a mutated copy. Every one FAILED THE BUILD, not merely printed:\n\n  check_wake_contract   `!mesh.txStarted()` -> `mesh.txOnAir()` in MtWake.cpp\n      FAIL announce phase 1 gates on txStarted()\n      wake contract BROKEN — 1 assertion(s)                    [FAILED] 0.67 s\n\n  check_verb_count_comment   re-inserted "// the 45-verb @command dispatcher" at MtCmd.h:2\n      FAIL lib/mt-cmd/src/MtCmd.h:2 claims 45 verb(s), dispatcher has 35\n      verb count comments BROKEN — 1 of 1 disagree                [FAILED] 0.66 s\n\n  check_rxms   `if (g_cmdRxSeen && mtWake.rxOpenMs())` -> `if (g_cmdRxSeen)` at main.cpp:2330\n      FAIL the obs append is guarded on seen AND rxOpenMs()\n      rxms contract BROKEN — 1 assertion(s)                       [FAILED] 0.71 s\n\nBaseline with the copy unmutated is green through all three, with every assertion named.\n\nTHREE THINGS FOUND WHILE PROVING IT, all inside quality-gates, none fixed here:\n\n1. check_verb_count_comment CHECKS ZERO COMMENTS in the real tree — "0 checked, all agree with\n   the derived 35". The offending count was deleted rather than corrected, so the gate now only\n   guards against reintroduction. That is a legitimate job but it is not what the spec claims it\n   is doing, and a gate with an empty input set is one rename away from being inert again.\n\n2. A MISTRIAL FAILS THE BUILD, and the code says it should not. check_verb_count_comment returns\n   2 with the comment "cannot decide: not evidence against anybody", and the module-level footer\n   is `if main() != 0: raise SystemExit(1)`. Failing loudly is defensible; disagreeing with its\n   own comment is not.\n\n3. check_v2_v3_sync.py IS A FOURTH DEAD CHECK — it still carries `if __name__ == \'__main__\'`, it\n   is in NO extra_scripts list, and its subject rak/v2/ is deleted in the working tree. Invoked\n   by nothing, about nothing.'}
