2026-08-22 18:52:11,744 2602540 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': 'SUPERSEDED, and the replacement is NOT the same thing, which matters for step 2.\n\n`docs/specs/AREAS.yaml` was git rm\'d on 2026-08-22 — it was a GENERATED specboard export, so new keys (class, depends, priority) had nowhere to be authored (raised with specboard, ACK, still open). The areas now live in mcpp: 17 of them, derived BY ACTION, each with a DONE-when clause on twelve of the seventeen.\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE NOBODY HAS PAID YET. The old ten were FILE-SCOPED, and step 2 proved "every source file under rak/ and esp32cam/ is claimed exactly once" against that scoping. The new seventeen are scoped by what the firmware DOES, not by where the code lives — main.cpp alone is touched by six of them. So:\n\n  * step 2\'s coverage proof holds for the ten and says nothing about the seventeen\n  * there is no file->area map any more, and nothing in mcpp can hold one (an area has\n    only name + description_md)\n  * ~16 files in this repo still reference the deleted AREAS.yaml\n  * docs/flow/areas.yaml is a FOURTH vocabulary and matches none of the seventeen names\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY OPEN, and it is Peter\'s: does the spec corpus follow the areas into mcpp, or stay on specboard under the old ten? Steps 4, 6 and 7 all sit behind that answer and cannot be worked until it is given. Recording it here rather than quietly rewriting the steps to whichever I happened to prefer.'}
