2026-08-22 19:06:15,322 2604716 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_area_new args={'items': [{'name': 'queue', 'description_md': '**product** — One command, and its four exits.\n\nAccept it or refuse it, spend it, and stop. Three of the four exits are success-shaped and one is not; telling them apart is the whole job. `src/bridge.js` — send(), fireOnHeard(), settleByAns(), correlation.\n\n**LIVE DEFECT:** at `maxQueued` 1 (`src/bridge.js:255`) an unsettled row refuses every new command to that unit. Three units blocked since 2026-08-22 12:04Z.'}, {'name': 'lifecycle', 'description_md': '**product** — A command\'s whole life, from one place.\n\nTHE STATE MACHINE NOBODY OWNS. Peter, 2026-08-19: *"there is no SSOT message lifecycle and there should be."* A consumer today joins queue/send/reply/orphan/giveup events plus GET /state plus frame.outcome.\n\n**KNOWN WRONG:** `/commands/lifecycle` publishes 10 states; the bridge emits 12 — `held` (`src/bridge.js:2338`) and `contradicted` (`:872`) are unpublished, and a command has been seen leaving `answered`, which is declared terminal.'}, {'name': 'wire', 'description_md': '**product** — Whether a frame\'s bytes can be trusted.\n\nDecode a positional frame, refuse one whose layout cannot be proven, decide what kind it is. `src/frames.js`, `src/classify.js`. A labels-only schema edit blinded the whole fleet for eight hours on 2026-08-18.\n\nTolerance is proven: 1281 foreign-hash frames decoded, zero "did not consume exactly" refusals. The exact-consumption check is `src/frames.js:184`.'}, {'name': 'contact', 'description_md': '**product** — Whether a unit is awake, overdue, or has returned.\n\n`src/devstate.js`, `src/schedule.js`. THE SSOT FOR WHEN A UNIT IS AWAKE — Peter, 2026-08-19: *"no independent determination of when the device is awake... NO EXCEPTIONS"*. Holds declared beat/window, measured beat, phase correction, overdue detector.\n\nTwo known defects: a Meshtastic telemetry frame counts as a beat, and a restart moves `link.heardAt` BACKWARDS, manufacturing a false overdue.'}, {'name': 'callers', 'description_md': '**product** — Who may command the units.\n\n`src/callers.js`, `src/api.js`. A request carrying an Origin header is a browser, and only pages served by this host may write. Absent Origin is curl and the CLI and passes.\n\nDefends against browsers ONLY — Origin is forged trivially by anything else, and there is no auth on this surface at all.'}, {'name': 'store', 'description_md': '**product** — What is kept, what is purged, and what is never purged.\n\n`src/db.js`. The one door to sqlite — no escape hatch, no raw SQL argument, and a test that fails if anything else imports the driver. Six command-response kinds are mode `keep` as a RULE.\n\n`witness` and `beat` have no retention policy at all (parked as park-derive-retention-per-table). Columns are `id, at, kind, subject, body`; `at` is INTEGER epoch-ms.'}, {'name': 'surface', 'description_md': '**product** — What the bridge publishes about itself.\n\n`src/surface.js`, `src/api.js`. The OpenAPI document, the x- extensions describing the far side of the radio, and the websocket feeds. 24 paths live.\n\nTrust it over any prose — but only since 2026-08-19, when it stopped declaring 200 for a route that returns 202. It is currently wrong about the lifecycle states (see **lifecycle**).'}, {'name': 'plugins', 'description_md': "**product** — What a plugin may and may not reach.\n\n`src/plugins.js`. The contract refuses `res`, the filesystem and any transport, so a plugin can never serve HTML or open a socket of its own. Loads from disk, namespaces routes, and refuses a plugin that would shadow a core route.\n\nTwo items open from the plugins repo: a live-loaded plugin logs a false REFUSED on rescan, and ctx cannot read a unit's live queue."}, {'name': 'aim', 'description_md': "**product — BEING EMPTIED, not improved.**\n\n`plugins/pointer`. SUPERSEDED 2026-08-21: Peter ruled all pointing goes through mesh-gw's aim plugin. The bridge serves no `aim` route; it lives on mesh-gw at `:8001/plugins/aim/{point,ledger,status,where}`.\n\nWhat remains ours afterwards is **when** to point — the wake prediction — which belongs to **health**. The rotator is SHARED HARDWARE with mt-radar: point, hold briefly, release, yield rather than queue."}, {'name': 'capture', 'description_md': '**product — NEEDED, NOT BUILT.**\n\nEverything the unit says is kept, whatever it is. A frame nobody recognises is still evidence: 56 real alarms were discarded as `unknown`, and 13 fields arriving free on every wake are decoded by nothing — cons, grst, n, rxms, and both telemetry frames including battery voltage.\n\nCapture is not handling. Storing an alarm costs a rule; acting on one is the product.'}, {'name': 'health', 'description_md': "**product — NEEDED, NOT BUILT.**\n\nThe twelve vital signs, judged against each unit's own normal. 5 of 12 decoded, none judged. Every threshold comes from the unit's own declarations — silence against its own `must`, stack against the 58% floor measured across 8,412 obs.\n\n**Link margin CANNOT come from SNR** — device measured 2026-08-22 that LoRa SNR saturates at the top end, so an SNR-derived margin is not physical. Spec: `docs/spec/the-fleet-has-vital-signs.md`"}, {'name': 'evidence', 'description_md': "**product — NEEDED, NOT BUILT.**\n\nThe picture of what happened, or why there isn't one. Zero camera frames of any kind have ever reached this bridge. cam, camu, grab, chunk, push, err and diag are seven frame families the device can send and `src/` names one of them.\n\nAn image that never arrived is exactly as invisible as one never taken, and the difference is the whole diagnosis."}, {'name': 'act', 'description_md': "**product — NEEDED, NOT BUILT, AND BLOCKED.**\n\nKeeping the unit alive without being asked. Lengthen a beat while there is still power to hear the command, re-anchor a drifting wake, hold intent across a six-hour sleep.\n\nBLOCKED on Peter's ruling — watch and tell, or watch and act unasked — because three vital signs have actions that spend the unit's own power budget."}, {'name': 'detect', 'description_md': '**product — NEEDED, NOT BUILT, AND DELIBERATELY LAST.**\n\nSomething happened, and Peter is told, and kept told. Peter, 2026-08-22: *"the alarm detection / handling / triggers would really be the final thing to be done."*\n\nTrigger rules written before the data can be seen are written against a guess, and a system that cries wolf is worse than one that is quiet. Built on the history that **capture** collects.'}, {'name': 'tools', 'description_md': "**tooling** — it builds, proves or reaches the product and never ships.\n\n`tools/reanchor.py`, `tools/anchors.yaml` — the only python in this repo. Re-derives every flow chart's `src: file:line` from a stable grep pattern, because a line number is invalidated by any edit above it and `flow_derive drift` cannot see that. 39 citations went stale three times in one day.\n\nAlso the repo's checks: `npm test` (the only one with a caller), `tools/reanchor.py --check` and `flow_prove` (invoked by nothing). No CI, no git hooks."}]}
