2026-08-22 19:10:00,123 2604716 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_area_new args={'items': [{'name': 'daemon', 'description_md': '**product · priority 8** — The process itself.\n\n`bin/bridged.js`. What is wired to what at boot, which transport a command takes, and the ports and defaults nothing else declares.\n\n`transport` defaults to `storeward` (`:254`) — every command is handed to mesh-gw at queue time and they own the waiting. `--transport own` is the way back and it is ONE RESTART; the own path is kept reachable, not deleted. Port 8790 is declared here and in no document.'}, {'name': 'tests', 'description_md': '**tooling · priority 15** — The suite that proves the product.\n\n`test/**`, 590 tests. The only check in this repo with a caller (`package.json` `scripts.test`). 587 pass, 3 committed RED on purpose in `test/round-trip-follows-a-storeward-command.test.js`.\n\n**COARSEST DECISION IN THE AREA LIST, and the first to revisit.** 99 files in one area, so "what is open in `wire`" will never include wire\'s own tests. Splitting per area is the obvious refinement; not done because a test filename does not reliably say which area it proves, and guessing would misfile silently.'}, {'name': 'harness', 'description_md': '**tooling · priority 16** — The instruments that ask the live fleet a question.\n\n`bin/round-trip.js`, `bin/verb-sweep.js`, `bin/wake-accuracy.js`. They reach the product; nothing they produce ships.\n\n**`round-trip.js` LIES on the storeward path** — it latches the packet id from our own `send` event (`:872`), which carries `id: null` because mesh-gw mints the id when it fires. Three committed-red tests encode it.\n\n**`verb-sweep.js` and `wake-accuracy.js` are LIVE on invocation — `--help` STARTS A SWEEP.** Assume any invocation puts frames on the air.'}]}
