2026-08-22 19:10:16,780 2604716 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_area_describe args={'name': 'wire', 'description': '**product · priority 2** — Whether a frame\'s bytes can be trusted.\n\n`src/frames.js`, `src/classify.js`, `src/handlers.js`. Decode a positional frame, refuse one whose layout cannot be proven, decide what kind it is, and decide what happens to a class nobody is consuming.\n\nA labels-only schema edit blinded the whole fleet for eight hours on 2026-08-18 — the hash moved though the wire layout did not.\n\nTolerance is now proven in production: **1281 foreign-hash frames decoded across four hashes, zero "did not consume exactly" refusals.** The exact-consumption check is `src/frames.js:184` and it is held against our own frames too.'}
2026-08-22 19:10:22,371 2604716 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_area_describe args={'name': 'surface', 'description': '**product · priority 5** — What the bridge publishes about itself.\n\n`src/api.js`, `src/surface.js`. The OpenAPI document, the x- extensions describing the far side of the radio, the HTTP routes and the websocket feeds. **24 paths live** — `curl -s localhost:8790/schema`.\n\nTrust it over any prose — but only since 2026-08-19, when it stopped declaring 200 for a route that returns 202.\n\n**IT IS WRONG RIGHT NOW** about the lifecycle machine: `/commands/lifecycle` publishes 10 states and the bridge emits 12. See **command**. The test that should catch it compares two hand-written lists, which is why it keeps recurring.'}
