2026-08-22 21:06:09,723 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_new args={'name': 'traceroute-live-capture-reads-the-wrong-path', 'title': 'BUG: on_event reads route_discovery from two paths core never writes, so no route is ever learned while running', 'area': 'traceroute', 'steps': ['VERIFY: red check — a live port-70 frame with a decoded RouteDiscovery is not stored', 'BUG: read it from where core writes it, and prove a reply lands', 'TRACK: hashes, check_specs, commit, register verdict', 'MEASURE: with capture working, get a real first hop for Sen1']}
2026-08-22 21:06:22,083 2586895 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'A traceroute reply that arrives while the gateway is running must be kept, so first_hop exists and the yagi can be pointed at the station that actually carries the traffic.\n\nFOUND BY EXPERIMENT, 2026-08-22. Peter: "Sen1. I want to target him. who do we know around him or in his direction, we can traceroute him and see if we can open a path". Seven traceroutes went out; one real reply came back and was discarded on arrival.\n\n!10596db0 (S2) answered at gw_rx_time 1787428294 with route_back=[3608510722] and snr_back=[-49,-2] — the first traceroute reply this gateway has ever captured. GET /plugins/traceroute/!10596db0 still answers "no route held".\n\ncore/state.py:231 is the ONLY place in the repo that parses RouteDiscovery, and writes it to\n    event["data"]["packet"]["decoded"]["route_discovery"]\nplugins/traceroute on_event reads\n    event["route_discovery"]  or  event["decoded"]["route_discovery"]\nNeither exists, so on_event returns early on every port-70 frame.\n\nTHE SILENCE LOOKED CLEAN, which is why it survived: failures=0, dropped_events=0, and the store is not empty — it holds 2 rows, both source=backfill from the startup read of the retained stream. Zero rows have source=observed. Nothing anywhere says "I have never learned anything live".\n\nTHE CONSEQUENCE IS THE POINTING. first_hop only ever exists on a route the plugin keeps, so /{node}/aim always falls back to `direct` — and for Sen1 it said so itself: "no traceroute is known, so direct is the only method with an input. If the path is in fact relayed this bearing is wrong". We knew from heard_by that Sen1 is 4 hops. We aimed on the method the plugin warned was wrong, because the data that would have corrected it was being thrown away.'}
