2026-08-23 09:53:21,464 2618727 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'One module owns door identity, and the broadcast address stops being published as a relay.\n\nPeter, 2026-08-23: "look all of these bits and pieces belong together, it should not have taken 30 mins to identify them" — then "go".\n\nThe time it took IS the defect, not a symptom of one. The set (observatory, inferences, snapshot-api, clusters, reach, doors, terrain, obs_* tables) has no name, no index and no boundary, so finding it means reading eight files and noticing three of them do the same thing.\n\nIncrement 1 only: establish src/reach.js as the entry point and move the one thing that is provably duplicated. Consolidating all five live modules at once would be a rewrite of code /events consumers depend on today.\n\nNamed and NOT done, so nobody reads this as finished: migrate clusters/terrain/frontier behind the same entry point; adopt the catalogue contract from inferences.js; revive obs_observation persistence; the table-level WS feed; drop mission-runner.js and the observatory UI on unarchive — actions are not part of this.'}
2026-08-23 09:53:30,974 2618727 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Spec: docs/modules/reach.md (attached, id 1483).\nRegister entry: broadcast-address-counted-as-a-door — GUILTY 1/1, then closed on a green prove.\n\n1. RED FIRST. tests/test_doors.mjs asserts the OUTPUT of doorUsage(), not the SQL — a\n   test that greps for a filter passes the day somebody writes a sixth query. Includes\n   the control that stops it passing for the wrong reason: not-empty when the window\n   holds completed traceroutes, since a filter removing everything would satisfy the\n   broadcast check and be useless.\n2. src/reach.js gains doorUsage({since}) and exports BROADCAST — the constant lives once,\n   in the module that owns door identity, not copied into each caller.\n3. snapshot-api.js distribution() calls it. newGround() is a first-APPEARANCE count, not a\n   usage ranking, so it cannot call doorUsage() — it takes the constant and states the rule.\n4. provenLinks() excludes it too. It has never actually leaked, only because place() needs\n   a nodes row with a position and 0xFFFFFFFF has none — an accident of the store, not a rule.\n5. check_snapshot.mjs restates the exclusion in its own SQL and deliberately does NOT import\n   BROADCAST: a check that imports the code it checks asserts only that the code equals itself.\n6. Register tests/test_doors.mjs in check_all.mjs — ledger B96, a check nothing invokes.\n\ndoors.js untouched: knownDoor/dominantDoor/relayDoor/doorAim answer AIMING, not usage, its\nchain filters already exclude the broadcast, and its one consumer is standing-tasks.js.\n/events message shape unchanged — distribution.doors keeps its fields, the broadcast row\njust disappears from it. Nothing unarchived.'}
