2026-08-23 09:56:06,204 2618727 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 5, 'text': 'TRACKED.\n\nRegister: broadcast-address-counted-as-a-door — GUILTY 1/1, then closed on a green prove.\n  .proofs/broadcast-address-counted-as-a-door.trial.txt  (red)\n  .proofs/broadcast-address-counted-as-a-door.fix.txt    (green)\n\nSpecs current — check_specs 18/18 including four rewritten, not merely rehashed:\n  reach.md          NEW, attached id 1483 — the five-implementation table, the\n                    scope of increment 1, and the five increments NOT done\n  snapshot-api.md   "Door identity is not this module\'s" — both call sites, and why\n                    newGround cannot call doorUsage\n  check-harness.md  "The two door SQL strings were wrong, and passing" — the harness\'s\n                    own failure mode: independent SQL is only independent if it is\n                    written from the REQUIREMENT, and both of these were written from\n                    the board\n  check-all.md      `doors` added to the inventory — and recorded that the table has\n                    drifted materially behind the runner (radio_admin, interval_tables,\n                    interval_options, no_channel_resolver, resolve, aim, traceroute_flow,\n                    transport_encoding, reply_snippet all registered and unlisted).\n                    Reconciling it is a task of its own, NOT attempted here — recorded\n                    rather than silently left, since a stale list is the exact failure\n                    that file exists to prevent.\n\nxsession #85 to mesh-gw: their defect 2 fixed, plus the finding they could not have seen\n— that the check agreed with the bug for 54 assertions across six windows. Flagged it to\nthem as a class of defect to look for in their own checks.\n\nSTILL OPEN, said plainly rather than left to be inferred:\n  - increments 2-6 of the consolidation (clusters/terrain/frontier behind the entry point,\n    the catalogue contract, obs_observation persistence, the table-level WS feed, dropping\n    mission-runner). Named in the spec.\n  - mesh-gw\'s other two: nodes.bearing = 25500990 across 8 non-null rows; rf_last_heard\n    vs signal_history (any-path vs direct-only) undocumented.\n  - mesh-gw owes #66 — is radio config core or plugin. Blocking the port.'}
