2026-08-23 11:44:08,368 2618377 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'Peter, 2026-08-12, quoted in the code that half-implemented it: "instead of silently refusing, we should instead transmit a overflow error packet... at least we would know that the device received the command but was unable to send it rather than silence."\n\nPeter, 2026-08-23, on finding it was not global: "it should be global on messages and be the final thing before being dispatched to the radio."\n\nreportOverflow() is called from ONE place — pb_encode failure. Five other refusals in buildAndQueue return false in silence, including both DM paths. Nothing checks size at enqueueFrame, the one funnel every frame passes through on its way to the radio.\n\nDONE when no message can fail to reach the air without both (a) a named counter moving and (b) a correlated err/overflow reply carrying the cap of the lane actually used — and when each of those has been FORCED on the bench rather than reasoned about.'}
2026-08-23 11:44:17,128 2618377 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'TWO GATES, and the split is forced by what each place still knows.\n\nbuildAndQueue is the REPLY gate — the last point holding portnum, len and requestId, so the only place a refusal can be ANSWERED in a way the caller can attribute. Every refusal reports here, with the cap of the lane actually used (JSON_CAP on the channel lane, TEXT_CAP_PKI on the PKC lane).\n\nenqueueFrame is the SIZE gate — the only funnel every frame passes, whatever built it (buildAndQueue :292, the ack retransmit :889, resend() :979). It holds bytes, not a message: no requestId, no portnum, so it can only refuse and count. Still the right place, because nothing can bypass it.\n\nstartSending() is NOT the gate despite being the transmit chokepoint: the frame is already built and encrypted, the message context is gone, and a failure first visible there is unanswerable. That is why _txDropped tells you nothing.\n\nOrder: enumerate (step 1) -> reply gate (step 2) -> size gate (step 3) -> force each on the bench (step 4).\n\nThis lands BEFORE the verb removal and the DM reintroduction, both of which Peter has also authorised, because :254 is the DM lane and it is silent.'}
2026-08-23 11:44:31,967 2618377 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 1, 'text': 'ENUMERATED. Every path by which a message can fail to reach the air, and what each records TODAY.\n\n  line  refusal                                              counter          reply\n  198   len > sizeof(meshtastic_Data_payload_t::bytes)        NONE             none\n  234   pb_encode failed (Data does not fit MAX_PAYLOAD)      _txOverflows     reportOverflow\n  254   !peer  — no PKI key held for the destination          NONE             none\n  254   plainLen + PKI_SCRATCH > MAX_PAYLOAD  (DM oversize)   NONE             none\n  259   pkiEncrypt failed                                     NONE             none\n  261   ctrCrypt failed                                       NONE             none\n  293   enqueueFrame false — queue full                       NONE             none\n  498   startTransmit failed                                  _txDropped,      none\n                                                              _txFailStreak\n  579   TX-done never arrived, frame abandoned                _txDropped,      none\n                                                              _txFailStreak\n  1003  drain gave up                                         _txDrainGiveUps  none\n\nSIX of the ten have NO COUNTER AT ALL. One of the ten replies.\n\nTHE ASYMMETRY IS THE FINDING, and it is stark against the same file\'s RX side:\n\n  RX has NINE named drop reasons, every one counted and published:\n    _rxDropCrc _rxDropLen _rxDropSelf _rxDropChan _rxDropAddr _rxDropPsk\n    _rxDropPb _rxDropDup _rxDroppedByTx\n\n  TX has five silent refusals and no way to distinguish them.\n\nSo we can say exactly why an arriving frame was rejected, and almost nothing about why a\ndeparting one never left. The RX side is the model to copy — named reason, counter,\naccessor — and the work is to bring TX up to it.\n\nPUBLISHED ACCESSORS TODAY: ackRetransmits, ackFailTotal, txFailStreak, txDropped,\ntxOverflows. _txDrainGiveUps has no accessor, so even the counter that exists is invisible.\n\nAND THE CAP IS WRONG ON THE LANE THAT MATTERS. reportOverflow hardcodes JSON_CAP (217).\nTEXT_CAP_PKI is JSON_CAP - 16 = 201 (MeshtasticTransport.h:524). A DM overflowing at 208\nwould report "was 208, cap 217" — which reads as FITS.\n\nNOTHING GATES SIZE AT THE FUNNEL. enqueueFrame (:328) does not look at len at all; it casts\nto uint16_t and hands it to _txq.enqueue. Its three callers are buildAndQueue :292, the ack\nretransmit :889, and resend() :979 — so it is the one place every frame passes, and the one\nplace with no size assertion.'}
