2026-08-23 11:50:13,899 2618377 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_notes_set args={'number': 2, 'text': 'DONE. Every refusal in buildAndQueue now reports, each with its own name and the cap of the lane actually used.\n\n  TXR_PAYLOAD_LEN  "payload"   len > Data.payload.bytes, before any encode  cap = Data.payload.bytes\n  TXR_ENCODE       "overflow"  pb_encode refused                            cap = JSON_CAP\n  TXR_NO_KEY       "nokey"     no public key held for the destination       cap = TEXT_CAP_PKI\n  TXR_PKI_SPACE    "pkispace"  plaintext + PKI_SCRATCH overruns the payload cap = TEXT_CAP_PKI\n  TXR_PKI_CRYPT    "pkicrypt"  pkiEncrypt refused                           cap = TEXT_CAP_PKI\n  TXR_CH_CRYPT     "chcrypt"   ctrCrypt refused                             cap = JSON_CAP\n\nFIVE DECISIONS WORTH RECORDING, because each could reasonably have gone the other way:\n\n1. "overflow" IS KEPT VERBATIM for TXR_ENCODE. It is the only reason that ever went on the air,\n   so a consumer may already match on it. Renaming it to something tidier would have been a\n   silent wire-format change to the one message this whole task exists to make reliable.\n\n2. THE `!peer || oversize` PAIR IS SPLIT. They were one `||` behind one silent return, so a DM\n   could fail for either and look identical. They are not the same fault and do not have the\n   same fix: no key is a key-exchange problem, oversize is a budget problem.\n\n3. _txOverflows++ MOVED INTO reportOverflow. It was at the call site, so the total could drift\n   from the per-reason counters and a new refusal site could forget it. One place now.\n\n4. COUNTING HAPPENS BEFORE THE _inOverflow GUARD. A refusal raised while reporting an earlier\n   refusal still happened; the guard drops its FRAME deliberately, but counting after it would\n   lose exactly the events that occur when the transport is in trouble.\n\n5. `if (!_radio)` STAYS A BARE RETURN, split out of the old combined test. There is nothing to\n   report a refusal ON, and the report would re-enter the same test.\n\nBUILD: SUCCESS, 5.80 s. RAM 25.5% (+24 B), Flash 39.9% (+672 B). All nine pre-build gates green.'}
