2026-08-23 11:51:33,635 2618727 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'goal', 'text': 'docs/modules/relay-observation.md said of the 2026-08-23 transport backfill:\n\n  "The mapping is bijective, so nothing is lost and the change is reversible."\n\nTrue of the VALUE, false of the PROVENANCE. I wrote it. CORRECTED 2026-08-23.\n\nFound by device, not by us, by applying our own enum warning back at us. We told them\nnever to store a peer\'s enum verbatim; they checked their tree, found it clean, and\nvolunteered a caveat about their own meshgw-tap.py — it writes our events verbatim ON\nPURPOSE, because a witness log that normalises has destroyed the evidence it exists to\nhold. That is the opposite requirement to this table\'s, which is the whole finding.\n\nMeasured:\n  TRANSPORT_INTERNAL  505754  2026-08-03 07:39:39 -> 2026-08-23 09:45:03\n  TRANSPORT_LORA      268824  2026-08-03 07:39:43 -> 2026-08-23 09:44:34\nTwo clean rows, continuous, NO SEAM. No column holds the raw wire value. The instant\nmesh-gw changed encoding is no longer answerable from the data.\n\nNOT un-backfilling. Six queries compare that column to string literals; consistency in\na working column is what they depend on. THE DEFECT WAS THE CLAIM, NOT THE CHANGE.\n\n  Never store a peer\'s enum verbatim in a table you QUERY.\n  Never rewrite it in a log you keep as EVIDENCE.\n  If you hold only one of those, you are missing the other.\n\nCORRECTION TO MY OWN FIRST VERSION OF THIS NOTE, which said "their tape is now the\nauthority on our own peer surface". TOO BROAD, and I checked rather than left it:\n\n  - the tap runs --only !987ab80f, so it witnesses ONE NODE, not mesh-gw\'s surface\n  - it writes into TMPFS (3.9G, the tape is 631 MB of it) — a reboot erases it\n  - it does cover 2026-08-22 17:06, running continuously since 2026-08-10\n\nSo neither side holds an unfiltered durable record. node-dash holds only the working\ntable; that gap is real, named, and NOT closed by this task