2026-08-23 11:51:43,324 2618727 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'plan', 'text': 'Doc-only. No source file changes, so check_specs stays green without a rehash — the\nhash is of src/relay-observation.js, which is untouched. Verified: "All specs current."\n\nSpec attached: docs/modules/relay-observation.md itself (id 1486) — it is both the\nsubject and the deliverable, which is the normal shape for a correction task.\n\n1. Measure the loss rather than assert it: PRAGMA table_xinfo for a raw-value column\n   (none), and the per-encoding ts ranges (continuous, no seam).\n2. Replace the "nothing is lost" sentence with the value/provenance split, the measured\n   ranges, and the reason the backfill still stands.\n3. Add a section stating the two-artefact rule and naming node-dash\'s gap as OPEN —\n   including both of my own errors, because they are the same error twice and the second\n   one happened AFTER device warned me about the first.\n4. Do NOT decide whether node-dash needs its own tape. That is step 3 of this task and\n   it is a real question with a cost.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE, deliberately:\n  - un-backfilling (six queries depend on the consistency)\n  - building a witness log\n  - anything in device\'s repo — their process, their tape, their call, and I only ever\n    read its command line and timestamps, never its contents'}
