2026-08-23 19:08:36,983 2696393 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'TIDY: remove the dead NodeInfo republish path, its unused constant, and the superseded pin accessor', 'description': 'Three symbols in plugins/pki/__init__.py had no caller, verified by exhaustive reference search across *.py, *.md, *.yaml, *.json and idiot.yaml:\n\n- `_republish_our_nodeinfo` :822 — superseded by `_ask_it_to_announce`\n- `NODEINFO_BROADCAST_S` :82 — assigned, never read\n- `pinned_key` :375 — superseded by `_pin_observation`\n\nNOT removed: `may_repair`. It is uncalled by the plugin but three checks call it, one asserts its existence and bounds its body, docs/PKI_PLUGIN.md documents it, and idiot.yaml cites it among the proven safety rails. Retained deliberately and recorded as such in the spec.\n\nNo register entry: a tidy is neither `bug` (behaviour wrong) nor `new` (behaviour absent), and it has no red to capture. Evidence is regression, not falsification — the nine pki checks green before and after, with a control proving the suite can see a removal that matters.\n\n851 → 810 lines.\n\nFOUND IN PASSING, registered, out of scope: `a-check-hardcodes-the-repo-path-so-it-tests-the-working-tree-even-when-run-from-a-copy`.'}
