2026-08-23 19:35:16,604 2696393 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': 'BUG: every log line reaches the journal at one priority, so colour and filtering are dead', 'description': 'Peter, 2026-08-23: "all logs in the journalctl are all the same colour and say only info and bug and none of them identify which module the log came from. impossible to track in the logs" and "logs need some way of differenctaiting log source and probably colours as well."\n\nMEASURED: python emitted 106 WARNING/ERROR records in one hour; `journalctl -u mesh-gw -p warning` returns 1. module/main.py:43 basicConfig writes plain text to stdout and systemd stamps the whole stream with one priority.\n\nThree defects in one format string:\n1. no syslog priority, so journalctl cannot colour or filter\n2. %(asctime)s duplicates the journal\'s own stamp, pushing the source 62 chars in\n3. uvicorn\'s access lines carry neither timestamp nor logger name\n\nFix without new dependencies: a Formatter that prepends the systemd `<N>` level prefix, drops asctime, and puts the logger name first in a fixed-width field; uvicorn\'s loggers pointed at the same handler.\n\nFirst of three, because the instrument and the state machine are both diagnosed THROUGH the logs.'}
