2026-08-24 12:06:02,184 2696393 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'title': "NEW: do the phone app's two-stage connect handshake instead of inventing a mid-session node fetch", 'description': 'ROOT CAUSE. core/ble_device.py:2883 picks ONE nonce at connect from sync_mode and treats that single want_config as the whole session establishment. All three choices are wrong against the reference: the app does not choose, it sends 69420 THEN 69421 as one handshake.\n\nMeshtastic-Android, HandshakeConstants.kt: "Stage 1 (CONFIG_NONCE 69420): requests device config, module config, and channels. Stage 2 (NODE_INFO_NONCE 69421): requests the full node database."\n\nMeshConfigFlowManagerImpl.handleConfigOnlyComplete, after Stage 1 completes:\n    delay(wantConfigDelay)                      // 100ms\n    heartbeatSender.sendHeartbeat("inter-stage")  // aborts if not sent\n    delay(wantConfigDelay)                      // 100ms\n    connectionManager.startNodeInfoOnly()       // want_config(69421)\nGuards: HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_STAGE1 = 30s, HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_STAGE2 = 60s.\n\nSo 69421 is Stage 2 of the CONNECT handshake, never a mid-session query. We stop at Stage 1, declare READY, then fire Stage 2 cold minutes later at a firmware whose handshake has finished — and the RAK4631 stops answering entirely.\n\nEverything built around that was scaffolding: fetch_nodes, the nodes-only probe, the full-dump fallback (which wedged the radio), and the liveness rescue that survives the wedge.\n\nBLAST RADIUS, measured in Phase 1:\n  plugins/nodes/__init__.py:296 is the ONLY production caller of fetch_nodes, inside\n  POST /plugins/nodes/radio/refresh — which docs/HANDOVER.md:116 calls "used constantly,\n  the only way to read a pinned key", and which tests/check_both_ends_hold_a_current_key.py\n  drives. Three test files bind fetch_nodes directly.\n\nDECISION: after the handshake the node table is already in _sync_nodes, so fetch_nodes\nreturns the cache and NEVER sends a want_config. The route keeps working, the wedge class\ndisappears, and no mid-session config request is ever sent again.'}
